INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (113, 2, 4, 'Atlas Orion Silver Edition 100mm T2 2X Anamorphic Prime (EF)', 'atlas-orion-silver-edition-100mm-t2-2x-anamorphic-prime-ef', 'The Atlas Orion Silver Edition 100mm T2 2x Anamorphic Prime (EF) is a premium EF-mount lens that provides a cinematic, 2x-squeeze image with fantastic bokeh and remarkable flare, all while minimizing breathing. Key features include:

Neutral flare characteristic and optimized tuning
For Super35 sensors providing up to 31mm coverage
2x anamorphic squeeze & fast T2.0 aperture
Better controlled lens flare with minimal breathing

What’s Changed? The Atlas Orion Silver Edition 100mm T2 2x Anamorphic Prime differs from the standard edition lenses in a couple of key areas. Flares take on the color of your light source, giving you more flexibility in getting the look you want. This is in contrast to the standard editions, which produce a blue-tinged flare. Additionally, Atlas has optimized the air spaces between the lens elements to provide a different focus fall-off. The standard edition lenses have the target optimized through-focus set for 50% fore and 50% aft, while the Silver Edition lenses have the through-focus optimized to land with best focus 25% into depth of the target focus, with a smooth 75% fall-off behind the target focus.

The Anamorphic Look. The Atlas Orion Anamorphic Prime Silver Edition lenses provide a clean, oval shaped bokeh you might expect out of more expensive anamorphics. The Orions produce a unique but well-controlled anamorphic lens flare. If you want that J.J. Abrams look, this lens will give it to you. Shining a light toward the lens in the frame will produce a wonderful flare that goes almost edge to edge depending on light strength. Unlike the standard edition of this lens, the Silver Edition has a neutral flare characteristic that assumes the color of your light source. The 100mm lens has significantly better flare control than the 40mm, which has the most wild look of the Atlas Orions.

Standardized Features. All the Orion Anamorphic lenses have the same front lens diameters, and focus and iris ring positions. This allows for super-fast lens changes just by swinging your matte box and dropping your follow focus without moving their positions. Markings in feet appear on both sides making it easy for ACs and focus-pullers to do their jobs. This lens has industry-prevalent 0.8 pitch gears a 114mm front diameter.

