Introducing CFexpress Media. This camera features dual CF express media slots. The form factor of this media is the same as XQD but features maximum write speeds around 1200 MB/s. For the C500 Mk II, that means internal 12-bit recording in Canon’s Cinema RAW Light codec at up to 59.94 fps. There is also an SD slot for recording XF-AVC 4:2:2 10-bit files or 8-bit XF-AVC proxies.', 13000000.0, '{"Brand": "Canon", "Camera Mount": "PL", "Camera Type": "Cinema", "Compatible Media": "CFexpress Type B and SD", "Imaging": "Sensor Type: CMOS Effective Pixels: 18.69 MP Maximum Resolution5952 × 3140 Bit Depth Raw: 10-bit/12-bit XF-AVC: 4:2:0 8-bit", "Inputs/Outputs": "Audio Inputs 2x XLR 3-pin  MIC (3.5mm mini-jack) Monaural mic Audio Output Headphone out (3.5mm mini-jack) Video Outputs 12G/HD-SDI (BNC) Monitor Out (BNC) HDMI (Type A) Additional Inputs/Outputs USB Remote (2.5mm sub-mini jack) Video terminal (Canon monitors) Remote", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Photo Resolution": "20.8 MP", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Monitoring": "LCD Panel 4.3” capacitive touchscreen", "Physical": "Dimensions (WxHxD) Camera Unit: 6.0 × 5.8 × 6.6 in. Weight Camera Unit: Approximately 3.8 lbs. Accessory Mounts: Tripod: ¼”-20 & ⅜”-16 threaded holes Additional: ¼”-20 threaded holes (camera bottom) (3x), ¼”-20 threaded holes (camera top) (8x)", "Power Supply": "InputDC IN 12V jack (DC 11.5V–20V) (4-pin XLR) Battery Type: BP-A30 (available separately)/BP-A60 (included)", "Recording": "MediaCFexpress (Cinema Raw Light/XF-AVC) (2x)SDXC (MP4/XF-AVC) (1x) Formats Video: RAW: Cinema RAW Light, XF-AVC: MPEG-4 AVC/H.264 Audio: Linear PCM (24 bit – 48kHz; 4-channel recording)", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Detachable", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Stabilization": "Yes"}', 'Includes

