INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (407, 1, 12, 'Canon EOS R50 V', 'canon-eos-r50-v', 'The Canon EOS R50 V is a compact, crop-format, RF-mount mirrorless camera with a feature set optimized for streamers, vloggers, and influencers. Key features include:

Sleek, brick-like body with vertical orientation mounting
24.2MP APS-C CMOS sensor, Dual Pixel CMOS AF II
Video-prioritized buttons and modes
UHD 4K60p cropped, 6K oversampled UHD 4K30p

What’s Changed. What’s Changed. The EOS R50 V introduces Canon’s EOS V-series, which is a line of compact cameras that prioritize mobile video. Despite the V designation, the EOS R50 V carries a very similar spec sheet to the R50. They both use the same APS-C sensor and AF system and both boast unlimited recording and 15 frames-per-second shooting speeds. Where the R50 V diverges from the prior model is in its build. Designed with user feedback in mind, Canon addressed the needs of content creators with video-focused elements such as a red tally light, a red “recording border” around the LCD, two recording buttons, vertical and horizontal tripod mounts, and a zoom lever for Power Zoom compatible lenses – all in a palm-sized form factor.

A Comprehensive Hybrid Solution. Equipped with some of the popular features of the Cinema EOS line, the EOS R50 V is versatile enough for pros while still being accessible to novices, whether it’s for social media, travel, streaming, or corporate work. The EOS R50 V sports Canon Log 3, HLG, PQ, 709 Recording, False Color, Zebras, and four-channel audio recording. For beginners, there are automatic movie presets including Close-up Demo (for e-commerce marketers), Smooth Skin, Movie IS (designed especially for vlogging), and Color Filter with 14 different grading options.

Complex Projects, Simplified Workflows. The aim of the EOS R50 V is wider accessibility of higher-end features presented in a simpler way. Want to explore slow motion effects? This camera placed the Slow and Fast mode right on the top dial for quick control of both the video frame rate and playback speed in-camera. Capture that cinematic look instantly with Cinema View mode, which creates a letterboxed 2.35:1 aspect ratio.

Versatile Connectivity. For both burgeoning and established streamers, this camera is equipped with 5 and 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and built-in wireless livestreaming. For livestreaming there are four options: over USB-C, with the Live Switcher app (for multi-cam setups), over micro-HDMI, or with the Camera Connect app (for remote control via smartphone). Access these options quickly with the dedicated “Live Stream” button. UVC/UAC compatibility means you can use this camera as a webcam to stream live video with the broadcasting software of your choice, directly through social media, or with video conferencing software like Zoom.

Lenses to Use with the EOS R50 V. This is an APS-C-format (crop-frame) sensor camera and it will pair with both full frame and crop-frame RF-mount lenses. It has a 1.6x crop factor (with some additional cropping in certain video modes). Popular crop-sensor lenses for compact hybrid cameras like the EOS R50 V include the Canon RF-S 10-18mm and the Canon RF-S 18-45mm, both of which are under 3" long and under a pound. They also each have a stepping motor for fast and smooth continuous autofocus performance when shooting video. For the official kit lens made specifically for the EOS R50 V, check out the Canon RF-S 14-30mm f/4-6.3 IS STM PZ, which is equipped with power zoom functionality and image stabilization. Complete your kit with a portable digital microphone with three pickup settings and the Canon PD-E2 for continuous power over USB-C.', 1100000.0, '{"Brand": "Canon", "Camera Mount": "Canon RF", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "SD", "General": "Accessory Mounts1x 1/4\\"-20 (bottom)1x 1/4\\"-20 (side)Battery TypeLP-E17Dimensions (W x H x D)4.6 × 3.4 × 2.7″FlashHot shoe onlyMfr. Model Number6895C002Monitor3\\" articulating touchscreenWeight11.4 oz.Wireless2.4/5 GHz Wi-FiBluetooth 4.2", "Imaging": "FocusPhase detection4503 points (photo), 3713 points (video)ISO100-32,800 (100-51,200 expanded)Max Resolution6K (6000 × 4000)Sensor24.2MP APS-C CMOSShooting SpeedUp to 15 fpsShutterElectronic rollingElectronic: 1/8,000 sec.-30 sec.Electronic: 1/4,000 sec-30 sec. (front curtain mode)StabilizationDigital only", "Inputs/Outputs": "Audio I/O1x 3.5mm headphone jack1x 3.5mm mic jackOther I/O1x USB-C (data, shared with power)Power I/OUSB-C (shared with data)1x LP-E17 battery portStorage I/O1x SD UHS-II slotVideo I/O1x Micro-HDMI", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Frame Rate": "120", "Maximum Photo Resolution": "24.2 MP", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Sensor Size": "APS-C", "Stabilization": "No", "Video Capture": "CompressionH.265/HEVCH.264/AVCFormat.MP4ResolutionUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) up to 59.94 fpsFHD 1080p (1920 × 1080) up to 120 fps", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "0.7 lb.", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

	Canon EOS R50V
	Body cap
