INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (436, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 10-20mm f/4 L IS STM', 'canon-rf-10-20mm-f-4-l-is-stm', 'The Canon RF 10-20mm f/4 L IS STM is a versatile, professional-grade ultra-wide zoom in Canon’s full-frame RF mount. Key features include:

Full-frame RF-mount zoom; advanced optical design
Great for landscape, nature, and architectural photography
Fast, accurate, silent autofocus; full-time manual focusing
Five stops of image stabilization; six stops with IBIS

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 10-20mm f/4 L IS STM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with Canon RF-mount cameras.

Versatile Ultra-Wide Zoom. This lens’s ultra-wide zoom length makes it great for a range of applications, including landscape, nature, architectural, and interior photography. Its nine-blade diaphragm gives your shots a pleasing bokeh quality. Its constant f/4 maximum aperture range isn’t useful for low-light shooting, so you’ll probably want to stick with outdoor lighting conditions for best results.

Advanced L-Series Optical Design. The 10-20mm’s twelve-group/sixteen-element rectilinear optical design includes one Super Ultra-Low Dispersion elements, three standard Low-Dispersion elements, and three aspherical elements, which combine to provide superlative edge-to-edge sharpness throughout the zoom range while minimizing chromatic aberration and distortion. Air Sphere and Subwavelength Coatings on the lens elements promote contrast and color accuracy while reducing flare and ghosting.

Stepping Autofocus Motor. This lens uses a ring-type Stepping Motor to provide fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for both still and video shooters. You also get full-time manual-focus override for precision adjustments. The minimum focusing is just under ten inches at all focal lengths, so you can get interesting ultra-wide close-ups.

Optical Image Stabilization. The RF 10-20mm f/4’s built-in image stabilizer compensates for five stops of camera shake, so that you can shoot in lower light at slower shutter speeds without worry. If you pair it with an EOS R-series camera that has In-Body Image Stabilization, you get up to six stops of camera shake.

Configurable Control Ring. This RF-mount lens features an integrated, configurable control ring that you can use to adjust a range of exposure settings, including ISO, aperture, and exposure compensation.

High-Quality Build. This lens boasts a weather-resistant build that protects against the elements so you can use it in adverse conditions. It accepts rear insert-type gelatin filters and includes a built-in petal-shaped hood. An FLC fluorine coating on the front element repels dust, water, grease, and other debris, making the lens easy to clean.', 2625000.0, '{"Angle of View": "130°-94° 25’", "Aperture Blades": "9", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.3 × 4.4″ (ø x L)", "Filter Style": "Gel Filter", "Filter Type": "Rear Mount", "Focal Length": "10-20", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "12/16", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "4", "Maximum Magnification": "0.12x", "Mfr. Model Number": "6182C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "9.8\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "1.3lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon RF 10-20mm f/4 L IS STM
	Hood
	Dust cap', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (437, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 100-300mm f/2.8 L IS USM', 'canon-rf-100-300mm-f-2-8-l-is-usm', 'The Canon RF 100-300mm f/2.8 L IS USM is a well-rounded high-speed telephoto zoom for full-frame Canon RF-mount cameras. Key features include:

Fast, versatile telephoto zoom; RF Extender compatible
Great for indoor-sports, theater, and fashion photography
Up to six stops of image stabilization with select cameras
Fast, accurate, and silent autofocus; internal-focus design

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 100-300mm f/2.8 L IS USM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with RF-mount cameras, but it doesn’t work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Fast, Versatile Telephoto Zoom. This lens’s versatile telephoto zoom range makes it perfect for portrait, fashion, indoor-sports, theater, and video applications. Its fast f/2.8 constant aperture and circular nine-blade diaphragm give you extensive depth-of-field control, let you work in available light, and help produce smooth, pleasing bokeh while keeping your subject sharp.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s 18-group/23-element optical formula includes 1 fluorite element, 1 aspherical element, and 4 Ultra-Low Dispersion elements to combat chromatic aberrations and color fringing throughout the zoom range while maximizing clarity, color fidelity, and sharpness. Canon has applied Air Sphere and Super Spectra coatings to each lens element to further minimize ghosting and flare, even in harsh light.

Fast, Ultra-Precise Autofocus. The Dual Nano Ultrasonic Motor (USM) autofocus system uses a combination of ring-type USM and stepping-motor (STM) mechanisms to provide fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for both still and video shooters. There are two separate, independently actuated focusing groups to give you even greater sustained sharpness throughout the zoom range, and you get an AF/MF switch for full-time manual-focus override. You can set the focus-range limiter to the full focusing range, from 5.9 feet to infinity, or from 19.7 feet to infinity for faster performance if you’re only working with distant subjects.

Additional Focusing Features. This lens’s internal focusing and zooming design means it maintains its overall length throughout the zoom and focus ranges, which makes for faster operation. A Focus Preset button allows for pre-focusing on a particular spot, storing its focus distance, and then instantly returning to that position. Four programmable L-Fn buttons let you control a host of lens and camera functions.

Optical Image Stabilization. The 100-300mm f/2.8 L’s built-in image stabilizer compensates for 5.5 stops of camera shake so that you can shoot hand-held, in lower light, and at slower shutter speeds without worry. When you pair this lens with newer EOS R bodies that themselves feature five-axis in-body image stabilization, you get up to 6 stops of shake correction.

L-Series Design. A customizable control ring lets you adjust a range of exposure settings, including aperture, ISO, flash control, white balance, and more. A built-in rotating tripod mount lets you use this lens on a tripod or monopod, and lets you quickly switch between portrait and landscape shooting orientations. A weather-sealed build keeps you shooting in inclement conditions, and a fluorine coating on the front lens element protects against moisture, fingerprints, and debris.

Extender Compatibility. The 100-300mm is compatible with the Canon RF Extender 1.4x and 2x, each of which will extend the lens’s effective reach.', 10275000.0, '{"Angle of View": "24°-8° 15’", "Aperture Blades": "9, rounded", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "5 × 12.7″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "112mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "100-300", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "18/23", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Telephoto, Supertelephoto, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "2.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.16x", "Mfr. Model Number": "6055C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "5.9’", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "5.7lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon 100-300mm f/2.8
	Canon ET-124 hood
	Lens case', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (438, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 100-400mm f/5.6-8 IS USM', 'canon-rf-100-400mm-f-5-6-8-is-usm', 'The Canon RF 100-400mm f/5.6-8 IS USM is a versatile, relatively portable telephoto zoom for Canon RF-mount mirrorless cameras. Key features include:

Versatile, relatively portable telephoto zoom
5.5 stops of optical image stabilization
Fast, quiet, and accurate autofocus system
Customizable control ring

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 100-400mm f/5.6-8 IS USM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with Canon RF-mount cameras but does not work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Versatile Zoom Range. This lens’s telephoto focal range makes it perfect for sports, wildlife, and travel photography. The f/5.6-8 aperture range isn’t great for low-light shooting, so you’ll probably want to stick with outdoor lighting conditions for best results.

Optical Image Stabilization. The built-in optical image stabilization system provides up to 5.5 stops of correction, allowing you to shoot in lower light and at lower shutter speeds without worry. When you use this lens with a camera that has an in-body image stabilizer, you get up to six stops of correction.

Nano USM Autofocus. This Nano USM autofocus system uses both a ring-type USM and an STM mechanism to ensure fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance. You also get full-time manual focusing when you’re working in one-shot AF mode.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s nine-group/twelve-element optical design includes one Ultra-Low Dispersion element and one aspherical element which combine to reduce aberrations, color fringing, and distortion for maximum clarity, color accuracy, sharpness, and rendering.

Although this rental will not include a hood, we do have the Canon ET-74B Hood available to add to your order!', 875000.0, '{"Angle of View": "24° to 6° 10’", "Aperture Blades": "9, Rounded", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "ø: 3.1 x L: 6.5\\"", "Filter Size": "67mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "100-400", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Telephoto, Supertelephoto, and For Mirrorless", "Macro Reproduction Ratio": "1:2.44", "Magnification": "0.41x", "Maximum Aperture": "f/5.6-8", "Mfr. Model Number": "#5050C002", "Minimum Aperture": "f/32 to 45", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "2.9’", "Optical Design": "12 Elements in 9 Groups", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "1.4 lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon 100-400mm f/5.6-8
	Front & rear caps
	67mm protective filter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (439, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 100-500mm f/4.5-7.1L IS USM', 'canon-rf-100-500mm-f-4-5-7-1l-is-usm', 'The Canon RF 100-500mm f/4.5-7.1L IS USM is a versatile, high-quality short- to super-telephoto zoom for Canon RF-mount mirrorless cameras. Key features include:

Versatile, portable short- to super-telephoto zoom
Five stops of optical image stabilization
Fast, quiet, and accurate autofocus system
Customizable control ring

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 100-500mm f/4.5-7.1L IS USM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with RF cameras, such as the EOS R5, EOS R6, EOS R, EOS Ra, and EOS RP. It does not work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Versatile Zoom Range. This lens’s focal length covers an impressive short- to super-tele focal range, making it perfect for sports shooting, wildlife photography, photojournalism, and aviation photography. The f/4.5-7.1 aperture range isn’t useful for low-light shooting, so you’ll probably want to stick with outdoor lighting conditions for best results.

Optical Image Stabilization. The built-in optical image stabilization system provides up to five stops of correction, allowing you to shoot in low light and at lower shutter speeds without worry. There are three stabilization modes, each of which suits a different purpose: a standard single-shot mode, a panning-optimized mode, and a mode that only activates the stabilizer during the exposure.

Dual Nano Autofocus. The Dual Nano autofocus system uses both a ring-type USM and an STM mechanism to ensure fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance. You also get full-time manual focusing when you’re working in one-shot AF mode.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s fourteen-group/twenty-element optical design includes six Ultra-Low Dispersion elements and one Super UD element which combine to reduce aberrations, color fringing, and distortion for maximum clarity, color accuracy, sharpness, and rendering.

Customizable Control Ring. You can configure the RF 100-500’s customizable control ring to adjust a variety of exposure settings, such as aperture, ISO, and exposure compensation.

High-Quality Build. This lens boasts a weather-resistant build that protects against the elements so you can use it in adverse conditions.

Teleconverter Compatible. The RF 100-500 is compatible with the Extender RF 1.4x and Extender RF 2x teleconverters, both of which are available as separate rental items. You can use these teleconverters in the lens’s 300-500mm range to extend its focal length.', 2675000.0, '{"Angle of View": "24°-5°", "Aperture Blades": "9, rounded", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.7 × 8.2″ (o x L)", "Filter Size": "77mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "100-500", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "14/20", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Telephoto, Supertelephoto, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "4.5-7.1", "Maximum Magnification": "0.33x", "Mfr. Model Number": "4112C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "2.95’", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "3lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon RF 100-500mm f/4.5-7.1
	ET-83F hood
	Tripod Ring
	Front & rear caps
	77mm Protection filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (440, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 100mm f/2.8L Macro IS USM', 'canon-rf-100mm-f-2-8l-macro-is-usm', 'The Canon RF 100mm f/2.8L Macro IS USM is a superior medium-telephoto macro prime designed exclusively for EOS-R series cameras. It’s ideal for macro shooting and portraiture, and it lets you adjust bokeh on the fly. Key features include:

Versatile medium-telephoto macro prime
Spherical Aberration Control Ring adjusts bokeh on the fly
Up to eight stops of image stabilization
Fast, accurate, and silent autofocus

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 100mm f/2.8L Macro IS USM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with RF-mount cameras, but it doesn’t work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Versatile Medium-Telephoto Macro Prime. This lens’s medium-telephoto length and 10.2-inch minimum focusing distance make it great for portraiture and macro photography. Its aperture is consistently bright throughout the zoom range, and its rounded nine-blade diaphragm gives you great depth-of-field control for selective focusing. On top of that, a Spherical Aberration Control Ring lets you alter the shape and character of foreground and background bokeh to create dreamlike images with a soft-focus look.

Redesigned Optics. This lens’s thirteen-group/seventeen-element optical formula was designed to minimize chromatic aberrations and color fringing while providing high clarity, color fidelity, and sharpness. Canon has applied a Super Spectra coating to the lens elements to further combat ghosting and flaring, even in harsh lighting.

Fast, Ultra-Precise Autofocus. The Dual Nano autofocus system uses both a ring-type USM and an STM mechanism to provide fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for both still and video shooters. You also get full-time manual-focus controlled by a customizable electronic focusing ring with three sensitivity levels, and a Focus Preset button to quickly recall a programmed focus position.

Optical Image Stabilization. The 100mm f/2.8L’s built-in image stabilizer compensates for five stops of camera shake, so that you can shoot in lower light at slower shutter speeds without worry. When you pair this lens with newer EOS R bodies that themselves feature five-axis in-body image stabilization, you get a staggering eight stops of shake correction.

Tripod Mount Available. If you’re looking for a tripod mount that works with the lens, we offer the Canon Tripod Mount for RF 100mm f/2.8L Macro IS as a separate rental item.', 1475000.0, '{"Angle of View": "24°", "Aperture Blades": "9", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.2 × 5.8″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "67.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "100-100", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "13/17", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Telephoto, Macro, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "2.8", "Maximum Magnification": "1.4x", "Mfr. Model Number": "4514C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "10.2\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "1.6 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Includes

