INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (449, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 20-50mm f/4 L IS USM PZ', 'canon-rf-20-50mm-f-4-l-is-usm-pz', 'The Canon RF 20-50mm f/4 L IS USM PZ expands on Canon’s hybrid telephoto lens series, sporting a redesigned style with internal focus and power zoom to produce consistent, professional photo and video results in a snap. Key features include:

Full-Frame sensor coverage
f/4 to f/22 aperture
Manual, lockable iris ring
Optical image stabilizer

New Product – Coming Soon.

Place your reservation now! We fill orders on a first-come, first-served basis. Please note that included items and rental cost could change as we finalize this listing.

If the listed rental price increases between your preorder and ship dates, don’t worry—you’ll be locked in at your original pre-order price. And if the price decreases, you’ll still pay the lower price. We’ll always contact you to confirm pricing before we ship your order.

Easy Breezy Focusing. The Canon RF 20-50mm f/4 L IS USM PZ sports an entirely redesigned look, and features like internal focus and power zoom make it an optimal pick for gimbal use. It features a focus drive system with two nano USM motors that promote smooth and steady autofocus capabilities.

Canon RF. This lens belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mounted, hybrid telephoto lenses. This lens is great for use with compact RF cameras, like the EOS R7, or a cinema camera, like the EOS R5 C. Please note that this lens is not designed for use with Canon EF-Mount cameras.

Fast-Aperture Telephoto Zoom. This lens’s focal length covers an impressive portrait to short-tele focal range, making it perfect for sports shooters and event photographers. The fast f/4 aperture and rounded nine-blade diaphragm offer shallow depth-of-field capability and enable shooting in difficult light.

Optical Image Stabilization. The built-in optical image stabilization system provides up to five stops of correction, allowing you to shoot in low light and at lower shutter speeds without worry. There are three stabilization modes, each of which suits a different purpose: a standard single-shot mode, a panning-optimized mode, and a mode that only activates the stabilizer during the exposure.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s eleven-group/thirteen-element optical design incorporates three Ultra-Low Dispersion element and two aspherical elements which combine to reduce aberrations, color fringing, and distortion for maximum clarity, color accuracy, sharpness, and rendering.', 2250000.0, '{"Angle of View": "94° to 46°", "Aperture Blades": "9", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.1 × 3.9″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "67mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "20-50", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "11/13", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Standard and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "4", "Maximum Magnification": "0.33x", "Mfr. Model Number": "7286C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "9.5\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "14.8 oz", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon RF 20-50mm f/4 L IS USM PZ', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (450, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 200-800mm f/6.3-9 IS USM', 'canon-rf-200-800mm-f-6-3-9-is-usm', 'The Canon RF 200-800mm f/6.3-9 IS USM is a versatile telephoto-to-super-telephoto zoom for Canon RF-mount mirrorless cameras. Key features include:

Versatile, telephoto-to-super-telephoto zoom
5.5 stops of optical image stabilization
Smooth, quiet, and accurate autofocus system
Customizable control ring and two L-Fn buttons

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 200-800mm f/6.3-9 IS USM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with Canon RF-mount cameras but does not work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Versatile 4x Zoom Range. This lens’s flexible telephoto-to-super-telephoto zoom range makes it perfect for sports, wildlife, nature, and travel photography. The f/6.3-9 aperture range isn’t great for low-light shooting, so you’ll probably want to stick with outdoor lighting conditions for best results.

Optical Image Stabilization. The built-in optical image stabilization system provides up to 5.5 stops of correction, allowing you to shoot hand-held, in less-than-ideal lighting, and at lower shutter speeds without worry. This lens supports Coordinated IS when you use it with a camera that has an in-body image stabilizer.

Nano Ultrasonic Motor Autofocus System. This Nano Ultrasonic Motor (USM) autofocus system uses both a ring-type USM to ensure smooth, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance that’s great for video and stills alike. It supports EOS R cameras’ Dual-Pixel CMOS autofocus systems, even when you’re using an extender, and it supports focus-breathing correction on cameras that offer that function.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s eleven-group/seventeen-element optical design includes three Ultra-Low Dispersion elements to reduce aberrations, color fringing, and distortion for maximum clarity, color accuracy, sharpness, and rendering.

Intuitive Controls and Durable Build. You can configure the RF 200-800’s customizable focus/control ring to adjust a variety of exposure settings, such as aperture, ISO, and exposure compensation. Two lens-function buttons on the lens barrel give you instant, precise control over your preferred camera settings. This lens boasts a dust- and weather-resistant construction that protects against the elements so you can use it in adverse conditions, while its white paint serves as a countermeasure to heat.

Teleconverter Compatible. The RF 200-800 is compatible with the Extender RF 1.4x and Extender RF 2x teleconverters, both of which are available as separate rental items.', 2725000.0, '{"Angle of View": "12°-3° 5’", "Aperture": "9", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "4 × 12.4″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "95mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "200-800", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "11/17", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Supertelephoto and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "6.3-9", "Maximum Magnification": "0.25x", "Mfr. Model Number": "6263C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "2.6’", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "4.5lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon RF 200-800mm f/6.3-9 IS USM
	Canon ET-101 hood
	Front & rear caps
	Hoya EVO 95mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (451, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 20mm f/1.4 L VCM', 'canon-rf-20mm-f-1-4-l-vcm', 'The Canon RF 20mm f/1.4 L VCM is an RF-mount, full-frame, ultrawide prime equipped with L-series optics for photo/video hybrid shooters. Key features include:

Fast, quiet floating autofocusing system
Linear focus motor for easy manual control
De-clickable aperture ring, rear gel filter holder
Custom control ring, function button

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 20mm f/1.4 L VCM belongs to Canon’s advanced EOS R line, which offers a wide-diameter mount that allows RF lenses to sit close to an EOS R sensor for reduced aberrations, increased sharpness, and better light-gathering abilities. Extra pins inside this camera line’s mount produces fast communication between camera and lens, which benefits rapid and efficient autofocus.

Optimized for Hybrid Shooting. Designed with both photographers and videographers in mind, the RF 20mm offers responsive AF, minimal focus breathing, and customizable handling. A manual aperture ring is de-clickable for smooth and silent iris pulls, while the linear focus motor allows for intuitive manual focus control. For autofocus, this lens uses a floating focusing system consisting of a Nano Ultrasonic Motor and a Voice Coil Motor to produce the right mix of speed and quiet performance.

Ultrawide Lens with Wide Feature Set. Despite having such a large max aperture and large RF mount, this lens is extremely portable and consistent with Canon’s other RF-mount hybrid lenses. It is just shy of 4" long and weights barely over a pound. It will accept both 67mm front filters and pre-cut gel filters via the rear filter holder.

Configurable Control Ring. Take exposure control into your hands, literally, with the Canon RF 20mm f/1.4’s on-barrel control ring. This click-stopped ring can be customized to a setting of your choice: shutter speed, aperture, ISO, and exposure compensation. This can be changed in the Custom Functions menu of an EOS R-series camera. This is a great feature for settings you access most frequently. To assign additional controls, there is also a mappable function button.

Try it with These RF-Mount Cameras. The portable nature of this lens makes it a great option for shooters on the go and pairs well with slightly more compact cameras like the Canon EOS R8 and the Canon EOS RP. However, this full-frame lens can be used with any EOS R-series, RF-mount camera. On a cropped-sensor (APS-C) EOS R camera, the Canon RF 20mm f/1.4 L VCM produces an effective focal length of approximately 32mm.', 2075000.0, '{"Angle of View": "94º", "Aperture Blades": "11, rounded", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3 × 3.9\\" (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "67mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "20-20", "Focus Type": "Autofocus and Manual Focus", "Groups/Elements": "11/15", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "1.4", "Maximum Magnification": "0.19x", "Mfr. Model Number": "7023C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "7.9\\"", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "1.1lb", "Zoom Type": "Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon RF 20mm f/1.4 L VCM
	Front & rear caps
	Canon EW-73H hood
	67mm Hoya EVO antistatic filter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (452, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 24-105 f/2.8L Power Zoom w/ 20-Pin Control Port Kit', 'canon-rf-24-105-f-2-8l-power-zoom-w-20-pin-control-port-kit', 'The Canon RF 24-105 f/2.8L Power Zoom w/ 20-Pin Control Port Kit combines Canon’s 24-105 f/2.8L lens & PZ-E2B Adapter for smooth zoom control. Key features include:

Controller operation via 20-pin port
Adapter easily attaches/detaches
5.5 stops of optical image stabilization
Fast, quiet, and accurate Nano USM autofocus system

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 24-105mm f/2.8L IS USM Z belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with Canon RF-mount cameras. but does not work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Fast, Versatile Midrange Zoom. This lens’s standard zoom range and fast, constant f/2.8 aperture makes it perfect for portraiture, wedding and event photography, photojournalism, video applications, studio sessions, and low-light shoots. Using an APS-C camera? You’ll get an approximate 38.4-168mm focal length.

Optical Image Stabilization. The built-in optical image stabilization system provides up to 5.5 stops of correction, allowing you to shoot hand-held, in lower light, and at lower shutter speeds without worry. When you use this lens with a compatible camera’s in-body Coordinated Image Stabilization system, you’ll get eight stops of correction.

Nano USM Autofocus. This autofocus system uses dual Nano USM motors to ensure fast, accurate, and nearly silent performance that’s great for photo and video applications. You also get full-time manual focusing, and an eleven-blade aperture that helps produce pleasing bokeh.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s 18-group/23-element optical design includes 4 Ultra-Low Dispersion elements and 3 aspherical elements which combine to reduce chromatic and spherical aberrations, color fringing, and distortion for maximum clarity, color accuracy, sharpness, and rendering. Super Spectra and Air Sphere coatings on the lens elements help minimize ghosting and flare.

Multiple Control Rings. The 24-105 is the first Canon RF-mount lens to include a stepless aperture ring, which lets you adjust exposure and background blur when capturing video with compatible cameras. Its smooth action is akin to what you’d find in a cine lens. The focus ring has soft click-stops to let you track focus adjustment, while the manual-focus ring lets you fine-tune your image.

High-Quality Build. This lens boasts a weather-resistant build that protects against the elements so you can use it in adverse conditions. Canon has applied a fluorine coating to the front element that keeps debris, water, oil, and fingerprints from sticking. Focusing and zooming are handled internally, which keeps the lens barrel from moving during those functions.

Precise Zoom Control. The Canon PZ-E2B 20 Pin Power Zoom Adapter is designed specifically for the included Canon RF 24-105mm f/2.8L IS USM Z lens and provides precision zoom control. To adjust the zoom speed, there is a small dial (labeled Z.S for Zoom Speed) located near the bottom of the adapter.

Power Talk. The adapter sources power directly through contacts on the lens, but can also be fueled with the separately available PD-E1 USB Power Adapter through the USB-C port.

Compatibility Corner. Thanks to the 20-pin port, this zoom adapter is compatible with a wide variety of Canon cinema and broadcast lens accessories, like a servo grip, zoom demand, or focus demand!', 5525000.0, '{"Angle of View": "84°-23° 20’", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "Lens: 3.5 × 7.8″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "82mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "24-105", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "18/23", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Standard, Kit, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "2.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.29x", "Mfr. Model Number": "6347C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "17.7\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "Lens: 2.9lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

Canon RF 24-105mm f/2.8L IS USM Z
Canon PZ-E2B 20 Pin Power Zoom Adapter



See Details', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (453, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 24-105mm f/2.8L IS USM Z', 'canon-rf-24-105mm-f-2-8l-is-usm-z', 'The Canon RF 24-105mm f/2.8L IS USM Z is a fast, versatile midrange zoom for Canon RF-mount mirrorless cameras. Key features include:

Great for portraiture, events, photojournalism, and video
5.5 stops of optical image stabilization
Fast, quiet, and accurate Nano USM autofocus system
Sharp, color-accurate rendering; weather-sealed build

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 24-105mm f/2.8L IS USM Z belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with Canon RF-mount cameras. but does not work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Fast, Versatile Midrange Zoom. This lens’s standard zoom range and fast, constant f/2.8 aperture makes it perfect for portraiture, wedding and event photography, photojournalism, video applications, studio sessions, and low-light shoots. Using an APS-C camera? You’ll get an approximate 38.4-168mm focal length.

Optical Image Stabilization. The built-in optical image stabilization system provides up to 5.5 stops of correction, allowing you to shoot hand-held, in lower light, and at lower shutter speeds without worry. When you use this lens with a compatible camera’s in-body Coordinated Image Stabilization system, you’ll get eight stops of correction.

Nano USM Autofocus. This autofocus system uses dual Nano USM motors to ensure fast, accurate, and nearly silent performance that’s great for photo and video applications. You also get full-time manual focusing, and an eleven-blade aperture that helps produce pleasing bokeh.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s 18-group/23-element optical design includes 4 Ultra-Low Dispersion elements and 3 aspherical elements which combine to reduce chromatic and spherical aberrations, color fringing, and distortion for maximum clarity, color accuracy, sharpness, and rendering. Super Spectra and Air Sphere coatings on the lens elements help minimize ghosting and flare.

Multiple Control Rings. The 24-105 is the first Canon RF-mount lens to include a stepless aperture ring, which lets you adjust exposure and background blur when capturing video with compatible cameras. Its smooth action is akin to what you’d find in a cine lens. The focus ring has soft click-stops to let you track focus adjustment, while the manual-focus ring lets you fine-tune your image.

High-Quality Build. This lens boasts a weather-resistant build that protects against the elements so you can use it in adverse conditions. Canon has applied a fluorine coating to the front element that keeps debris, water, oil, and fingerprints from sticking. Focusing and zooming are handled internally, which keeps the lens barrel from moving during those functions.

Power Zoom Available. Looking for some power zoom options? We have the Canon PZ-E2B 20 Pin Power Zoom Adapter and Canon PZ-E2 Power Zoom Adapter available separately! If you’d like to bundled this lens with either zoom adapter, check out the Canon RF 24-105 f/2.8L Power Zoom w/ 20-Pin Control Port Kit and Canon RF 24-105 f/2.8L IS USM Z Power Zoom Adapter Kit.', 3550000.0, '{"Angle of View": "84°-23° 20’", "Aperture Blades": "11", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.5 × 7.8″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "82mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "24-105", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "18/23", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle, Wide Angle, Standard, Telephoto, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "2.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.29x", "Mfr. Model Number": "6347C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "17.7\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "2.9lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon RF 24-105mm f/2.8L IS USM Z
	Canon EW-88E hood
	Canon RF 24-105mm f/2.8 tripod foot
	Hoya 82mm EVO antistatic filter
	Canon LZ1326 lens case', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (454, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 24-105mm f/4-7.1 IS STM', 'canon-rf-24-105mm-f-4-7-1-is-stm', 'The Canon RF 24-105mm f/4-7.1 IS STM is a versatile, professional-grade midrange zoom in Canon’s full-frame RF mount. Key features include:

Full-frame RF-mount lens
Center Macro Focus; 1:2 magnification
Fast, accurate, silent autofocus; full-time manual focusing
Five stops of image stabilization

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 24-105mm f/4-7.1 IS STM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with RF cameras, such as the EOS R, EOS Ra, EOS RP, and EOS R5.

Versatile Midrange Zoom. This lens’s wide-angle to telephoto-zoom length and variable aperture make it great for a range of applications, including vacation photography and general “walking-around” photography. Its rounded seven-blade diaphragm gives your shots a pleasing bokeh quality.

Center Macro Focus. The RF 24-105mm’s specialized Center Macro Focus setting lets you work with its 5.2-inch minimum focusing distance and 1:2 maximum magnification to really get in close with your subject.

Built-In Autofocus. This lens uses a ring-type Stepping Motor to provide fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for both still and video shooters. You also get full-time manual-focus override for precision adjustments.

Optical Image Stabilization. The RF 24-105mm  f/4-7.1’s built-in image stabilizer compensates for five stops of camera shake, so that you can shoot in lower light at slower shutter speeds without worry.

Configurable Control Ring. This RF-mount lens features an integrated, configurable control ring that you can use to adjust a range of exposure settings, including ISO, aperture, and exposure compensation.

High-Quality Build. This lens boasts a weather-resistant build that protects against the elements so you can use it in adverse conditions.', 750000.0, '{"Angle of View": "84-23°20’", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.02 × 3.5″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "67mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "24-105", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "11/13", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Telephoto, For Mirrorless, and Macro", "Maximum Aperture": "4-7.1", "Maximum Magnification": "0.5x", "Mfr. Model Number": "4111C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "5.16\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon RF 24-105mm f/4-7.1 IS STM
	Front & rear caps
	67mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (455, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 24-105mm f/4L IS', 'canon-rf-24-105mm-f-4l-is', 'The Canon RF 24-105mm f/4L IS is a versatile, professional-grade midrange zoom in Canon’s full-frame RF mount. Key features include:

Full-frame RF-mount lens
Versatile wide-angle to telephoto zoom
Fast, accurate, silent autofocus; full-time manual focusing
Five stops of image stabilization

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 24-105mm f/4L IS belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with Canon RF cameras. It does not work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Versatile Midrange Zoom. This lens’s wide-angle to telephoto-zoom length makes it great for a range of applications, including vacation photography and general “walking-around” photography, while its 1.5-foot minimum focusing distance is quite nice for close-up work. Its constant f/4 aperture provides consistent performance throughout the zoom range, and its rounded nine-blade diaphragm gives you great depth-of-field control for selective focusing.

Advanced Optics. This lens’s fourteen-group/eighteen-element optical formula includes “F” Low Dispersion and Super Low Dispersion elements that minimize chromatic aberrations and color fringing while providing high clarity, color fidelity, and sharpness. Canon has applied a Super Spectra coating to the lens elements to further combat ghosting and flaring, even in harsh lighting.

Ultrasonic Focusing Motor. This lens uses a ring-type Ultrasonic Motor and an STM mechanism to provide fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for both still and video shooters. You also get full-time manual-focus override for precision adjustments when working in one-shot autofocus mode.

Optical Image Stabilization. The RF 24-105mm f/4L’s built-in image stabilizer compensates for five stops of camera shake, so that you can shoot in lower light at slower shutter speeds without worry.

Configurable Control Ring. This RF mount L-series lens features a new integrated, configurable control ring that you can use to adjust a range of exposure settings, including ISO, aperture, and exposure compensation.

High-Quality Build. This lens boasts a weather-resistant build that protects against the elements so you can use it in adverse conditions.', 1550000.0, '{"Angle of View": "84°-23° 20’", "Aperture Blades": "9, Rounded", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.29 × 4.22″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "77mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "24-105", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "14/18", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle, Wide Angle, Standard, Telephoto, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "4", "Maximum Magnification": "0.24x", "Mfr. Model Number": "2963C002", "Minimum Aperture": "22", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "1.54lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon RF 24-105mm f/4L IS
	Canon EW-83N hood
	Front & rear caps
	77mm protective filter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (456, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 24-240mm f/4-6.3 IS', 'canon-rf-24-240mm-f-4-6-3-is', 'The Canon RF 24-240mm f/4-6.3 IS is a high-quality all-in-one zoom for Canon RF-mount mirrorless cameras. Key features include:

Versatile wide to telephoto zoom range
Five stops of optical image stabilization
Fast, quiet, accurate autofocus; full-time manual focusing
Customizable control ring

Wide to Super-Telephoto Zoom Range. The Canon RF 24-240mm f/4-6.3 IS’s focal length covers an impressive wide to telephoto focal range, making it a fantastic all-purpose zoom for the Canon RF mount.

Optical Image Stabilization. The built-in optical image stabilization system provides up to five stops of correction, allowing you to shoot in low light and at lower shutter speeds if needed. A more active Dynamic Image Stabilization option is great for capturing video, especially when walking or moving, and is particularly useful at the wide end of the zoom range.

UltraSonic Autofocus Motor. The Nano USM system uses both a ring-type USM and an STM mechanism to ensure fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance. Since this lens uses an internal focusing system, it works great with filters.

Customizable Control Ring. You can configure the RF 24-240’s customizable control ring to adjust a variety of exposure settings, such as aperture, ISO, and exposure compensation.', 1325000.0, '{"Angle of View": "74°- 8° 35′", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.2 × 4.8″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "72mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "24-240", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups": "15/21", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle, Wide Angle, Standard, Telephoto, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "4-6.3", "Maximum Magnification": "0.26x", "Mfr. Model Number": "3684C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "1.64’", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "1.65lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon 24-240mm f/4-6.3
	Front & rear caps
	72mm protective filter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (457, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 24-50mm f/4.5-6.3 IS STM', 'canon-rf-24-50mm-f-4-5-6-3-is-stm', 'The Canon RF 24-50mm f/4.5-6.3 IS STM is a versatile, budget-friendly wide-to-normal-length zoom for full-frame Canon RF-mount cameras. Key features include:

Full-frame RF-mount lens
Versatile wide-angle to normal-length zoom
Fast, accurate, silent autofocus; full-time manual focus
4.5 stops of image stabilization; 7 stops with IBIS

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 24-50mm f/4.5-6.3 IS STM belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with Canon RF cameras. It does not work with Canon EF-mount cameras.

Wide-to-Normal Zoom. This lens’s versatile wide-angle to normal-length zoom range makes it ideal for landscapes, cityscapes, street scenes, portraiture, and product photography, among other applications. Its variable f/4.5-6.3 aperture isn’t going to give you much flexibility in very low light, so it’s probably not the best for night shoots. Using an APS-C camera? You’ll get a 38-80mm equivalent focal length.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s eight-group/eight-element optical formula includes two aspherical elements that work to minimize chromatic aberrations and color fringing while providing high clarity, color fidelity, and sharpness. Canon has applied a Super Spectra coating to the lens elements to further combat ghosting and flaring, even in harsh lighting.

Built-In Autofocus. This lens uses a screw-type Stepping Motor to provide fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for both still and video shooters. You also get full-time manual-focus override for precision adjustments. This lens lets you work with a 0.11x maximum magnification ratio and a 11.8-inch minimum focusing distance so you can get reasonably close to your subjects.

Optical Image Stabilization. The 24-50mm f/4.5-6.3’s built-in image stabilizer compensates for 4.5 stops of camera shake on its own, or 7 stops if you’re using an EOS R-series camera with an In-Body Image Stabilizer (IBIS), so that you can shoot in lower light and at slower shutter speeds without worry.

Configurable Control Ring. This RF mount lens features a new integrated, configurable control ring that you can use to adjust a range of exposure settings, including ISO, aperture, and exposure compensation.', 550000.0, '{"Angle of View": "84°", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "2.7 × 3.7″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "58mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "24-50", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "8/8", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle, Wide Angle, Standard, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "4.5-6.3", "Maximum Magnification": "0.11x", "Mfr. Model Number": "5823C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "11.8\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "7.4oz", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Canon 24-50mm f/4.5-6.3
	E-58 II lens cap
	Dust cap
	Hoya EVO 58mm antistatic protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (458, 2, 12, 'Canon RF 24-70mm f/2.8L IS', 'canon-rf-24-70mm-f-2-8l-is', 'The Canon RF 24-70mm f/2.8L IS is a versatile, professional-grade, wide-angle to portrait-length zoom in Canon’s full-frame RF mount. Key features include:

Full-frame RF-mount lens
Versatile wide-angle to portrait-length zoom
Five-stop optical image stabilization
Fast, accurate, silent autofocus; full-time manual focusing

Canon RF Mount. The Canon RF 24-70mm f/2.8L IS belongs to Canon’s line of RF-mount lenses. It’s compatible with RF cameras, such as the EOS R and EOS RP.

Versatile Wide to Portrait Zoom. This lens’s wide-angle to portrait-length zoom length makes it great for a range of applications, including portrait and event photography, while its 8.3-inch minimum focusing distance is quite nice for close-up work. The fast f/2.8 aperture and rounded nine-blade diaphragm offer shallow depth-of-field capability and enable shooting in difficult light.

Advanced Optics. This lens’s 15-group/21-element optical formula includes 3 Ultra-Low Dispersion elements and 3 aspherical elements that minimize chromatic aberrations and color fringing while providing high clarity, color fidelity, and sharpness. Canon has applied an Air Sphere Coating to the lens elements to combat flare and ghosting.

Optical Image Stabilization. The RF 24-70mm f/2.8L IS’s built-in image stabilizer compensates for five stops of camera shake, so that you can shoot in lower light at slower shutter speeds without worry.

Nano USM Autofocus System. This lens uses a ring-type Ultrasonic Motor and an STM mechanism to provide fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for both still and video shooters. You also get full-time manual-focus override for precision adjustments when working in one-shot autofocus mode.

Configurable Control Ring. This L-series lens features a new integrated, configurable control ring that you can use to adjust a range of exposure settings, including ISO, aperture, and exposure compensation.

High-Quality Build. This lens boasts a weather-resistant build that protects against the elements so you can use it in adverse conditions.', 2350000.0, '{"Angle of View": "84-34°", "Aperture Blades": "9, rounded", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.48 × 4.95″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "82mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "24-70", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "15/21", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Standard, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "2.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.3x", "Mfr. Model Number": "3680C002", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "8.27\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "1.98lb", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

