This is one of Canon’s four standard-format, tilt-shift, manual-focus lenses. The 90mm, along with the Canon TS-E 45mm f/2.8, is generally thought to be among the sharpest lenses in Canon’s lineup.', 1300000.0, '{"Angle of View": "27°", "Aperture Blades": "9, rounded", "Brand": "Canon", "Dimensions": "3.42 × 4.59″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "77mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "90-90", "Focus Type": "Manual Focus Only", "Groups/Elements": "9/11", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon EF", "Lens Type": "Telephoto, For DSLR, Macro, and Tilt-Shift", "Maximum Aperture": "2.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.5x", "Mfr. Model Number": "2544A003", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "1.28’", "Stabilization": "No", "Tilt/Shift": "± 10° tilt\\n± 12mm shift", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "2.01lb", "Zoom Type": "Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Includes

