Parfocal Design. The parfocal design means this lens holds focus throughout its zoom range, and its internal-focusing floating-elements construction all but eliminates focus breathing.

Cinema Build. The 70-135mm T2.9’s aperture and focusing rings boast standard 0.8 mod gears so that you can easily install a follow-focus system. Its geared focus ring has 240° of travel and ensures smooth, precise focusing and zooming, while its 2.5-foot minimum focusing distance lets you get in close. You get a 100° zoom rotation range and an 80° iris rotation range. Its 80mm front diameter lets you use standard matte boxes, and there’s a 77mm filter thread to boot.

Durable, Lightweight Construction. This lens’s polycarbonate and glass-fiber body keeps its weight a low 3.5 lbs., so you can use it handheld or with a gimbal or drone. It’s about 8.4 inches long, which is fairly typical for a cine lens with this range.', 4250000.0, '{"Angle of View": "32-18º", "Aperture Blades": "16", "Brand": "DZOFilm", "Dimensions": "3.1 × 8.4″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "77.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On, Drop-In, and Matte Box Mount", "Focal Length": "70-135", "Focus Rotation": "270°", "Focus Type": "Manual Focus Only", "Front Lens Diameter": "80mm", "Gearing": "0.8 MOD zoom, focus, iris", "Groups/Elements": "11/17", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Canon RF", "Lens Type": "Telephoto, Cine, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "2.9", "Mfr. Model Number": "DZO-FF70135RF", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "2.5’", "Parfocal/Varifocal": "Parfocal", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "2.5 lb.", "Zoom Ratio": "1.9x", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

