Medium Telephoto Prime. The Fuji GF 250mm f/4 R LM OIS WR’s 197.5mm-equivalent focal length and reasonably bright maximum aperture make it great for subject-background isolation and working with shallow depth-of-field techniques. It’s also ideal for portraiture and landscape photography.

Manual Controls. Like many other GF lenses, the GF 250mm f/4 features a manual aperture ring with a C (Command) position to allow aperture adjustment via command dial.

Linear Autofocus Motor. The linear motor provides fast, quiet, and accurate autofocus performance, while its updated mechanism keeps the same focus position even when you turn off the camera. The lens’s internal-focusing design allows its physical length to remain unchanged while giving you consistent performance throughout the entire focusing range, and the Focus Preset function button lets you easily recall saved focusing positions.

Optical Image Stabilization. This lens’s built-in optical image stabilization system provides five stops of stabilization, according to Fuji.

High-Quality Optics. The GF 250mm f/4’s ten-group/sixteen-element design includes one super extra-low dispersion element and two extra-low dispersion elements to minimize chromatic aberrations, and to produce clear, high-contrast images.

Durable Build. The dust- and weather-sealed build lets you work under harsh conditions in temperatures as low as 14°F. A fluorine coating keeps flare and ghosting at bay while maintaining color fidelity.

Teleconverter Compatible. The GF 250mm f/4 R LM OIS WR is compatible with the Fuji GF 1.4x TC WR Teleconverter, which extends its focal length to 350mm.', 4225000.0, '{"Brand": "Fuji", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Fuji G", "Lens Type": "Telephoto"}', 'Includes

