INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (726, 1, 19, 'Fuji X100VI (Silver)', 'fuji-x100vi-silver', 'The Fuji X100VI (Silver) is a large-sensor fixed-lens compact camera that boasts an array of features aimed at bloggers and content creators. It’s a substantial upgrade to the wildly popular Fuji X100V. Key features include:

Improved video and stills; faster operation speed
40.2MP X-Trans CMOS 5 sensor; X-Processor 5 engine
In-body image stabilization; 425-point autofocus
Built-in 23mm f/2 lens; Frame.io functionality

What’s Changed? The Fuji X100VI (Silver) features quite a few improvements over its predecessor, the X100V, including an improved 40.2MP X-Trans CMOS 5 HR sensor, the faster X-Processor 5 engine, series-first in-body image stabilization, cropped 6.2K 30p video in 4:2:2 10-bit color, faster operation speed, a faster maximum continuous shooting rate, an updated autofocus system, and increased battery life when using the OVF.

40.2MP X-Trans CMOS 5 HR Sensor. The X100VI’s X-Trans 5 sensor uses an enhanced image-processing algorithm to increase resolution without affecting the signal-to-noise ratio, producing extremely sharp and clear images throughout its normal ISO range of 125-12,800.

X-Processor 5 Engine. The X-Processor 5 engine facilitates great low-light performance and supercharges operation speed. It greatly reduces startup time, shutter lag, and navigation. The combination of this engine and the X-Trans CMOS 5 sensor increases the maximum continuous shooting rate to 13 fps and extends the ISO-sensitivity range to 64-51,200 for photo and 125-25,600 for video.

6.2K 30p Video. The X100VI captures 6.2K 30p video in 4:2:2 10-bit color from a 1.23x cropped region of the sensor, HQ 4K 60p video at a 1.14x crop oversampled from 6.2K footage, sub-sampled 4K 60p video at a 1.14x crop, and sub-sampled 4K 60p video at the sensor’s full width. The micro-HDMI port lets you record 10-bit 4:2:2 footage to an optional external recorder, and you can use one of Fuji’s many built-in film-simulation modes to give your footage a distinct look.

Takin’ It To The Streets. The X100VI is purpose-built for street photography. Its 1/180,000 sec top electronic shutter speed and 1/4,000 maximum mechanical shutter speed mean you’ll be ready to capture even the most fast-moving subjects. If you hold down the shutter button, the X100VI records images at up to 20 fps at a 1.29x crop with the electronic shutter, and at 11 fps with the mechanical shutter.

In-Body Image Stabilization. The five-axis image-stabilization system—a first for the X series—markedly reduces the effects of camera shake on your footage by up to six stops so that you can easily shoot hand-held or in low light.

Focus, Focus, Focus. The X100VI’s hybrid autofocus system uses contrast- and phase-detection methods for fast, accurate performance in a wide range of lighting conditions. Its 425 selectable points cover almost the entire sensor for pinpoint focusing, even when capturing fast-moving subjects. A machine-trained subject-recognition autofocus feature can track an array of different subjects in any lighting conditions you throw at it.

Advanced Hybrid Viewfinder. The Advanced Hybrid Viewfinder lets you switch between optical viewfinder (OVF) and electronic viewfinder (EVF) modes with a dedicated lever. The 0.66x-magnification OVF mode recalls traditional rangefinder cameras, with an electronic rangefinder that you can manually adjust for improved accuracy. The 3.69m-dot EVF mode gives you 100% frame coverage and access to advanced electronic focusing options and precision manual focusing. Its fast refresh rate keeps lag to a minimum for smooth panning and tracking.

Integrated Fujinon 23mm f/2 Lens. This integrated wide-angle lens, which was carried over from the X100V, features a revised six-group/eight-element optical design that incorporates two aspherical elements for even greater sharpness and clarity. This lens provides a focal length equivalent to 35mm after sensor crop, which makes it great for everyday use. The fast f/2 aperture lets you shoot in low light, while giving you great depth-of-field control for subject-background isolation. While this lens is a fixed focal length, the X100VI includes 50mm- and 75mm-equivalent digital teleconverter settings that simulate longer focal lengths.

Film-Simulation Modes. The X100VI includes twenty film-simulation modes—among them REALA ACE—to give your shots and footage a distinct look based on many of Fujifilm’s classic film types. You get a number of monochrome modes that simulate the effects of color filters, and a Grain Effect mode that gives your shots an old-timey appearance.

Ergonomics and Build. The retro-styled body features physical control dials for settings selection, and precision ISO and shutter-speed adjustments; a tilting 3.0-inch, 1.62m-dot touchscreen LCD; and a rear joystick for autofocus control, menu navigation, and image playback. Most of the controls are on the right-hand side of the X100VI for easy one-handed shooting.

Additional Features. Built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth let you wirelessly share images and use a linked mobile device to remotely control the camera. The X100VI is powered by an NP-W126S battery, which gives you approximately 310 shots per charge when working with the EVF or 450 shots per charge with the OVF. You also get a single UHD-I compatible SD-card slot.

Frame.io Camera-to-Cloud Functionality. You can use this camera’s Wi-Fi or an ethernet connection to instantly and securely upload your Apple ProRes proxy video files and JPEG, HEIF, or RAW stills to the Frame.io cloud platform. Uploading your videos and shots to the cloud from your shooting location lets you speed up your workflow with real-time access and editing from anywhere. For more information, please click here.', 3100000.0, '{"Brand": "Fuji", "Camera Type": "Compact", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Environmental": "Environmental ProtectionWeather-Resistant (Unrated) with Optional AR-X100 Adapter Ring and PRF-49 Protector FilterOperating Temperature32 to 104°F / 0 to 40°COperating Humidity10 to 80%", "Exposure Control": "Shutter Speed – Mechanical1/4000 to 15 Minutes in Manual Mode1/4000 to 15 Minutes in Shutter Priority Mode1/4000 to 30 Seconds in Aperture Priority Mode1/4000 to 30 Seconds in Program ModeUp to 60 Minutes in Bulb ModeShutter Speed – Electronic1/180000 to 15 Minutes in Manual Mode1/180000 to 15 Minutes in Shutter Priority Mode1/180000 to 30 Seconds in Aperture Priority Mode1/180000 to 30 Seconds in Program ModeFixed 1 Second in Bulb ModeBulb/Time ModeBulb ModeISO Sensitivity Range – Photo125 to 12,800 (Extended: 64 to 51,200)ISO Sensitivity Range – Video125 to 12,800 (Extended: 25,600)Metering MethodsAverage, Center-Weighted Average, Multi, Spot, TTL 256-ZonesExposure ModesAperture Priority, Manual, Program, Shutter PriorityExposure Compensation-5 to +5 EV (1/3 EV Steps)White Balance2500 to 10,000KWhite-Balance PresetsAWB, Auto, Color Temperature, Custom, Custom 1, Custom 2, Daylight, Fluorescent (Cool White), Fluorescent (Daylight), Fluorescent (Warm White), Incandescent, Shade, UnderwaterContinuous Shooting – Electronic ShutterUp to 13 fps for up to 80 Frames (JPEG) / 38 Frames (RAW)Up to 8.9 fps for up to 84 Frames (JPEG) / 38 Frames (RAW)Continuous Shooting – Mechanical ShutterUp to 11 fps for up to 38 Frames (JPEG) / 33 Frames (RAW)Up to 8 fps for up to 76 Frames (JPEG) / 35 Frames (RAW)Up to 6 fps for up to 97 Frames (JPEG) / 36 Frames (RAW)Interval RecordingYesSelf-Timer2/10-Second Delay", "Flash": "Built-In Flash/LightYes, Flash OnlyFlash ModesAuto, Commander, Manual, Slow SyncEffective Flash RangeISO 1600: 24.3’ / 7.4mExternal Flash ConnectionShoe Mount</ul", "General": "Battery Type1x NP-W126S Rechargeable Lithium-Ion (Approx. 310 Shots)Shoe Mount1x Hot ShoeDimensions (W x H x D)5 × 2.9 × 2.2″ / 128 × 74.8 × 55.3mmWeight1.1 lb. / 521 g (With Battery, Recording Media)1.0 lb. / 471 g (Body Only)", "Imaging": "Sensor ResolutionEffective: 40.2 Megapixel (7728 × 5152)Image Sensor23.5 × 15.7mm (APS-C) CMOSImage StabilizationSensor-Shift, 5-AxisDigital (Video Only)", "Interface": "Media/Memory Card SlotSingle Slot: SD/SDHC/SDXCInternal MemoryNoVideo I/O1x Micro-HDMI (Unspecified Signal) OutputAudio I/O1x 2.5mm Submini TRS Stereo Microphone InputPower I/O1x USB-C InputOther I/O1x USB-C Data Output (Shared with Power Input)1x 2.5mm Sub-Mini FlashSync Input (Shared with Mic/Line Input)WirelessWi-Fi 5 (802.11ac), Bluetooth 4.2Mobile App CompatibleYes: Android & iOSApp Name: FUJIFILM XAppFunctionality: Access Stored Files, Adjust Settings, Firmware Update, Remote Control, View Live FeedGlobal Positioning (GPS, GLONASS, etc.)GPS, Via Connected Smartphone", "Item Type": "Camera", "Lens": "Focal Length23mm (35mm Equivalent: 35mm)Maximum Aperturef/2Minimum Aperturef/16Focus Range3.9\\" to Infinity / 10 cm to InfinityGroups/Elements6/8Filter Size49mm (Front)", "Maximum Video Resolution": "6K", "Mfr. Model Number": "16821822", "Monitor": "Display Size3\\"Resolution1,620,000 DotDisplay TypeTilting Touchscreen LCD", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Tilt", "Sensor Size": "APS-C", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Still Image Capture": "Aspect Ratio1:1, 3:2, 4:3, 5:4, 16:9Image File FormatsHEIF, JPEG, RAW, TIFFBit Depth14-Bit", "Video Capture": "Internal Recording Modes – H.265 Long GOP/MOV 4:2:2/4:2:0 10-Bit6240 × 3510 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [50 to 200 Mb/s]Internal Recording Modes – H.264 Long GOP/H.265 Long GOP/MOV/MP4 4:2:2/4:2:0 8/10-BitDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps [50 to 200 Mb/s]3840 × 2160 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps [50 to 200 Mb/s]2048 × 1080 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97/50/59.94/100/120/200/240 fps [50 to 200 Mb/s]1920 × 1080 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97/50/59.94/100/120/200/240 fps [50 to 200 Mb/s]External Recording Modes – 4:2:2 10-Bit via HDMI6240 × 3510 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fpsDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps3840 × 2160 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps2048 × 1080 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps1920 × 1080 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97/50/59.94/100/120 fpsRecording LimitUp to 45 Minutes in 4KUp to 50 Minutes in 1080p HFRIP StreamingNoBuilt-In Microphone TypeStereoAudio Recording24-Bit 48 kHz LPCM AudioMPEG4: 24-Bit 48 kHz LPCM AudioMP4: AAC Audio", "Viewfinder": "TypeOpticalBuilt-In Electronic (OLED)Resolution3,690,000 DotCoverage100%MagnificationApprox. 0.66xDiopter Adjustment-4 to +2", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

	Fuji X100VI (Silver)
	Fuji X100VI front cap
	Fuji NP-W126S battery
	Fuji BC-W126S charger
	Fuji BC-T125 plug adapter
	Thunderbolt 4 USB cable – 3-foot', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (727, 2, 19, 'Fuji XC 13-33mm f/3.5-6.3 OIS', 'fuji-xc-13-33mm-f-3-5-6-3-ois', 'The Fuji XC 13-33mm f/3.5-6.3 OIS is a highly portable zoom lens for X-mount APS-C Fuji cameras. Key features include:

Four-stop optical image stabilization
STM motor
7.9" minimum focusing length
Only 1.5" long and 4.4 oz

Portable Crop-Frame Zoom. With an equivalent focal range of 20-50mm (in 35mm terms), this tiny Fuji lens is an ideal companion for landscapes and portraits alike. The STM motor balances speed with precision, making it a great choice for street and travel photography.

Overall Usability. The aperture range is f/3.5 at the wide end and f/6.3 on the long end, which isn’t ideal for low light. However, that is compensated for with four-stop optical image stabilization. It does offer a constant 7.9" minimum focusing distance for extreme closeups. The optical design uses unique flare-suppressing elements for crisp, clean results.

Try it with These Cameras. At only 1.5 inches long, this is a really fun walking-around lens that would pair well both functionally and aesthetically with Fuji’s rangefinder-style portable cameras, such as the Fuji X-E5 or the Fuji X-M5.', 775000.0, '{"Angle of View": "95.1-46.6°", "Brand": "Fuji", "Dimensions": "2.4 × 1.5″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "49.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "APS-C", "Lens Mount": "Fuji X", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle and For Mirrorless", "Mfr. Model Number": "16960719", "Optical Design": "Groups/Elements9/10Aperture Blades9, Rounded", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "0.3 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Fuji XC 13-33mm f/3.5-6.3 OIS
	49mm Hoya EVO antistatic filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (728, 2, 19, 'Fuji XC 15-45mm f/3.5-5.6 OIS PZ', 'fuji-xc-15-45mm-f-3-5-5-6-ois-pz', 'The Fuji XC 15-45mm f/3.5-5.6 OIS PZ is a versatile normal-range power zoom for Fuji X-mount cameras. Key features include:

Versatile walk-around zoom for daylight conditions
Built-in optical image stabilization and autofocus
Nine-group/ten-element optical design
High-quality images throughout the zoom range

Versatile Normal-Range Power Zoom. Providing a 35mm-equivalent range of 23-69mm, the compact, retractable XC 15-45mm is great as a walk-around zoom lens in daylight conditions. The built-in optical image stabilization allows you to hand-hold slower shutter speeds, which is very helpful in low light with the limited f/3.5-5.6 aperture. It also offers a fast, silent autofocus system.

High-Quality Optics. The nine-group/ten-element optical design ensures high image quality. Three aspherical elements and two extra-low dispersion elements help to minimize chromatic aberrations, distortions, and color fringing throughout the zoom range. There’s also Fuji’s Super Electron Beam Coating, which reduces ghosting and lens flare.

Versatility. The rounded seven-blade diaphragm gives you pleasing bokeh when you’re using selective focus and shallow depth of field. You can get up close with the 5.1-inch minimum focusing distance.', 625000.0, '{"Angle of View": "86.9° to 35°", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Autofocus": "Autofocus", "Brand": "Fuji", "Extra Low-Dispersion Elements": "2", "Groups/Elements": "9/10", "Hood Included": "No", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Fuji X", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle and Standard", "Maximum Magnification": "0.24x", "Mfr. Model Number": "16565789", "Minimum Aperture": "22.0"}', 'Includes

	Fuji XC 15-45mm
	52mm protective filter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (729, 2, 19, 'Fuji XC 35mm f/2', 'fuji-xc-35mm-f-2', 'The Fuji XC 35mm f/2 is a normal-length prime for Fuji X-mount cameras. Key features include:

Great for low-light photography
High-quality optical design
Fast, accurate autofocus system
Fourteen-inch minimum focusing distance

Fast-Aperture Normal-Length Prime. A 35mm-equivalent focal length of 53mm and an f/2 aperture make the Fuji XC 35mm f/2 a good choice for shooting in low light, but it’s also really useful for just about any type of photography.

High-Quality Optics. This lens’s nine-element/six-group design includes two aspherical elements that help to minimize chromatic aberrations and distortions for increased clarity and sharpness. A rounded nine-blade aperture rounds out the optical feature set, creating a pleasing out-of-focus quality when working with shallow depth of field.

Stepping Motor Autofocus System. The XC 35mm f/2 features a quick and accurate autofocus system that delivers an extremely smooth, incredibly quiet performance. This lens is capable of finding focus as quickly as 0.08 sec, and its 14-inch minimum focusing distance allows shooters to get very close to their subjects. Its internal-focusing design allows its physical length to remain unchanged while giving you consistent performance throughout the entire focusing range.', 550000.0, '{"Angle of View": "44.2°", "Aperture Blades": "9, Rounded", "Autofocus": "Autofocus", "Brand": "Fuji", "Groups/Elements": "6/9", "Hood Included": "No", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Fuji X", "Lens Type": "Standard", "Maximum Magnification": "0.14x", "Mfr. Model Number": "16647434", "Minimum Aperture": "16.0"}', 'Includes

	Fuji 35mm f/2 XC
	43mm protective filter
	Front & rear lens caps', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (730, 2, 19, 'Fuji XF 10-24mm f/4 R OIS WR', 'fuji-xf-10-24mm-f-4-r-ois-wr', 'The Fuji XF 10-24mm f/4 R OIS WR is a versatile wide-angle zoom designed for Fuji X-mount mirrorless cameras. Key features include:

Great for capturing sweeping landscapes and cityscapes
Advanced optical design
Up to 3.5 stops of optical image stabilization
Fast, accurate, nearly silent autofocus

Versatile Wide-Angle Zoom. With a focal length range equivalent to 15-36mm after crop factor, the Fuji XF 10-24mm f/4 R OIS WR gives users a high-quality wide-angle zoom that’s ideal for use in a range of photo and video applications. It’s great for capturing sweeping landscapes and cityscapes. The constant f/4 aperture isn’t quite fast enough for low-light shooting, but it’s better than a variable-aperture zoom and helps to limit this lens’s size and weight.

High-Quality Optics. The ten-group/fourteen-element optical design features four aspherical elements and four extra-low dispersion elements, which effectively eliminate chromatic, spherical, and axial aberrations while keeping distortion to a minimum. This results in images with consistent edge-to-edge sharpness and illumination. Super EBC coating helps to eliminate flare and ghosting while helping ensure contrast and color fidelity.

Optical Image Stabilization.- This lens’s built-in optical image stabilization system minimizes the appearance of camera shake by up to 3.5 stops to help keep your images sharp when you’re working with longer focal lengths or slower shutter speeds.

Stepping Autofocus Motor. The XF 10-24mm’s stepping motor and internal-focusing design work in tandem to provide fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance that’s ideal for stills and video alike. Its rounded seven-blade diaphragm produces pleasing bokeh when you’re using selective-focusing and shallow depth-of-field techniques, while its 9.4-inch minimum focusing distance lets you get in close.

Updated Physical Design. This pro-caliber lens offers a weather-resistant design to keep you shooting even in adverse conditions. The aperture ring has a locking “A” position and labeled f/stop scale, and the aperture and focus rings are slightly smaller than on Fuji’s previous 10-24mm to help reduce the lens’s weight.', 1725000.0, '{"Angle of View": "110° to 61.2°", "Aperture Blades": "7, Rounded", "Autofocus": "Autofocus", "Brand": "Fuji", "Extra Low-Dispersion Elements": "4", "Groups/Elements": "10/14", "Hood Included": "Yes", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Fuji X", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle and Wide Angle", "Maximum Magnification": "0.16x", "Mfr. Model Number": "16666753", "Minimum Aperture": "22.0"}', 'Includes

	Fuji XF 10-24mm f/4
	Front & rear caps
	72mm protective filter
	Hood
	Lens pouch', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (731, 2, 19, 'Fuji XF 100-400mm f/4.5-5.6 R LM OIS WR', 'fuji-xf-100-400mm-f-4-5-5-6-r-lm-ois-wr', 'The Fuji XF 100-400mm f/4.5-5.6 R LM OIS WR gives X-Mount mirrorless users a pro-caliber super telephoto zoom lens. Key features include:

Great for long-distance sports and wildlife photography
Fast, nearly silent autofocus
Five-stop optical image stabilization
High-quality optics

Super Telephoto Zoom. With its 152-609mm equivalent focal length after sensor crop, the Fuji XF 100-400mm f/4.5-5.6 R LM OIS WR is your go-to zoom lens for long-distance sports and wildlife photography. While not the brightest, the f/4.5-5.6 aperture is plenty fast for shooting fast-moving subjects in daylight to moderately low-light conditions.

Twin Linear Autofocus Motor. Provides smooth yet quick performance for fast-moving subjects. Built-in focus limiting switch allows you to constrain focus when shooting distant subjects, or disengage to enable the full range.

Optical Image Stabilization. Provides five stops of stabilization, according to Fuji.

Optics. The 14-group/21-element optical formula offers a combination of five ED elements and one Super ED element to minimize chromatic aberrations and fringing throughout the zoom range.

Professional Build. Thirteen distinct weather seals across the barrel make this lens a strong workhorse in even the poorest of conditions. The included tripod ring enables tripod/monopod use (recommended for extended shooting periods), and the included lens hood features a sliding window for better CP and variable ND filter use.

Teleconverter Compatible. This lens is compatible with the Fuji XF1.4x TC WR and XF 2x TC WR Teleconverters, which are available as separate rental items.', 2875000.0, '{"Angle of View": "16.2° – 4.1°", "Brand": "Fuji", "Dimensions": "Length: 8.29\\"", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Fuji X", "Lens Type": "Telephoto and Supertelephoto", "Mfr. Model Number": "16501109"}', 'Includes

