S35 Take on 2/3 ENG Lenses. Merging functionality with versatility, Fuji set out to make a portable broadcast-style lens that can be used for cinematic purposes as well as news gathering. With a digital drive unit and zoom rocker switch, the Duvo HZK 24-300mm can be operated in the same way as portable-type broadcast zoom lenses while also being equipped with 0.8M focus ring gearing for traditional cinema-style focus pulling.

For All Formats. Not only does this lens offer an incredibly versatile focal length range, but it also offers a 1.5x expander setting for compatibility with full frame cameras. The Duvo HZK 24-300mm is capable of covering an image circle up to 28.5mm across the entire zoom range in its default Super35 mode. Engage the 1.5x expander and you get coverage up to 41.3mm. The use of the expander shifts the focal length by 1.5 for a 36-450mm range that is great for faraway subjects. Despite the over 12x zoom range, the Duvo maintains a fast T2.9-4.2 maximum aperture.

User-Friendly Features. The Fuji Duvo HZK 24-300mm is for PL mount cameras and is 6.5 pounds and 10.6 inches long, allowing it to be used handheld. It offers a range of pro-level features, including breathing compensation, Zeiss eXtended Data support, and compatibility with third-party lens controllers. The front diameter is an industry-standard 114mm for easy pairing with a matte box. The rubber hood can accommodate a 127mm filter. To tackle the decrease in sharpness that zooms are prone to, the Duvo includes a Remote Back Focus feature that will automatically adjust focus to ensure consistency in sharpness when moving between focal lengths. This lens is a great choice for sports/news and narrative/creative cinematographers alike.', 32775000.0, '{"Angle of View": "54.8-2.7º", "Aperture Blades": "9", "Brand": "Fuji", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "PL", "Lens Type": "Standard and Broadcast", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "6.5 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

