INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1070, 1, 38, 'Nikon D750', 'nikon-d750', 'The Nikon D750 is a prosumer-level full-frame DSLR that’s been designed with both photographers and videographers in mind. Looking for an updated model? We also carry the Nikon D780. Key features include:

24.3MP FX-Format CMOS sensor
51-point autofocus system
Sharp images and excellent low-light performance
Full HD video capture at 60p

24.3MP FX-Format CMOS Sensor. The D750’s full-frame sensor balances high-resolution images with great low-light performance. It offers a normal ISO range of 100-12,800, with the ability to extend to 50-51,200 when needed. The EXPEED 4 image processor enables 6.5 full-resolution fps in continuous shooting, making it the fastest non-pro level full-frame DSLR to date (September 2014).

Full HD Video Recording. The D750 borrows nearly all of its video specs from its big brother, the D810. It captures Full HD 1920 × 1080 video at up to 60p. It has Flat Picture Control profile for greater flexibility in post-production, expanded ISO options including full 64-12,800 range and Auto ISO capability, zebra stripes, a built-in stereo microphone, and uncompressed 4:2:2 8-bit HDMI output with simultaneous recording to memory cards.

Pro-Caliber Autofocus. The D750’s improved version of the Multi-CAM 3500FX autofocus sensor has detection sensitivity down to -3 EV for superior low-light focusing. The autofocus specs are otherwise the same as the D810’s, with 51 AF points to choose from (15 of which are cross-type).

Build. With the D750, you’re getting a magnesium-alloy chassis and shell that feel great. The 3.2" 1,229k-dot tilting LCD is a welcome addition for video shooters and photo shooters alike, and the large pentaprism optical viewfinder offers 100% frame coverage with organic EL display to display shooting information.

Other Notable Features. Built-in Wi-Fi connectivity allows wireless image capture, review and transfer from a smartphone with the Nikon Wireless Mobile Utility app installed. Like many other Nikon DSLRs, the D750 has an in-camera intervalometer for capturing time-lapse video straight from the camera. The built-in pop-up flash provides both fill-flash and Nikon CLS control, and dual SD slots give users recording flexibility. It uses the Nikon EN-EL15 rechargeable battery (1 included) that’s rated for 1,230 shots per charge, or roughly 55 minutes of continuous video recording.', 2800000.0, '{"Brand": "Nikon", "Camera Mount": "Nikon F", "Camera Type": "DSLR", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Environmental": "Operating Temperature32 to 104°F / 0 to 40°C", "Exposure Control": "Shutter TypeElectronic ShutterShutter Speed – Electronic Front Curtain Shutter1/4000 to 30 SecondsBulb/Time ModeBulb Mode, Time ModeISO Sensitivity – Photo100 to 12,800 in Auto Mode (Extended: 50 to 51,200)ISO Sensitivity – Video200 to 12,800 in Auto ModeMetering Method3D Color Matrix, Center-Weighted Average, Highlight Weighted, SpotExposure ModesAperture Priority, Manual, Program, Shutter PriorityExposure Compensation-5 to +5 EV (1/3, 1/2 EV Steps)Metering Range0 to 20 EVWhite Balance PresetsAuto, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Direct Sunlight, Flash, Fluorescent, Incandescent, Preset Manual, ShadeContinuous ShootingUp to 6.5 fpsInterval RecordingYesSelf-Timer2/5/10/20-Second Delay", "Flash": "Built-In FlashYesFlash ModesAuto, Auto/Red-Eye Reduction, Fill Flash, Hi-Speed Sync, Off, Rear Curtain/Slow Sync, Rear Sync, Red-Eye Reduction, Slow Sync, Slow Sync/Red-Eye ReductionGuide Number39’ / 11.89m at ISO 100Maximum Sync Speed1/200 SecondFlash Compensation-3 to +1 EV (1/3, 1/2, 1 EV Steps)Dedicated Flash SystemiTTLExternal Flash ConnectionHot Shoe", "Focusing": "Focus TypeAuto and Manual FocusFocus ModeAutomatic, Continuous-Servo AF, Full-Time Servo, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AFAutofocus PointsPhase Detection: 51 (15 Cross-Type)Autofocus Sensitivity-3 to +19 EV", "General": "Battery Type1x EN-EL15 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 7 VDC, 1900 mAhTripod Mounting Thread1x 1/4\\"-20 Female (Bottom)Accessory Mount1x Hot Shoe MountMaterial of ConstructionMagnesium AlloyDimensions (W x H x D) – camera body only5.5 × 4.4 × 3.1″ / 140.5 × 113 × 78mmWeight – camera body only1.7 lb. / 750 g", "Imaging": "Sensor ResolutionActual: 24.93 MegapixelEffective: 24.3 Megapixel (6016 × 4016)Image Sensor35.9 × 24mm (Full-Frame) CMOSImage StabilizationNoneMirror Lock-UpYesCapture TypeStills & Video", "Interface": "Media/Memory Card SlotDual Slot: SD/SDHC/SDXC (UHS-I)Video I/O1x Mini-HDMI OutputAudio I/O1x Mini-HDMI OutputPower I/ONoneOther I/O1x Mini-USB 8-Pin (USB 2.0) OutputWirelessWi-FiGlobal Positioning (GPS, GLONASS, etc.)None", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Video Resolution": "1080p", "Mfr. Model Number": "1543", "Monitor": "Size3.2\\"Resolution1,229,000 DotDisplay TypeTilting LCDSecondary DisplayTop: Status Display", "Screen Type": "Tilt", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Stabilization": "No", "Still Image Capture": "Image Sizes\\n3:2 JPEG3936 × 26242944 × 19681968 × 1312Aspect Ratio3:2Image File FormatsJPEG, RAWBit Depth14-BitInternal Recording Modes\\nH.264/MOV1920 × 1080p at 23.98/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps1280 × 720 at 50/59.94 fpsExternal Recording Modes\\nHDMI1920 × 1080p at 23.98/25/29.97/59.94 fps1280 × 720 at 29.97/50/59.94 fpsBroadcast OutputNTSC/PALIP StreamingNoneBuilt-In Microphone TypeStereoAudio RecordingLPCM Audio", "Viewfinder": "TypeOptical (Pentaprism)Eye Point21mmCoverage100%MagnificationApprox. 0.7xDiopter Adjustment-3 to +1", "Viewfinder Type": "Optical", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi"}', 'Includes

	D750 camera
	Body cap
