All-in-One Wide-to-Telephoto Zoom. With full-frame sensor coverage, this lens’s versatile 24-200mm focal length is excellent for portraiture, landscape photography, architectural photography, candid street photography, and anything in between. It covers the wide-to-telephoto focal lengths to give you serious flexibility while still maximizing image quality and speed.

High-Quality Optics. The Nikon Z 24-200mm’s fifteen-group/nineteen-element optical design features two extra-low dispersion elements and two aspherical elements to promote sharpness and color rendering while limiting chromatic aberrations. Nikon has applied ARNEO, Nano Crystal, and Super Integrated coatings to the elements to combat ghosting and lens flare, even when you’re working in bright or backlit conditions.

Variable Aperture. The variable f/4-6.3 aperture isn’t useful for low-light shooting, so you’ll probably want to stick with outdoor-lighting conditions for best results. The rounded seven-blade diaphragm contributes to smooth, pleasing bokeh for shallow depth-of-field techniques.

Vibration Reduction. The built-in vibration reduction provides up to five stops of correction for minimizing camera shake at slower shutter speeds and producing sharper results when shooting hand-held.

Stepping Motor Autofocus System. The stepping motor allows for fast, silent, and smooth operation. Pairing a speedy AF system together with a continuous manual mechanism allows you to hit your focus with confidence, while the internal-focusing design means that the lens maintains its length during focusing.

Advanced Build. This lens’s durable, moisture-resistant construction means you can use it in adverse conditions without worry. A programmable control ring lets you adjust manual focus, aperture, or exposure compensation.', 1350000.0, '{"Angle of View": "84° to 12° 20’", "Aperture Blades": "7, Rounded", "Brand": "Nikon", "Extra Low-Dispersion Elements": "2", "Groups/Elements": "15/19", "Hood Included": "Yes", "Item Type": "Lens", "Length": "4.5\\"", "Lens Mount": "Nikon Z", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Standard, and Telephoto", "Maximum Magnification": "0.28x", "Mfr. Model Number": "20092"}', 'Includes

