	Case
	Case Insert (bolster)
	Case Insert', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1198, 1, 46, 'PTZOptics Move SE 30x-SDI/HDMI/USB/IP Camera', 'ptzoptics-move-se-30x-sdi-hdmi-usb-ip-camera', 'The PTZOptics Move SE 30x is an auto-tracking streaming camera with bandwidth-saving NDI built in. Key features include:

Captures 1080p60 over IP, HDMI, USB-C, or 3G-SDI
Auto-tracks subject, easy subject switching
Transmits two simultaneous streams with any two outputs
Supports external audio, embeds in stream

Presentation Perfect. Move around a stage and the PTZOptics Move SE is right there with you, thanks to smooth and responsive AI-powered automatic tracking with speeds up to 100 degrees per second. As the PTZ name suggests, this camera also pans, tilts, and zooms for dynamic coverage of presenters and performers. The lens is designed specifically for studios, conference rooms, stages, churches, and more thanks to its flexible fields of view and large aperture range.

Power to Control the Scene. There are several ways to control this camera and your stream, whether you’re using OBS, PTZOptics’s own selection of free softwares, or by typing ptzoptics.local into a browser and typing in admin for both username and password to access the camera’s web UI. Not only can you control the camera remotely this way, but you can adjust settings for exposure, color, presets, audio, and RTMP for up to two simultaneous streams. Adjust orientation and framing from up to nearly 30 feet away with the included remote – a great feature for solo operators. You also have the option to connect the camera to an IP/serial joystick controller, such as the PTZOptics PT-SUPERJOY-G1.

High-Quality Footage 24/7. Connect directly to your computer over USB-C or to a video switcher over HDMI/SDI while powering the camera with wall power or via PoE (power-over-Ethernet). There is no power switch on this camera. It is designed to be on continuously when using the power adapter or PoE (do not use both sources of power at once). This is an ideal setup for long events. Though this camera only streams in 1080p (there is also a 4K version available), it is no slouch in other areas. The 30x zoom can display a half-body shot that nearly fills the frame from around 80 feet away! Automatically embed high-quality sound when you connect external audio equipment (line level required) via a 3.5mm port. The Move SE is natively-equipped with the Network Device Interface High Efficiency (NDI|HX) protocol for high-quality video streaming in limited bandwidth situations and for compatibility with other networked NDI-enabled devices.

Level Up Your Streaming Game. Whether you’re actually streaming games or operating a multi-view setup for a concert, the PTZOptics Move SE 30x offers both stellar automatic settings and massive customization over operation and output, making it a great choice for novices and professionals alike.', 2825000.0, '{"Brand": "PTZOptics", "Camera Type": "PTZ", "Compatible Media": "External Storage", "General": "Accessory Mounts1x 1/4\\"-20 (bottom)Dimensions (W x H x D)5.6 × 6.5 × 6.7″Mfr. Model NumberPT30X-SE-GY-G3MonitorNo, software-based onlyWeight3 lb.WirelessIR (for included remote)", "Imaging": "ISODynamic Range: 8 stopsISO Range: 100-12,800 (effective range, approximate)Max ResolutionFHD (1920 × 1080)ND FiltersNo (also no IR cut filter)Sensor2.07MP 1/2.8\\"-Type CMOSShutter1/30-1/1000 sec.StabilizationNo", "Inputs/Outputs": "Audio I/O1x 3.5mm line in jack1x 3.5mm line out jackOther I/O1x USB-C1x USB-A (firmware)1x RS-485 in1x RS-232 in1x RS-232 outPower I/O1x 12V DC1x Ethernet (PoE)Storage I/ONoVideo I/O1x BNC (3G-SDI)1x HDMI", "Item Type": "Camera", "Lens": "Angle of ViewHorizontal: 2.3-60.7ºVertical: 1.28-34.1ºFilter SizeNoFocal Length4.42-132.6mmFocus TypeAutofocus and Manual FocusMax Aperturef/1.8-2.8Min Focusing DistanceN/A (there is a “close” mode)Prime/ZoomZoom (30x optical, 16x digital)", "Maximum Video Resolution": "1080p", "Sensor Size": "1-Inch", "Stabilization": "No", "Video Capture": "CompressionH.265 HEVCH.264 AVCM-JPEGFormat.MP4.MOV.AVIResolutionFHD (1920 × 1080) up to 60 fps via HDMI, SDI, USB-C, IP", "Weather Sealing": "No"}', 'Includes

	PTZOptics Move SE 30x camera
	PTZOptics IR remote
	AC adapter

• 7’ PTZOptics DB9 to Mini DIN8 RS-232 cable
	HPRC4050 hard case', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1199, 2, 44, 'Panasonic 100-300mm f/4-5.6 Power OIS II', 'panasonic-100-300mm-f-4-5-6-power-ois-ii', 'The Panasonic 100-300mm f/4-5.6 Power OIS II is a super telephoto zoom designed for the Micro 4/3 system. Key features include:

High-quality optics for sharp, clear images
200-600mm focal length (35mm equivalent)
Fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus system
POWER Optical Image Stabilization system

What’s Changed? This update to the original Panasonic 100-300mm f/4-5.6 OIS sees a new Power OIS system that adds compatibility with Panasonic’s cameras with 5-axis Dual IS / Dual IS II.  Additional changes include an autofocus system update for faster performance, smoother automatic exposure changes via new iris, and cosmetic changes to the barrel.

Super Telephoto Zoom. With a focal length equivalent to 200-600mm after crop factor, the Panasonic 100-300mm f/4-5.6 Power OIS II is great for sports, nature, and wildlife photography.

High-Quality Optics. The Leica influence shows in this lens’s optics. The 100-300 features one extra-low dispersion element to reduce chromatic and spherical aberrations throughout the zoom range while keeping your images clear and sharp. A Nano Surface Coating reduces ghosting and flare.

Linear Autofocus Motor. This lens’s linear motor provides fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for still images and videos alike.

POWER Optical Image Stabilization. The in-lens stabilizer helps to minimize camera shake. Dual-IS compatibility with supported Panasonic cameras works in tandem with sensor stabilization to further eliminate camera shake.

High-Quality Build. The 100-300mm’s high-quality splash- and dustproof build gives you peace of mind when shooting in adverse conditions.', 1425000.0, '{"Angle of View": "12° – 4.1°", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Dimensions": "Length: 4.96\\"", "Groups/Elements": "12/17", "Hood Included": "Yes", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Micro 4/3", "Lens Type": "Supertelephoto", "Magnification": "0.21x", "Mfr. Model Number": "H-FSA100300"}', 'Includes

	Lens
	Front & rear caps
	Lens hood
	67mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1200, 2, 44, 'Panasonic 12-35mm f/2.8 X Power OIS II', 'panasonic-12-35mm-f-2-8-x-power-ois-ii', 'The Panasonic 12-35mm f/2.8 X Power OIS II is a fast-aperture standard zoom designed for the Micro 4/3 system, and the predecessor to the Panasonic Leica 12-35mm f/2.8 ASPH Vario-Elmarit Power IOS. Key features include:

High-quality optics for sharp, clear images
24-70mm focal length (35mm equivalent)
Fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus system
POWER Optical Image Stabilization system

Fast-Aperture Standard Zoom. With a focal length equivalent to 24-70mm after crop factor, the Panasonic 12-35mm f/2.8 X Power OIS II is great for reportage and everyday photography.

High-Quality Optics. The Leica influence shows in this lens’s optics. The 12-35 features four aspherical elements and one extra-low dispersion element to drastically reduce chromatic and spherical aberrations throughout the zoom range while keeping your images clear and sharp. A Nano Surface Coating reduces ghosting and flare.

Linear Autofocus Motor. This lens’s linear motor provides fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus performance for still images and videos alike.

POWER Optical Image Stabilization. The in-lens stabilizer helps to minimize camera shake. Dual-IS compatibility with supported Panasonic cameras works in tandem with sensor stabilization to further eliminate camera shake.

High-Quality Build. The 12-35mm’s high-quality splash-, dust-, and freezeproof metal build gives you peace of mind when shooting in adverse conditions.', 1425000.0, '{"Angle of View": "84° – 34°", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Groups/Elements": "9/14", "Hood Included": "Yes", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Micro 4/3", "Lens Type": "Standard", "Magnification": "0.17x", "Mfr. Model Number": "H-HSA12035"}', 'Includes

	Panasonic 12-35mm f/2.8
	Front & rear caps
	Lens hood
	58mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1201, 2, 44, 'Panasonic 12-60mm f/3.5-5.6 Power OIS', 'panasonic-12-60mm-f-3-5-5-6-power-ois', 'The Panasonic 12-60mm f/3.5-5.6 Power OIS is a compact, normal-range zoom lens for Micro 4/3 cameras and camcorders. Key features include:

Excellent general-purpose travel zoom
Power Optical Image Stabilization system
Fast, silent autofocus
High-quality optics for sharp, clear images

Travel-Friendly Zoom. With a focal range equivalent to 24-120mm after sensor-crop factor, the Panasonic 12-60mm f/3.5-5.6 Power OIS is a great choice as a general-purpose travel zoom. The f/3.5-5.6 variable aperture won’t excel in dark conditions, but that’s not its intended use.

Power Optical Image Stabilization. In-lens stabilizer helps to minimize camera shake. Dual-IS compatibility with supported Panasonic cameras works in tandem with sensor stabilization to further eliminate camera shake.

Fast Autofocus. The inner focus drive system and stepping motor provides fast, silent performance when shooting still images and video.

Optics and Build. One extra-low dispersion element and three aspherical elements reduce optical aberrations while maximizing sharpness and clarity throughout the zoom range. The lens’s dust- and splash-proof construction gives you peace of mind when shooting in the elements.', 950000.0, '{"Angle of View": "4/3 Frame: 84.05° – 20.44°", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Dimensions": "Length: 2.6\\"", "Focusing System": "Internal and stepping motor", "Groups/Elements": "9/11", "Hood Included": "Yes", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Micro 4/3", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Standard, and Telephoto", "Maximum Magnification": "0.27x", "Mfr. Model Number": "H-FS12060", "Weather Resistant": "Yes", "Zoom Method": "Barrel extending"}', 'Includes

	Panasonic 12-60mm
	Hood
	Front & rear caps
	58mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1202, 2, 44, 'Panasonic 14-140mm f/3.5-5.6 II ASPH Power OIS', 'panasonic-14-140mm-f-3-5-5-6-ii-asph-power-ois', 'The Panasonic 14-140mm f/3.5-5.6 II ASPH Power OIS is a versatile, durable wide-angle to telephoto zoom designed for Micro 4/3 cameras. Key features include:

Versatile wide-angle to telephoto zoom
High-quality optical formula for maximum sharpness
Fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus system
Built-in optical image stabilization

What’s Changed? Not much.  This updated version sees the addition of weather-sealing that the previous generation Panasonic 14-140mm f/3.5-5.6 OIS lacked.  However, as usual, take “weather-sealed” with a grain of salt with any lens.

Versatile All-in-One Zoom. The Panasonic 14-140mm f/3.5-5.6 II ASPH Power OIS’s versatile 28-280mm equivalent focal length range makes it a solid choice for a range of applications, from landscapes to portraiture. Its 11.8-inch minimum focusing distance and 0.25x maximum magnification make it great for capturing close-up subjects.

High-Quality Optical Design. The twelve-group/thirteen-element optical formula includes three aspherical elements and two extra-low dispersion elements to increase clarity and sharpness while reducing chromatic aberrations and distortion. Multi-coatings have been applied to the elements to combat flare and ghosting.

High-Speed Stepping Autofocus Motor. The stepping motor provides fast, accurate, nearly silent autofocus performance for still and video use. This autofocus system is compatible with Lumix cameras’ high-speed contrast-detection autofocus systems for speeds up to 240 fps.

Optical Image Stabilization. The in-lens stabilizer helps to combat camera shake, allowing you to shoot hand-held at slower shutter speeds.', 975000.0, '{"Angle of View": "75° to 8.8°", "Aperture Blades": "7, Rounded", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Groups/Elements": "12/14", "Hood Included": "Yes", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Micro 4/3", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Standard, and Telephoto", "Maximum Magnification": "0.25x", "Mfr. Model Number": "H-FSA14140"}', 'Includes

	Panasonic 14-140mm f/3.5-5.6 II ASPH OIS
	H-FS14140 hood
	Front & rear caps
	Bag
	58mm protective filter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1203, 2, 44, 'Panasonic 16-35mm f/4 S PRO', 'panasonic-16-35mm-f-4-s-pro', 'The Panasonic 16-35mm f/4 S PRO is a versatile wide-angle zoom for L-mount mirrorless cameras. Key features include:

Versatile wide-angle zoom
Fast, accurate, quiet autofocus; full-time manual override
Advanced optical design
Compatible with all L-mount cameras

Versatile Wide-Angle Zoom. The Panasonic 16-35mm f/4 S PRO covers a versatile, popular range of focal lengths that makes it great for landscapes, cityscapes, and large group shots, among other applications. Using an APS-C camera? You’ll get a 24-52.5mm equivalent focal-length range.

L-Mount Alliance. This wide-diameter lens mount is a joint collaboration between Leica, Panasonic, and Sigma that’s focused on a line of premium cameras and lenses in a mirrorless format. At 51.6mm mount diameter and just 20mm flange distance, the L-mount is well-suited for fast-aperture full-frame optics with compact dimensions.

Linear Motor Autofocus System. This lens’s autofocus system uses a linear motor to provide fast, accurate, nearly silent autofocus performance for still and video use. There’s a focus clutch mechanism that allows for almost instant AF/MF switching.

Constant f/4 Aperture. The constant f/4 maximum aperture gives you consistent illumination throughout the lens’s zoom range. The rounded nine-blade diaphragm contributes to a pleasing bokeh quality.

Advanced Optics. The nine-group/twelve-element optical formula includes three aspherical elements, one ultra-high refractive index element, and one extra-low dispersion element to reduce chromatic aberrations and distortion.', 2100000.0, '{"Angle of View": "107° to 63°", "Aperture Blades": "9, Rounded", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Diameter": "3.3\\"", "Extra Low-Dispersion Elements": "1", "Groups/Elements": "9/12", "Hood Included": "Yes", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "L", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle", "Maximum Magnification": "0.23x", "Mfr. Model Number": "S-R1635", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "0.8’", "Ultra High-Refractive Index Elements": "1"}', 'Includes

