	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1257, 2, 44, 'Panasonic Leica 8-18mm f/2.8-4 ASPH', 'panasonic-leica-8-18mm-f-2-8-4-asph', 'The Panasonic Leica 8-18mm f/2.8-4 DG Vario-Elmarit ASPH is a wide-angle zoom designed for the Micro 4/3 system. Key features include:

High-quality optics for sharp, clear images
16-36mm focal length (35mm equivalent)
Fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus system
Splash-, dust-, and freezeproof metal build

Wide-Angle Zoom. With a focal length equivalent to 16-36mm after crop factor, the compact and lightweight Panasonic Leica 8-18mm f/2.8-4 DG Vario-Elmarit ASPH is great for a range of everyday-shooting applications, such as landscapes and street photography.

High-Quality Optics. The Leica influence shows in this lens’s optics. The 8-18’s ten-group/fifteen-element design features one aspherical extra-low dispersion element, three aspherical elements, two extra-low dispersion elements, and one ultra high-refractive index element to drastically reduce color fringing, and chromatic and spherical aberrations throughout the zoom range while keeping your images clear, sharp, and color-accurate.

Fast 240 fps Autofocus. This lens’s extremely fast 240 fps autofocus drive provides accurate, nearly silent performance for still images and videos alike.

High-Quality Build. The 8-18mm’s high-quality splash-, dust-, and freezeproof metal build gives you peace of mind when shooting in adverse conditions.', 1475000.0, '{"Angle of View": "107-62°", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Groups/Elements": "10/15", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Micro 4/3", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle", "Magnification": "0.12x", "Mfr. Model Number": "H-E08018"}', 'Includes

	8-18mm lens
	Front & rear caps
	H-E08018 hood
	67mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1258, 2, 44, 'Panasonic Leica 9mm f/1.7 ASPH DG Summilux', 'panasonic-leica-9mm-f-1-7-asph-dg-summilux', 'The Panasonic Leica 9mm f/1.7 ASPH DG Summilux is a half-macro wide-angle prime designed for Micro 4/3 cameras. Key features include:

Excellent for cityscapes, landscapes, and close-ups
High-quality optical formula for maximum sharpness
Fast, accurate, and nearly silent autofocus system
Compatible with micro-step aperture control

Half-Macro Wide-Angle Prime. The Panasonic Leica 9mm f/1.7 ASPH DG Summilux’s 18mm equivalent focal length makes it great for cityscapes and landscapes, while its fast f/1.7 constant maximum aperture and rounded 7-blade diaphragm give you excellent depth-of-field control and low-light performance. Its 3.7-inch minimum focusing distance and 0.25x maximum magnification mean it’s exceptional for capturing subjects at a very close range.

Advanced Optical Design. The nine-group/twelve-element optical formula includes two aspherical elements, two extra-low dispersion elements, and one ultra high-refractive index element to increase clarity and sharpness while reducing chromatic aberrations, color fringing, and distortion.

High-Speed Autofocus System. A linear autofocus motor provides fast, accurate, nearly silent performance for still and video use. This autofocus system is compatible with Lumix cameras’ high-speed contrast-detection autofocus systems for speeds up to 240 fps. A focus-clutch mechanism lets you easily and quickly switch between autofocus and manual focusing.

High-Quality Build. The 9mm’s high-quality splash-, dust-, and freezeproof metal build gives you peace of mind when shooting in adverse conditions. It’s compatible with micro-step aperture control, which gives you smooth exposure changes when recording video.', 900000.0, '{"Angle of View": "100°", "Aperture Blades": "7, Rounded", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Hood Included": "Yes", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Micro 4/3", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle", "Maximum Magnification": "0.25x", "Mfr. Model Number": "H-X09", "Optical Design": "Groups/Elements9/12Aspherical Elements2Extra-Low Dispersion Elements2Ultra High-Refractive Index Elements1", "Physical": "Dimensions (ø x L)2.4 × 2″Weight0.3 lb."}', 'Includes

	Panasonic 9mm f/1.7
	55mm protective filter
	Front & rear caps
	Hood', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1259, 2, 44, 'Panasonic Lumix 14-28mm f/4-5.6 Macro', 'panasonic-lumix-14-28mm-f-4-5-6-macro', 'The Panasonic Lumix 14-28mm f/4-5.6 Macro is a versatile ultra-wide macro zoom for L-mount mirrorless cameras. Key features include:

1:2 to 1:4 magnification ratio
5.9-inch minimum focusing distance
Micro-step aperture control; fast, accurate autofocus
Compatible with all L-mount cameras

Versatile Ultra-Wide Macro Zoom. The Panasonic Lumix 14-28mm f/4-5.6 Macro’s 5.9-inch minimum focusing distance and 1:2 to 1:4 magnification ratio make it great for capturing close-up subjects, while its ultra-wide zoom range is well-suited for capturing landscapes, cityscapes, street scenes, and architecture. Its f/4.5-5.6 aperture is plenty fast for daytime use, but you probably won’t want to shoot too much in low light with this lens. A rounded seven-blade diaphragm helps produce pleasing bokeh, and micro-step aperture control gives you smooth exposure changes and pro-quality videos.

L-Mount Alliance. This ultra-wide lens mount is a joint collaboration between Leica, Panasonic, and Sigma that’s focused on a line of premium cameras & lenses in a mirrorless format. At 51.6mm mount diameter and just 20mm flange distance, the L-mount is well-suited for fast-aperture full-frame optics with compact dimensions.

Advanced Optical Design. The ten-group/fourteen-element optical formula includes one aspherical Extra-Low Dispersion element, one aspherical element, three Extra-Low Dispersion elements, and one Ultra High Refractive Index element to reduce chromatic aberrations and distortion while delivering beautiful, color-accurate images across the zoom range.

Fast, Accurate Autofocus. The motor provides fast, accurate, nearly silent autofocus performance for still and video use, and Panasonic claims the autofocus system supports frame rates up to 240 fps. You can use the AF/MF switch to easily toggle between autofocus and manual focus modes.

Durable Build. This lens’s dust- and splash-resistant build makes it usable in inclement conditions. A fluorine coating on the front lens elements protects it from debris and smearing.', 1300000.0, '{"Angle of View": "114-75°", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Dimensions": "3.3 × 3.5″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "77.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "14-28", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "10/14", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "L", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle, Macro, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "4.0", "Maximum Magnification": "0.5x", "Mfr. Model Number": "S-R1428", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "6\\"", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "0.76 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Panasonic Lumix 14-28mm f/4-5.6 Macro
	Front & rear caps
	Hood
	77mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1260, 1, 44, 'Panasonic Lumix BS1H Full-Frame Cinema Camera', 'panasonic-lumix-bs1h-full-frame-cinema-camera', 'The Panasonic Lumix BS1H Full-Frame Cinema Camera is a pro-grade box-style video-only camera for the L-mount system and an even more video focused counterpart of the DC-S1H. Key features include:

24.2 MP, full-frame MOS sensor with native L-Mount
Up to 5.9K H.264/H.265/HEVC recording to UHS-II SD cards
Dual Native ISO base sensitivity 100/640, extended ISO up to 51,200/204,800
Netflix approved camera

What’s In The Box? The DC-S1H is a hybrid photo/video mirrorless camera, and this Panasonic Lumix BS1H Full-Frame Cinema Camera comes equipped with all the same video features of the S1H, in a more compact, box-style camera housing that can be conveniently mounted on gimbals and hard to reach places. Please note, the BS1H does not have a built-in interface and will require an external monitoring solution in order to access camera settings.

PoE+, and Other Power Options. In addition to the included AC adapter, the BS1H can be powered by separately available batteries like the Panasonic AG-VBR118G High Capacity Battery, and you can pick up a dual charger here. The camera also supports Power-over-Ethernet, which allows for power and remote control for up to 12 BS1H cameras and streaming over a single cat6 or better cable.

24.2 MP, Full-Frame Sensor. The BS1H features a 24.2 MP full-frame sensor with a native ISO sensitivity up to 51,200. Using software, however, the camera can support dual native ISO 50 to 204,800, which extends the dynamic range in more shooting situations, especially when paired with the camera’s preinstalled V-Log L.

DCI 4K At 60 Frames Per Second. Options for DCI and UHD 4K are included here. The camera supports 4K/60p in 4:2:0 10-bit, and can even reach 6K and anamorphic 4K recording. High frame rate shooting is available at up to 240 fps in 1080p.

V-Log Installed. Panasonic did everyone a solid and decided to preinstall V-Log and V-Gamut on all copies of this camera, and it’s compatible with the “Cinema VariCam Look” as well. This provides an extremely flat gamma curve and image that’s capable of 14-stops of dynamic range for additional latitude when grading your footage. The BS1H supports outputting RAW over HDMI and video over SDI simultaneously.

Timecode In/Out.  BNC Timecode and Genlock ports allow for professional time code and sync options without the need for adapters. RJ45 Gigabit LAN also allows for network syncing.

Need a Memory Card? You’ll need an ultra-fast memory card for a camera this powerful, and we recommend the Sony 128GB SF-G Tough Series UHS-II SDXC. This camera can take full advantage of its superior 299 MB/s max write speed and 300 MB/s max read speed for high-resolution, high-bitrate capture.', 4050000.0, '{"Brand": "Panasonic", "Camera Mount": "L", "Camera Type": "Cinema", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Imaging": "SensorType: Live MOSSize: 35.6 × 23.8 mmEffective Pixels24.2MPISODynamic Range: Up to 14 stopsDefault Sensitivity: 100 – 51,200Expanded Sensitivity: 80 – 204,800", "Inputs/Outputs": "Audio InputsMic In (3.5mm stereo mini jack)Audio OutputsHeadphones Out (3.5mm stereo mini jack)Video OutputsHDMI Type-A3G-SDI BNCAdditional Inputs/OutputsRemote: 2.5mm LANCTimecode In/Out: BNCGenlock In: BNC, BBS signal / tri-level syncLAN: RJ-45 / PoE+USB: 3.1 GEN1 Type-C", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Physical": "Dimensions3.7 × 3.7 × 3.1″Weight1.3 lb", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Stabilization": "No", "Video Format": "Resolution @ framrate4096 × 2160p at 23.98, 24, 25, 29.97 fps3840 × 2160p at 23.98, 24, 25, 29.97 fps3328 × 2496p at 23.98, 24, 25, 29.97 fps1920 × 1080p at 23.98, 24, 25, 29.97 fps", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

	LUMIX BS1H camera
	Camera body cap
	AC adapter
	Non-polarized cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1261, 1, 44, 'Panasonic Lumix DC-FZ1000 II', 'panasonic-lumix-dc-fz1000-ii', 'The Panasonic Lumix DC-FZ1000 II is a large-sensor, point-and-shoot bridge camera and an update to the original DMC-FZ1000. Key features include:

4K video and still capture
20.1MP 1-inch high-sensitivity MOS sensor
16x Leica DC Vario-Elmarit zoom
Built-in HYBRID OIS image stabilization

What’s Changed? Compared to its predecessor, the Panasonic Lumix DC-FZ1000 II features a higher-resolution rear LCD with added touchscreen functionality, easy USB charging, and Bluetooth support.

Large Sensor. The 20.1MP 1.0-inch high-sensitivity MOS sensor lets you capture high-quality images and video at higher ISOs. The large sensor and image processor come together to provide great high-speed performance, letting you shoot continuously at up to 12 fps with single-shot AF, 30 fps at 8MP in 4K PHOTO modes, and UHD 4K video recording at 30p. Its Level Shot function automatically detects horizontal lines within an image and keeps it level while you’re shooting.

16x Leica DC Vario-Elmarit Zoom. The integrated lens offers a 25-400mm f/2.8-4 equivalent focal length that covers the wide to super telephoto range. The relatively fast f/2.8-4 variable aperture gives you the flexibility to shoot in low light when needed, as well as limited subject/background isolation.

Five-Axis HYBRID Optical Image Stabilization. This optical image stabilizer offers correction on five different axes, making the somewhat limited f/4 aperture at 400mm much more useful.

4K Video. Rather than just including video to appease the masses, the FZ1000 II features class-leading 4K QFHD video capture at 30p with a high bit rate of 100Mbps in MP4 format. Additionally, it shoots Full HD 1080 video at 60p, 30p, 24p, or 60i in AVCHD. There’s a built-in stereo zoom mic for capturing in-camera AAC or Dolby audio, and a 3.5mm input for connecting an external mic. Please note that 4K capture requires the use of a UHS Speed Class 3 memory card, such as the SanDisk SDXC 256GB Extreme Pro 170MB/s UHS-1 U3.

4K Photo. The 4K PHOTO modes give you three options for taking 8MP stills at 30 fps: 4K Burst mode lets you continuously record the images for up to 15 minutes, giving you a fast frame rate to capture the best moment; 4K Pre-Burst mode records the images one second before and one second after you press the shutter button, giving you 60 frames to choose from; and 4K Burst mode lets you play back your video, pause it at any moment you choose, and pretty the shutter button to save the selected frame as a still. The 4K PHOTO modes also let you produce stromotion images, which combine sequential exposures into one frame for a dynamic look.

Light-Speed Autofocus. Bridge cameras aren’t typically known for their autofocus performance, but the FZ1000 II has a little help from the company’s flagship GH4. Not only does it use the same image processor as the GH4, but it also inherits the LUMIX DFD (Depth From Defocus) technology. This, in combination with the high speed linear AF motor, provides near-instantaneous focus with extreme accuracy.

Other Notable Features. The FZ1000 II offers two methods to compose and view images: the 0.39-inch 2.36k-dot OLED electronic viewfinder and the 3.0-inch 1.24m-dot free-angle rear touchscreen LCD. Both methods offer 100% framing accuracy and anti-reflective coatings for uninhibited performance in bright lighting conditions. Built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth connectivity enable wireless image transfer and remote operation with a smartphone, and there’s a wide variety of Creative Control, Scene, and Photo Style modes for in-camera capture. The included DMW-BLC12PP battery is rated for up to 250 shots per charge, while images and video are recorded to SDHC/XC memory cards.', 1400000.0, '{"Aspect Ratio": "1:1, 3:2, 4:3, 16:9", "Audio Recording": "Built-In Mic: With Video (Stereo)\\nOptional External Mic: With Video (Stereo)", "Battery": "1x Rechargeable Lithium-Ion Battery Pack, 7.2 VDC, 1200 mAh", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Built-in Flash": "Yes", "Camera Type": "Compact", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Connectivity": "HDMI D (Micro), USB 2.0 Micro-B", "Continuous Shooting": "Up to 12 fps at 20.1 MP\\nUp to 7 fps at 20.3 MP\\nUp to 2 fps at 20.3 MP\\nUp to 30 fps at 8 MP", "Dimensions": "W x H x D: 5.4″ × 3.8″ × 5.2″", "Exposure Modes": "Modes: Aperture Priority, Manual, Program, Shutter Priority\\n\\nCompensation: -5 EV to +5 EV (in 1/3 EV Steps)", "External Flash Connection": "Hot Shoe", "File Format": "Still Images: JPEG, RAW\\nMovies: AVCHD 2.0, MP4\\nAudio: AAC, Dolby Digital 2ch", "Flash Modes": "Auto\\nAuto/Red-Eye Reduction\\nFirst-Curtain Sync\\nForced On\\nForced On/Red-Eye Reduction\\nOff\\nSecond-Curtain Sync\\nSlow Sync\\nSlow Sync/Red-Eye Reduction", "Focus Range": "Wide: 0.98’ to Infinity / 30 cm to Infinity\\n\\nTelephoto: 3.28’ to Infinity / 1 m to Infinity\\n\\nWide Macro: 1.18\\" to Infinity / 3 cm to Infinity", "Interval Recording": "Yes", "Item Type": "Camera", "LCD": "3.0\\" LCD Rear Touchscreen Swivel (1,240,000 Pixels)", "LCD Coverage": "100%", "Lens": "Leica DC Vario-Elmarit, 15 Elements in 11 Groups\\n\\n5 Aspherical, 4 ED\\n\\nEffective Focal Length: 9.1 to 146mm (35 mm Equivalent: 27 to 432mm)\\n\\nAperture: f/2.8 (W) to f/4 (T) to f/11", "Maximum Resolution": "4864 × 3648", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Pixels": "Actual: 20.9 Megapixel\\nEffective: 20.1 Megapixel", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Self Timer": "2, 10 Sec", "Sensor": "1\\" MOS", "Sensor Size": "1-Inch", "Shutter Speed": "Type: Mechanical\\nSpeed: 60 to 1/4000 Second\\n\\nType: Electronic\\nSpeed: 1 to 1/16000 Second\\n120 to 0 Second in Bulb Mode", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Video Clip Length": "Up to 29 Minutes 59 Seconds", "Video Recording": "Yes, NTSC", "Video Resolution": "3840 × 2160p: 29.97 fps, 24 fps\\n\\n1920 × 1080p: 120 fps, 59.94 fps, 29.97 fps, 24 fps\\n\\n1920 × 1080i: 59.94 fps\\n\\n1280 × 720p: 30 fps", "Viewfinder Coverage": "100%", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "Weather Sealing": "No", "White Balance": "Auto, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Daylight, Flash, Incandescent, Shade, White Set 1, White Set 2, White Set 3, White Set 4", "Wi-Fi": "Yes, Wi-Fi 4 (802.11n) Built In", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth", "Zoom": "Optical: 16x\\nExtra Optical Zoom (EZ): 22.4x\\nExtra Optical Zoom (EZ): 32x\\nIntelligent Zoom: 32x\\nDigital: 4x"}', 'Includes

	Panasonic Lumix DC-FZ1000 II
	Leica 25-400mm for FZ1000 Hood
	Protective Hoya EVO Antistatic 62mm	FIlter
	Panasonic DMW-BLC12PP Battery
	Type-A 1-Port Panasonic USB Charger
	USB 2.0 A Male to Micro B Cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1262, 1, 44, 'Panasonic Lumix DC-G100D', 'panasonic-lumix-dc-g100d', 'The Panasonic Lumix DC-G100D is a Micro 4/3 mount mirrorless camera with a feature set designed for multimedia content creators. Key features include:

Designed for vloggers and multimedia content creators
20.3MP Digital Live CMOS sensor and Venus Engine
Five-axis sensor-shift image stabilization
Nokia OZO audio with subject tracking

Made for Vloggers and Content Creators. The Panasonic Lumix DC-G100D has a range of specialized features designed for vloggers and other multimedia content creators. Its 3.0-inch vari-angle touchscreen LCD and Dedicated Video Selfie Mode make framing and taking selfies almost effortless; its five-axis sensor-shift image stabilization system compensates for camera shake when walking or moving; its 20.3MP MOS sensor and Venus engine produce crisp, detailed stills and UHD 4K30p video; its three built-in microphones capture optimized OZO audio with subject tracking; integrated Wi-Fi and Bluetooth let you quickly and easily share photos and videos, and control the camera; and its compact, lightweight design makes it ideal for shooting on the go.

20.3MP Digital Live CMOS Sensor and Venus Engine. This 20.3-megapixel Micro 4/3 sensor pairs with the updated Venus Engine to deliver sharp, detailed images with high sensitivity, low noise, accurate color reproduction, and quick response times. You get maximum resolution with minimum noise, with an ISO range that tops out at 25600.

UHD 4K Video. You can record UHD 4K video at 24p or 30p at a 100 Mbps bitrate with an 8-bit color depth and 4:2:0 sampling while recording internally. You can also record video externally via the micro-HDMI with 8-bit color depth and 4:2:2 sampling. The DC-G100D comes with V-Log L pre-installed, which will capture a flat, neutral gamma curve that’s well-suited for grading. A dedicated Video Selfie Mode optimizes depth of field and uses Face Detection AF and AE settings to highlight your main subject while also configuring the sound pickup range to best capture audio from your subject. You can use 4x and 2x slow-motion and 8x, 4x, and 2x quick-motion settings with Full HD recording, there are time-lapse and stop-motion video settings, and you get a 3.5mm input for capturing audio with an external mic.

Vlogging-Friendly UI. The DC-G100D’s updated UI was designed specifically for vloggers. Its REC Frame Indicator puts a red border around the image frame while you’re recording. You can use the Frame Marker overlay to highlight which portion of the frame will be displayed in a selected aspect ratio, making it a great tool for direct output to different social-media platforms.

Dual Image Stabilization. The G100D has a built-in five-axis hybrid image stabilization system to help keep your images clear and sharp when you’re walking, riding, or just working in low light. The in-camera stabilization can also be paired with select lens-based image stabilization systems to make sure your shots are steady and rock solid.

4K Photo Modes. While the DC-G100D is purpose-built for vlogging, it also includes three still-shooting modes that use its video-recording capability to capture 8MP stills at a 30fps shooting rate. Burst mode lets you continuously record, Pre-Burst mode records images one second before and one second after you press the shutter button so you get 60 frames to choose from, while Burst (S/S) mode lets you select the frame you want from recorded video footage.

Depth From Defocus Autofocus System. Depth From Defocus is a fancy way of saying the DC-G100D uses contrast detection to acquire focus in conditions down to -4EV. There’s subject-tracking continuous focus for keeping up with moving subjects and face/eye detection capabilities for making portraiture easier. You also get full-time manual-focus override.

Post Focus and Focus Stacking. Post Focus records images as 4K MP4 files at 30 fps and gives you a selection of focus ranges to choose from. During playback, you can use the touchscreen to tap the specific area of the image you want to be in focus, and the camera will create an 8MP JPEG. The Focus-Stacking feature generates images with different points of focus and combines them to produce an extended depth of field.

Nokia OZO Audio. The G100D incorporates Nokia’s OZO audio technology, which uses the three built-in mics to record spatial audio recording with improved richness and accuracy based on the location of the sound. You can manually or automatically configure the mics, and the Tracking setting works with the detected angle of view to deliver crystal-clear audio, making it great for selfie videos, interviews, and the like.

Viewfinder and Touchscreen. The large OLED live viewfinder has a 2.36m-dot resolution and 0.74x magnification that’s great for easy eye-level composition. You can use the 3.0-inch, 1.84m-dot rear touchscreen LCD for image composition, review, playback, and menu navigation. Its free-tilting and swiveling design lets you work from low and high angles, even when you’re shooting in vertical orientation, and you can set the camera’s Video Selfie Mode to automatically start once you rotate the screen forward.

Other Notable Features. Built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth connectivity enables wireless image transfer and remote camera operation, and a dedicated Send Images button on the camera’s top plate lets you instantly share images. The DC-G100D is powered by the DMW-BLG10 battery, which is rated for up to 270 shots per charge with the rear LCD, up to 250 shots per charge with the LVF, or roughly 900 shots per charge when you’re using Power Save LVF mode. You can charge the battery in-camera via USB or with AC power. The G100D records to SDHC/XC memory cards via its single card slot, and it fully supports U3 cards for 4K capture. The magnesium-alloy camera body is weather sealed against the elements.', 1250000.0, '{"Brand": "Panasonic", "Camera Mount": "Micro 4/3", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Environmental": "Operating Temperature32 to 104°F / 0 to 40°COperating Humidity10 to 80%", "Exposure Control": "Shutter TypeMechanical Focal Plane Shutter, Electronic Rolling ShutterShutter Speed – Electronic Front Curtain Shutter1/500 to 60 SecondsShutter Speed – Electronic Shutter1/16000 to 1 Second1/16000 to 1/25 Second in Movie ModeBulb/Time ModeBulb Mode, Time ModeISO Sensitivity Range – Photo200 to 25,600 (Extended: 100 to 25,600)ISO Sensitivity Range – Video200 to 6400Metering MethodCenter-Weighted Average, Multiple, SpotPrecise Scan-Rate ControlNoExposure ModesAperture Priority, Auto, Manual, Program, Shutter PriorityWhite-Balance PresetsAuto, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Daylight, Flash, Incandescent, Shade, White Set 1, White Set 2, White Set 3, White Set 4Continuous Shooting – Electronic ShutterUp to 10 fps for up to 20 Frames (RAW) / 480 Frames (JPEG)Interval RecordingYesSelf-Timer2/10-Second Delay", "Flash": "Built-In Flash/LightYes, Flash OnlyMaximum Sync Speed1/50 SecondDedicated Flash SystemTTLExternal Flash ConnectionShoe Mount", "Focus": "Focus TypeAuto and Manual FocusFocus ModesAutomatic, Continuous-Servo AF, Flexible, Manual FocusAutofocus PointsContrast Detection: 49", "General": "Battery Type1x DMW-BLG10PP Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 7.2 VDC, 1025 mAh (Approx. 270 Shots)Shoe Mount1x Hot ShoeTripod Mounting Thread1x 1/4\\"-20 Female (Bottom)Dimensions (W x H x D)4.55 × 3.25 × 2.13″ / 115.6 × 82.5 × 54.2mm (Without Protrusions)Weight0.7 lb. / 12.42 oz / 352 g (With Battery, Recording Media)", "Imaging": "Sensor ResolutionActual: 21.77 MegapixelEffective: 20.3 Megapixel (5184 × 3888)Sensor Dimensions17.3 × 13mm (Four Thirds) MOSSensor Crop (35mm Equivalent)Crop Factor: 2xImage StabilizationDigital, 5-AxisBuilt-In ND FilterNoCapture TypeStills & Video", "Interface": "Media/Memory Card Slot1x SD/SDHC/SDXC (UHS-II)Video I/O1x Micro-HDMI (Unspecified Signal) OutputAudio I/O1x 1/8\\" / 3.5mm TRS Stereo Microphone InputPower I/O1x USB-C Input/OutputOther I/O1x USB-C Input/Output (Shared with Power Input)WirelessWi-Fi 4 (802.11n), Bluetooth 4.2Mobile App CompatibleYes: Android & iOSApp Name: Panasonic LUMIX SyncFunctionality: Access Stored Files, Remote ControlGlobal Positioning (GPS, GLONASS, etc.)GPS, via connected smartphone", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Mfr. Model Number": "DC-G100DKK", "Monitor": "Display Size3.0\\"Resolution1,840,000 DotDisplay TypeArticulating Touchscreen LCD", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Sensor Size": "Micro 4/3", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Video Capture": "Internal Recording Modes – MP4 4:2:0 8-BitUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.98/29.97 fps1920 × 1080p at 29.97/59.94 fpsExternal Recording Modes – 4:2:2 8-Bit via HDMI1920 × 1080Fast-/Slow-Motion SupportYesRecording LimitUp to 10 Minutes in 4KUp to 30 Minutes in 1080pBroadcast OutputNTSCIP StreamingNoBuilt-In Microphone TypeStereoAudio RecordingAAC Audio", "Viewfinder": "TypeBuilt-In Electronic (OLED)Resolution2,360,000 DotEye Point20mmCoverage100%MagnificationApprox. 0.74x", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

	Panasonic Lumix G100D
	Panasonic DMW-BLG10 battery
	Panasonic Type-A 5V / 1A 1-Port USB charger
	USB 2.0 A Male to Type C cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
