INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1264, 1, 44, 'Panasonic Lumix DC-S1H', 'panasonic-lumix-dc-s1h', 'The Panasonic Lumix DC-S1H is a well-rounded and durable camera that offers advanced feature sets for stills and video. Key features include:

6K24p, DCI 4K, and 4K UHD video capture
24.2MP full-frame CMOS sensor and Venus Engine
Five-axis sensor-shift image stabilization
Netflix-approved camera

24.2MP Full-Frame CMOS Sensor and Venus Engine. The Panasonic Lumix DC-S1H’s 24.2MP MOS sensor is supported by an updated Venus Engine for impressive image quality, a fast 9 fps continuous shooting rate with AF-S, a 6 fps continuous shooting rate with AF-C, great low-light performance, and a 100-51,200 ISO range. The sensor and processor combine to enhance color reproduction and suppress noise levels throughout the camera’s sensitivity range.

L-Mount Alliance. This wide-diameter lens mount is a joint collaboration between Leica, Panasonic, and Sigma that’s focused on a line of premium cameras & lenses in a mirrorless format. At 51.6mm mount diameter and just 20mm flange distance, the L-mount is well-suited for fast-aperture full-frame optics with compact dimensions.

6K24p, DCI 4K, and 4K UHD Video. The Lumix S1H offers 6K24p capture, 16:9 5.9:30p, and both DCI and UHD 4K60p internal recording with 4:2:2 10-bit color in MP4 format with a 1.09x crop (via pixel binning). It’s also capable of Full HD 1080p capture at 119.88p and Anamorphic 4K at 48.00p. It features clean HDMI output to an external recorder, a built-in stereo mic for quick audio capture, and 3.5mm mic and headphone jacks for advanced audio recording and monitoring needs. Please note that for 6K and 4K capture, you must use an SD memory card that’s UHS-I Class 3 or faster, like the Sony 128GB SF-G Tough Series UHS-II SDXC.

Post-Production Optimization. The S1H has a pair of gamma settings suited to capturing a wide dynamic range. This camera comes with V-Log pre-installed. It lets you capture a flat, neutral gamma curve that’s well-suited for grading. You can use the High Dynamic Range mode and Hybrid Log Gamma to record greater shadow and highlight details.

6K and 4K Photo. The DC-S1H gives you three still-shooting modes for recording continuous 3:2 or 4:3 8MP stills at a 60 or 30 fps shooting rate or 18MP stills at a 30 fps shooting rate. Burst mode lets you continuously record, Pre-Burst mode records images one second before and one second after you press the shutter button so you get 60 frames to choose from, while Burst (S/S) mode lets you select the frame you want from recorded video footage. This camera can also record stills in 65:24 and 2:1 panoramic formats.

Light-Speed Autofocus. This contrast-based autofocus system uses Panasonic’s “Depth from Defocus” technology to provide extremely fast speeds. “Advanced AI technology” assists in subject tracking of fast-moving subjects, while the same AI system is used when shooting portraits for face/eye detection. And if you’re shooting in low light, the DFD autofocus system works down to -6 EV. You also get full-time manual focusing for added precision.

Sensor-Shift Image Stabilization. This system uses five-axis sensor-shift stabilization for up to six stops of correction. Mate the camera with a Panasonic lens that features Dual IS 2 (a lens-based two-axis stabilization) to compensate for roughly 6.5 stops of camera shake, giving your hand-held shots utmost sharpness. Its High Resolution mode captures and compiles 8 separate exposures into a single 96MP RAW or JPEG file at 12000 × 8000 pixel resolution, but your subject must be static and the camera must be locked down on a tripod.

Built-In Electronic Viewfinder. The 5.76m-dot OLED integrated electronic viewfinder offers 100% coverage and encompasses the entire Adobe RGB color space, allowing extremely faithful color reproduction. It offers 0.78x configurable viewing magnification and a smooth 60 fps or 120 fps changeable refresh rate, 0.005-second lag, and 10,000:1 contrast ratio.

Rear and Top LCDs. You can use the 2.3m-dot 3.2-inch rear touchscreen LCD for image composition, review, playback, and menu navigation. Its free-tilting design lets you work from low and high angles, even when you’re shooting in vertical orientation. Live View Boost mode was designed for composing images in low light, while Night Mode also helps you work in the dark by lowering the backlight intensity. A separate status LCD on top of the camera lets you quickly review shooting settings, even when the camera’s powered off.

Other Notable Features. The built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth provide wireless control and viewing options via the free Lumix Sync App. Images are recorded to SDHC/XC memory cards (remember, UHS-I Class 3 or faster for 6K and 4K video), and the rechargeable DMW-BLJ31 battery is rated for approximately 400 shots per charge when using the rear monitor, 380 shots per charge when using the EVF, and 1150 shots per charge when Power Save LVF mode is on.', 4175000.0, '{"Aspect Ratio": "1:1, 2:1, 3:2, 4:3, 16:9, 65:24", "Audio File Formats": "AAC, Dolby Digital 2ch, Linear PCM (Stereo)", "Audio Recording": "Built-In Microphone (Stereo)\\nExternal Microphone Input (Stereo)", "Autofocus Points": "Contrast Detection: 225", "Autofocus Sensitivity": "-6 to +20 EV", "Battery": "1x DMW-BLJ31 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 7.4 VDC, 3050 mAh (Approx. 400 Shots)", "Bit Depth": "14-Bit", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Built-in Flash": "No", "Camera Mount": "L", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Continuous Shooting": "Up to 9 fps at 24.2 MP for up to 60 Exposures (RAW)\\nUp to 9 fps at 24.2 MP for up to 999 Exposures (JPEG)\\nUp to 30 fps at 18 MP\\nUp to 60 fps at 8 MP", "Dedicated Flash System": "TTL", "Depth": "4.4\\"", "Diopter Adjustment": "-4 to +2", "Exposure Compensation": "-5 to +5 EV (1/3 EV Steps)", "Exposure Modes": "Aperture Priority, Manual, Program, Shutter Priority", "External Flash Connection": "Hot Shoe, PC Terminal", "External Video-Recording Modes": "4:2:2 10-Bit\\nDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) up to 24.00p/50p/59.94p\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) up to 24.00p/50p/59.94p", "Flash Compensation": "-3 to +3 EV (1/3 EV Steps)", "Flash Modes": "Auto, Auto/Red-Eye Reduction, Forced On, Forced On/Red-Eye Reduction, Off, Slow Sync, Slow Sync/Red-Eye Reduction", "Focus Type": "Auto and Manual Focus", "Focusing Method": "Continuous-Servo AF, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AF", "GPS": "No", "Height": "4.5\\"", "Image File Formats": "JPEG, RAW", "Inputs/Outputs": "USB Type-C (USB 3.1), 3.5mm Microphone, 3.5mm Headphone, HDMI A (Full Size), X-Sync Socket, 2.5mm Sub-Mini", "Interval Recording": "Yes", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Resolution": "6000 × 4000", "Maximum Sync Speed": "1/320 Second", "Maximum Video Resolution": "6K", "Memory Card Slot": "Dual Slot: SD/SDHC/SDXC (UHS-II)", "Metering Range": "0 to 18 EV", "Monitor Resolution": "2,330,000 Dot", "Monitor Size": "3.2\\"", "Monitor Type": "Free-Angle Tilting Touchscreen LCD", "Operating Temperature": "14 to 104°F / -10 to 40°C", "Pixels": "Actual: 25.28 Megapixel\\nEffective: 24.2 Megapixel", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Self Timer": "2/10-Second Delay", "Sensor Dimensions": "35.6 × 23.8mm", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Sensor Type": "CMOS", "Shutter Speed": "Mechanical Shutter\\n1/8000 to 60 Second\\n0 to 30 Minute in Bulb Mode\\n\\nElectronic Front Curtain Shutter\\n1/2000 to 60 Second\\n0 to 30 Minute in Bulb Mode\\n\\nElectronic Shutter\\n1/8000 to 60 Second\\n0 to 60 Second in Bulb Mode\\n1/16000 to 1/125 Second in Movie Mode", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Video Encoding": "NTSC/PAL", "Video Recording Modes": "MOV/H.265 4:2:0 10-Bit\\n6K 3:2 (5952 × 3968) at 23.976p/24.00p [200 Mb/s]\\n5.4K 3:2 (5376 × 3584) at 25p/29.97p [200 Mb/s]\\n5.9K (5888 × 3312) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p [200 Mb/s]\\nDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) at 47.95p/48.00p/50p/59.94p [200 Mb/s]\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 47.95p/48.00p/50p/59.94p [200 Mb/s]\\n4K Anamorphic (3328 × 2496) at 47.95p/48.00p/50p [200 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 47.95p/48.00p/100p/119.88p [100 to 150 Mb/s]\\n\\nMOV/H.264 4:2:2 10-Bit\\nDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p [150 to 400 Mb/s]\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p [150 to 400 Mb/s]\\n4K Anamorphic (3328 × 2496) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p [150 to 400 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p/50i/50p/59.94i/59.94p [50 to 200 Mb/s]\\n\\nMOV/H.264 4:2:0 8-Bit\\nDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [100 to 150 Mb/s]\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [100 to 150 Mb/s]\\n4K Anamorphic (3328 × 2496) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p/50p [100 to 150 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.976p/24.00p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [100 Mb/s]\\n\\nMP4/H.265 4:2:0 10-Bit\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [72 to 100 Mb/s]\\n\\nMP4/H.264 4:2:0 8-Bit\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [100 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [20 to 28 Mb/s]\\n\\nAVCHD 4:2:0 8-Bit\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.976p/50i/50p/59.94i/59.94p [17 to 28 Mb/s]", "Viewfinder Coverage": "100%", "Viewfinder Eye Point": "21mm", "Viewfinder Magnification": "Approx. 0.78x", "Viewfinder Resolution": "5,760,000 Dot", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "White Balance": "Auto, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Daylight, Flash, Incandescent, Shade, White Set 1, White Set 2, White Set 3, White Set 4", "Width": "5.9", "Wireless": "Bluetooth, Wi-Fi", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

	Panasonic Lumix DC-S1H
	3-foot USB 3.1 Type-C to Type-C cable
	DMW-BLJ31 battery
	DMW-BTC14 charger
	DVLV1001Z USB AC adapter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1265, 1, 44, 'Panasonic Lumix DC-S1R II', 'panasonic-lumix-dc-s1r-ii', 'The Panasonic S1R II is a high-resolution, full-frame, L-mount hybrid camera aimed at pro photographers who need advanced video options. It is the update of the popular DC-S1R. Key features include:

6.4K open gate, 8K30p and 4K120p 10-bit recording
8-stop, 5-axis IBIS and cropless Active IS
40 frames per second, 80-102,400 ISO
25% lighter and about 3% smaller than S1R

Lumix’s First 8K Hybrid Camera. This flagship camera represents the Lumix line’s entry into 8K video, in addition to open gate 6.4K and 4K120p. Other headline advancements include internal ProRes RAW recording, 14 stops of dynamic range, 40 fps burst shooting, and 177 megapixel image capture in sensor-shift High Resolution mode. This is truly a something-for-everyone camera. For a version of this camera that shoots open gate 6K with faster readout speeds and a burst up to 70 frames per second, check out the S1 II.

What’s Changed? The S1R II is smaller and lighter than the DC-S1R and offers unlimited RAW video, a higher max ISO, much faster burst shooting, a boost in stabilization, and increased battery life (doubled when paired with the DMW-BG2 Battery Grip). Flash photographers will love the return of a flash sync port. There have also been big improvements made to subject detection, with much more accurate tracking of eyes and faces even when objects get in the way. The in-body image stabilization is now “cropless”, so you’ll have a wider viewing angle when using IBIS. Lastly, a new Photo Style, Cinelike A2, has been added to the range of color expressions.

There are a couple of minor setbacks with this new model. The sensor is a bit smaller, with a 6% reduction compared to the original S1R (which also means the high-resolution mode is slightly smaller at 177 megapixels compared to 187). However, the 44MP BSI CMOS sensor reads out much more quickly than the earlier model to meet the demands of 8K recording and 40 fps burst capture. The LCD screen is also slightly smaller but, unlike in the S1R, this one is fully-articulating.

Expanded Workflow. Panasonic has beefed up their connectivity with a new (at the time of this writing) LUMIX Flow app for monitoring and organizing scenes with your smart device. The LUMIX Lab allows you to shoot with your smartphone, download creator LUTs, and stream up to 4K30p. The S1R II is now also tether-compatible with Capture One and you can dump footage directly to an SSD over USB-C. It has a built-in streaming encoder so you won’t need any extra hardware to stream with this camera. If you don’t have access to WiFi you can tether off your smartphone via USB-C. Direct IP streaming over Ethernet is possible with an adapter. When paired with the DMW-XLR2, 32-bit float audio recording is unlocked.

Build Quality and Ergo Updates. The S1R II body borrows heavily from the S5 II but with a new 3-way selector to choose between photo, video, and S&Q (slow and quick settings). Input your preferred settings for each one for fast switch-ups. Dual record buttons can be programmed as something else when in photo mode and front and back tally lights make recording confirmation very clear. A locking feature will prevent controls you choose from being adjustable mid-shoot, adding a layer of security to your workflow. The shutter mechanism has a protective curtain to keep dust away from the sensor when changing lenses. While most of the L-mount Lumix cameras have dual SD card slots, this one is equipped with one SD slot and one CFexpress Type B slot for recording internal RAW video (and for faster writing performance overall). Lastly, the sealed buttons and magnesium alloy shell ensure weatherproofing. The S1R II is an excellent hybrid powerhouse for indie filmmaking, pro and consumer photography, documentary work, and B-cam footage.', 4625000.0, '{"Brand": "Panasonic", "Camera Mount": "L", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "CFexpress Type B and SD", "General": "Accessory Mounts1x 1/4\\"-20 (bottom)Battery TypeDMW-BLK22Dimensions (W x H x D)5.29 × 4.03 × 3.61″Mfr. Model NumberDC-S1RM2BODYMonitorEVF3\\" articulating touchscreenWeight1.75 lb.Wireless2.4/5 GHz Wi-FiBluetooth 5.0", "Imaging": "FocusContrast, phase detection779 pointsISODynamic Range: 14 stopsPhoto: 40-102,400Video: 200-51,200Max Resolution8.1K (8128 × 4288)Sensor44.3MP full-frame CMOSShooting SpeedUp to 40 fpsShutterElectronic: 1/2,000 sec.-60 sec.Electronic: 1/10,000 sec-1/25 sec. (Movie Mode)Mechanical: 1/8,000 sec.-60 min.Stabilization5-axis IBIS", "Inputs/Outputs": "Audio I/O1x 3.5mm headphone jack1x 3.5mm mic jackOther I/O1x USB-C (data, shared with power)Power I/OUSB-C (shared with data)1x DMW-BLK22 battery portStorage I/O1x CFexpress Type B slot1x  SD UHS-II slotVideo I/O1x HDMI Type A", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Video Resolution": "8K", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Video Capture": "CompressionH.265/HEVCH.264/AVCProRes/ProRes RAWFormat.MP4.MOVResolution8.1K (8128 × 4288) at 23.98, 29.97 fpsUHD 8K (7680 × 4320) at 23.98, 29.97 fpsOpen-gate 6.4K (6432 × 4288)  at 23.98, 29.97 fps5.9K (5888 × 3312) up to 59.94 fps5.8K (5760 × 3040) up to 59.94 fpsDCI 4K (4096 × 2160) up to 120 fpsUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) up to 120 fpsFHD (1920 × 1080p) up to 120 fpsUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) up to 29.97 fps (HDMI out)", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Wireless Connectivity": "Bluetooth and None"}', 'Includes

	Panasonic Lumix S1R II camera
	Body cap
	Panasonic DMW-BLK22 battery
	Panasonic DMW-BTC15 charger
	1-port USB charger – Type-C 20V 1.5A 30W
	3’ LR Thunderbolt 4 USB cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1266, 1, 44, 'Panasonic Lumix DC-S5', 'panasonic-lumix-dc-s5', 'The Panasonic Lumix DC-S5 is a versatile, sleek, and durable camera that offers advanced feature sets for stills and video and precursor to the updated Panasonic Lumix S5 II. Key features include:

24.2MP full-frame CMOS sensor and Venus Engine
UHD 4K30p and UHD 4K60p video capture
Five-axis sensor-shift image stabilization
Accepts L-mount lenses

24.2MP Full-Frame CMOS Sensor and Venus Engine. The Panasonic Lumix DC-S5’s 24.2MP CMOS sensor is supported by an updated Venus Engine for impressive image quality, a 60 fps continuous shooting rate when using 6K or 4K PHOTO modes, a 7 fps continuous shooting rate with AF-S, a 6 fps continuous shooting rate with AF-C, great low-light performance, and a 100-51,200 ISO range that’s expandable to 50-204,800. The sensor and processor combine to enhance color reproduction and suppress noise levels throughout the camera’s sensitivity range. 
Please note, software v2.3 adds support for RAW video data output over HDMI! Supported RAW video formats can be found in the “External Video-Recording Modes” section under Specifications on this page.

L-Mount Alliance. This wide-diameter lens mount is a joint collaboration between Leica, Panasonic, and Sigma that’s focused on a line of premium cameras & lenses in a mirrorless format. At 51.6mm mount diameter and just 20mm flange distance, the L-mount is well-suited for fast-aperture full-frame optics with compact dimensions.

UHD 4K HDR Video Capture. The Lumix DC-S5 offers full-frame UHD 4K30p internal recording with 4:2:2 10-bit color, and UHD 4K60p recording using a 1.09x crop (via pixel binning) and 4:2:0 10-bit color. It’s also capable of Full HD 1080p capture at 60 fps, 4K capture at 30 fps, and anamorphic recording. It features clean HDMI output to an external recorder, a built-in stereo mic for quick audio capture, and 3.5mm mic and headphone jacks for advanced audio recording and monitoring needs. Please note that for 4K capture, you must use an SD memory card that’s UHS-I Class 3 or faster.

Post-Production Optimization. The S5 has a pair of gamma settings suited to capturing a wide dynamic range. This camera comes with V-Log pre-installed. It lets you capture a flat, neutral gamma curve that’s well-suited for grading. You can use the High Dynamic Range mode and Hybrid Log Gamma to record greater shadow and highlight details.

6K and 4K Photo. The DC-S5 gives you three still-shooting modes for recording continuous 3:2 or 4:3 8MP stills at a 60 or 30 fps shooting rate or 18MP stills at a 30 fps shooting rate. Burst mode lets you continuously record, Pre-Burst mode records images one second before and one second after you press the shutter button so you get 60 frames to choose from, while Burst (S/S) mode lets you select the frame you want from recorded video footage. This camera can also record stills in 65:24 and 2:1 panoramic formats.

Light-Speed Autofocus. This contrast-based autofocus system uses Panasonic’s Depth from Defocus technology to provide extremely fast speeds. Advanced AI technology assists in subject tracking of fast-moving subjects, while the same AI system is used when shooting portraits for face/eye detection. And if you’re shooting in low light, the DFD autofocus system works down to -6 EV. You also get full-time manual focusing with focus peaking and touch-to-focus operation for added precision.

Sensor-Shift Image Stabilization. This system uses five-axis sensor-shift stabilization for up to five stops of correction. Pair the camera with a Panasonic lens that features Dual IS 2 (a lens-based two-axis stabilization) to compensate for roughly 6.5 stops of camera shake, giving your hand-held shots utmost sharpness. Its High Resolution mode captures and compiles 8 separate exposures into a single 96MP RAW or JPEG file at 12000 × 8000 pixel resolution, but your subject must be static and the camera must be locked down on a tripod.

OLED EVF and Rear Touchscreen LCD. The high-resolution 2.36m-dot OLED EVF gives you a clear 0.74x magnification and a smooth 60 fps or 120 fps changeable refresh rate. You can use the 1.84m-dot 3.0-inch rear touchscreen LCD for image composition, review, playback, and menu navigation. Its free-tilting design lets you work from low and high angles, even when you’re shooting in vertical orientation.

Other Notable Features. The built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth provide wireless control and viewing options via the free Lumix Sync App. Images are recorded to SDHC/XC memory cards (remember, UHS-I Class 3 or faster for 4K video), and the rechargeable DMW-BLK22 battery is rated for approximately 440 shots per charge when using the rear monitor, 470 shots per charge when using the EVF, and 1500 shots per charge when Power Save LVF mode is on.', 2325000.0, '{"Aspect Ratio": "1:1, 2:1, 3:2, 4:3, 16:9, 65:24", "Audio File Formats": "AAC, Linear PCM", "Audio Recording": "Built-In Microphone (Stereo)\\nExternal Microphone Input", "Autofocus Points": "Contrast Detection: 225", "Autofocus Sensitivity": "-6 to +20 EV", "Battery": "1x DMW-BLK22 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 2200 VDC, 7.2 mAh (Approx. 440 Shots)", "Bit Depth": "14-Bit", "Brand": "Panasonic", "Built-in Flash": "No", "Camera Mount": "L", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Continuous Shooting": "Mechanical Shutter\\nUp to 7 fps at 24.2 MP for up to 24 Frames (RAW) / 999 Frames (JPEG)\\n\\nElectronic Shutter\\nUp to 7 fps at 24.2 MP for up to 24 Frames (RAW) / 999 Frames (JPEG)\\nUp to 30 fps at 18 MP\\nUp to 60 fps at 8 MP\\nUp to 30 fps at 8 MP", "Dedicated Flash System": "TTL", "Depth": "3.2\\"", "Diopter Adjustment": "-4 to +4", "Exposure Compensation": "-5 to +5 EV (1/3 EV Steps)", "Exposure Modes": "Aperture Priority, Manual, Program, Shutter Priority", "External Flash Connection": "Hot Shoe", "External Video-Recording Modes": "4:2:2 10-BitUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) up to 50p/59.94p12-bit Raw5.9K (5888×3312) 29.97p/25p/23.98p4K (4128×2176) 59.94p/50p/29.97p/25p/23.98p3.5K (3536×2656) 50p/29.97p/25p/23.98p", "Flash Compensation": "-3 to +3 EV (1/3 EV Steps)", "Flash Modes": "Auto, Auto/Red-Eye Reduction, Forced On, Forced On/Red-Eye Reduction, Off, Slow Sync, Slow Sync/Red-Eye Reduction", "Focus Modes": "Continuous-Servo AF, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AF", "Focus Type": "Auto and Manual Focus", "GPS": "No", "Height": "3.8\\"", "Image File Formats": "JPEG, RAW", "Inputs/Outputs": "USB Type-C (USB 3.1), HDMI D (Micro), 3.5mm Microphone, 3.5mm Headphone, 2.5mm Sub-Mini", "Interval Recording": "Yes", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Resolution": "6000 × 4000", "Maximum Sync Speed": "1/250 Second", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Memory Card Slot": "Slot 1: SD/SDHC/SDXC (UHS-II)\\nSlot 2: SD/SDHC/SDXC (UHS-I)", "Metering Range": "0 to 18 EV", "Mfr. Model Number": "DC-S5BODY", "Monitor Type": "Articulating Touchscreen LCD", "Operating Temperature": "32 to 104°F / 0 to 40°C", "Pixels": "Actual: 25.28 Megapixel\\nEffective: 24.2 Megapixel", "Recording Limit": "Up to 30 Minutes for UHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p (4:2:2 10-Bit)\\nUp to 30 Minutes for UHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 50p/59.94p (4:2:0 10-Bit)\\nUnlimited for UHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p (4:2:0 8-Bit)", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Self Timer": "2/10-Second Delay", "Sensor Dimensions": "35.6 × 23.8mm", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Sensor Type": "CMOS", "Shutter Speed": "Mechanical Shutter\\n1/8000 to 60 Second\\n0 to 30 Minute in Bulb Mode\\n\\nElectronic Front Curtain Shutter\\n1/2000 to 60 Second\\n0 to 30 Minute\\n\\nElectronic Shutter\\n1/8000 to 60 Second\\n0 to 60 Second in Bulb Mode\\n1/16000 to 1/25 Second in Movie Mode", "Stabilization": "Sensor-Shift, 5-Axis", "Video Encoding": "NTSC/PAL", "Video Recording Modes": "H.264/MOV 4:2:2 10-Bit\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p [150 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [100 Mb/s]\\n4K Anamorphic (3328 × 2496) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p [150 Mb/s]\\n\\nH.264/MOV 4:2:0 8-Bit\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [100 to 150 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [100 Mb/s]\\n4K Anamorphic (3328 × 2496) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p [100 to 150 Mb/s]\\n\\nH.265/MOV 4:2:0 10-Bit\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 50p/59.94p [200 Mb/s]\\n4K Anamorphic (3328 × 2496) at 50p [200 Mb/s]\\n\\nH.265/MP4 4:2:0 10-Bit\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p [72 to 100 Mb/s]\\n\\nH.264/MP4 4:2:0 8-Bit\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p [100 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p/100p/119.88p/180p [20 to 28 Mb/s]", "Viewfinder Coverage": "100%", "Viewfinder Eye Point": "20mm", "Viewfinder Magnification": "Approx. 0.74x", "Viewfinder Resolution": "2,360,000 Dot", "Viewfinder Size": "3\\"", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "White Balance": "Auto, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Daylight, Flash, Incandescent, Shade, White Set", "Width": "5.2\\"", "Wireless": "Bluetooth\\nWi-Fi", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

