INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1283, 1, 44, 'Panasonic Lumix S5 IIX', 'panasonic-lumix-s5-iix', 'The Panasonic Lumix S5IIX is an enhanced version of the standard Panasonic Lumix S5 II with extensive video and streaming features designed with professional content creators in mind. Key features include:

HDMI RAW video output; ALL-Intra and ProRes recording
SSD recording and playback via USB
Wireless/wired IP streaming; USB smartphone tethering
6K30p 4:2:0 10-bit video; on-sensor autofocus system

Pro-Grade Video Features. The Panasonic Lumix S5IIX differentiates itself from its sibling, the standard Panasonic Lumix S5 II, through the inclusion of an array of advanced video features aimed at professional content creators. You get HDMI RAW video-data output; support for recording to and playback from external SSDs via USB; ALL-Intra and ProRes recording; and wireless IP streaming, wired IP streaming, and USB tethering to smartphones.

Updated Sensor and Processing Engine. The S5IIX’s updated 24.2MP CMOS sensor features on-sensor phase detection for the first time on a Panasonic camera. A new processing engine, developed in partnership with Leica, works in tandem with the sensor to enable full-resolution shooting at up to 9 fps with the mechanical shutter and up to 30 fps with the electronic shutter. You also get great low-light performance, a 100-51,200 ISO range that’s expandable to 50-204,800, and enhanced color reproduction and suppressed noise levels throughout the camera’s sensitivity range. This camera can also record stills in 65:24 and 2:1 panoramic formats, 1:1 square format, and 16:9 format.

L-Mount Alliance. This camera’s wide-diameter lens mount is a joint collaboration between Leica, Panasonic, and Sigma that’s focused on a line of premium cameras & lenses in a mirrorless format. At 51.6mm mount diameter and just 20mm flange distance, the L-mount is well-suited for fast-aperture full-frame optics with compact dimensions.

6K30p, DCI 4K, and UHD 4K Video. The Lumix S5 IIX offers full-frame, open-gate 6K30p video capture with 4:2:0 10-bit color for up to half an hour, and unlimited video capture in DCI and UHD 4K60p 4:2:2 10-bit mode. You also get 120p capture for high-res slow-motion video. The 6K30p option uses the entire sensor to produce a 3:2 aspect ratio file that you can re-crop to any other aspect ratio you need, including 9:16, 1:1, 16:9, and 2.2:1. It features clean HDMI output to an external recorder, a built-in stereo mic for quick audio capture, and 3.5mm mic and headphone jacks for advanced audio recording and monitoring needs. Please note that for 6K and 4K capture, you must use an SD memory card that’s UHS-I Class 3 or faster.

Post-Production Optimization. The S5 IIX comes with V-Log pre-installed. This gamma lets you capture a flat, neutral gamma curve and an equivalent 14+ stops of dynamic range, giving you precise control for color grading in post and seamless editing with VariCam footage. Dual Native ISO uses two dedicated circuits per pixel to keep noise low and sensitivity high, facilitating shooting in a wide range of lighting conditions.

Phase Hybrid Autofocus System. The S5 IIX and S5 II are the first Lumix mirrorless cameras to incorporate an on-sensor Phase Hybrid autofocus system, which uses 779 phase-detection points to facilitate fast and highly accurate performance, even in backlit or low-light shooting situations. Three distinct subject-based tracking modes help to ensure maximum accuracy. Human + Animal Tracking mode will track any of the subjects you’ve trained it to recognize and will prioritize animals; Human mode tracks humans by detecting and prioritizing eyes, then faces, then heads, and then bodies; and Face/Eye detection only focuses on eyes and faces in the frame.

Dual I.S. 2 Image Stabilization. This system uses five-axis sensor-shift stabilization to compensate for roughly 6.5 stops of camera shake, giving your hand-held shots utmost sharpness. A newly developed Active I.S. system improves stabilization when you’re shooting video while you walk.

OLED EVF and Rear Touchscreen LCD. The high-resolution 3.68m-dot OLED EVF gives you a clear 0.78x magnification and a smooth 60 fps or 120 fps changeable refresh rate. You can use the 1.84m-dot 3.0-inch rear touchscreen LCD for menu navigation and image composition, review, and playback. The LCD’s free-tilting design lets you work from low and high angles, even when you’re shooting in vertical orientation.

Battery And Wall Charger Included. This rental will come to you with a single Panasonic DMW-BLK22 battery, a Type-A to Type-C charging cable, and a compatible wall block to connect the camera straight to the power source!

Other Notable Features. The built-in cooling fan keeps the camera’s internal temperature low during extended shoots. Wi-Fi and Bluetooth connectivity provide wireless control and viewing options via the free Lumix Sync App for Android and iOS. This camera has two UHS-II compatible SDHC/XC memory-card slots (remember, UHS-I Class 3 or faster for 4K video), and the rechargeable DMW-BLK22 battery is rated for approximately 370 shots per charge when using the rear monitor or the EVF.', 3200000.0, '{"Brand": "Panasonic", "Camera Mount": "L", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Environmental": "Operating Temperature32 to 104°FOperating Humidity10 to 80%", "Exposure Control": "Shutter TypeElectronic Shutter, Mechanical Focal Plane ShutterMechanical Shutter Speed1/8000 to 60 SecondsUp to 30 Minutes in Bulb ModeElectronic Front Curtain Shutter Speed1/2000 to 60 SecondsUp to 30 Minutes in Bulb ModeElectronic Shutter Speed1/8000 to 60 SecondsUp to 60 Seconds in Bulb ModeBulb/Time ModeBulb Mode, Time ModeISO Sensitivity (Photo/Video)100 to 51,200 (Extended: 50 to 204,800)Metering MethodCenter-Weighted Average, Highlight Weighted, Multiple, SpotExposure ModesAperture Priority, Auto, Manual, Program, Shutter PriorityExposure Compensation-5 to +5 EV (1/3 EV Steps)Metering Range0 to 18 EVWhite Balance2500 to 10,000KWhite-Balance PresetsAWB, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Daylight, Flash, Incandescent, Shade, White Set 1, White Set 2, White Set 3, White Set 4Continuous Shooting (Mechanical Shutter)Up to 9 fps for up to 200 Frames (RAW) / 300 Frames (JPEG)Up to 5 fps for up to 200 Frames (RAW) / 300 Frames (JPEG)Up to 2 fps for up to 200 Frames (RAW) / 300 Frames (JPEG)Continuous Shooting (Electronic Shutter)Up to 30 fps for up to 200 Frames (RAW) / 200 Frames (JPEG)Up to 9 fps for up to 200 Frames (RAW) / 300 Frames (JPEG)Up to 5 fps for up to 200 Frames (RAW) / 300 Frames (JPEG)Up to 2 fps for up to 200 Frames (RAW) / 300 Frames (JPEG)Interval RecordingYesSelf-Timer2/10-Second Delay", "Flash": "Built-In FlashNoFlash ModesAuto, Auto/Red-Eye Reduction, Forced On, Forced On/Red-Eye Reduction, Slow Sync, Slow Sync/Red-Eye ReductionMaximum Sync Speed1/250 SecondFlash Compensation-3 to +3 EV (1/3 EV Steps)Dedicated Flash SystemTTLExternal Flash ConnectionHot Shoe", "Focusing": "Focus TypeAuto and Manual FocusFocus ModeContinuous-Servo AF, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AFAutofocus Points (Photo, Video)Contrast Detection, Phase Detection: 779Autofocus Sensitivity-6 to +18 EV", "General": "Battery Type1x Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 7.2 VDC, 2200 mAh (Approx. 370 Shots)Tripod Mounting Thread1x 1/4\\"-20 Female (Bottom)Accessory Mount1x Hot Shoe Mount on Camera BodyMaterial of ConstructionMagnesium AlloyDimensions (W x H x D)5.29 × 4.03 × 3.55″Weight1.45 lbs. (Body Only)1.64 lbs. (With Recording Media)", "Imaging": "Sensor ResolutionActual: 25.28 MegapixelEffective: 24.2 Megapixel (6000 × 4000)Sensor Type35.6 × 23.8mm (Full-Frame) CMOSImage StabilizationSensor-Shift, 5-AxisBuilt-In ND FilterNoneCapture TypeStills & Video", "Interface": "Media/Memory Card SlotDual Slot: SD/SDHC/SDXC (UHS-II)Video I/O1x HDMI OutputAudio I/O1x 1/8\\" / 3.5mm TRRS Headphone/Mic Headphone Output1x 1/8\\" / 3.5mm TRRS Headphone/Mic Microphone InputPower I/O1x USB-C Input/OutputOther I/O1x USB-C Data Input/Output (Shared with Power Input)Wireless2.4 / 5 GHz Wi-Fi (802.11b/g), Wi-Fi 5 (802.11ac), Bluetooth 5.0App NameLumix SyncApp CompatibilityAndroid & iOSApp FunctionalityAccess Stored Files, Firmware Update, Remote ControlGlobal Positioning (GPS, GLONASS, etc.)None", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Video Resolution": "6K", "Mfr. Model Number": "DC-S5M2XBODY", "Monitor": "Size3\\"Resolution1,840,000 DotDisplay TypeFree-Angle Tilting Touchscreen LCD", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Still Image Capture": "Image Sizes (3:2)96 MP (12,000 × 8000) *Via In-Camera Pixel-Shift96 MP (8496 × 5664) *Via In-Camera Pixel-Shift24.2 MP (6000 × 4000)24.2 MP (4272 × 2848)24.2 MP (3024 × 2016)Image Sizes (4:3)96 MP (10,656 × 8000) *Via In-Camera Pixel-Shift96 MP (7552 × 5664) *Via In-Camera Pixel-Shift24.2 MP (5328 × 4000)24.2 MP (3792 × 2848)24.2 MP (2688 × 2016)Image Sizes (16:9)96 MP (12,000 × 6736) *Via In-Camera Pixel-Shift96 MP (8496 × 4784) *Via In-Camera Pixel-Shift24.2 MP (6000 × 3368)24.2 MP (4272 × 2400)24.2 MP (3024 × 1704)Image Sizes (1:1)96 MP (8000 × 8000) *Via In-Camera Pixel-Shift96 MP (5664 × 5664) *Via In-Camera Pixel-Shift24.2 MP (4000 × 4000)24.2 MP (2848 × 2848)24.2 MP (2016 × 2016)Image Sizes (65:24)24.2 MP (6000 × 2208)Image Sizes (2:1)24.2 MP (6000 × 3000)Aspect Ratio1:1, 2:1, 3:2, 4:3, 16:9, 65:24Image File FormatJPEG, RAWBit Depth14-Bit", "Video Capture": "Internal Recording Modes (H.264/H.265/MOV/MPEG-4 AVC 4:2:2/4:2:0 8/10-Bit)5952 × 3968 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [200 Mb/s]5952 × 3136 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [200 Mb/s]5888 × 3312 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [200 Mb/s]4096 × 2160 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [150 Mb/s]3840 × 2160 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [72 to 150 Mb/s]1920 × 1080 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97/47.95/48.00/50/59.94/100/ fps [20 to 150 Mb/s]External Recording Modes (12-Bit via HDMI)5888 × 3312 at 23.98/25/29.97 fpsExternal Recording Modes (10-Bit via USB)5776 × 3056 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps4096 × 2160 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps1920 × 1080 at 24.00/25/50 fpsSensor Crop Modes (Super35/APS-C)4096 × 21603840 × 21603328 × 24961920 × 1080Fast-/Slow-Motion SupportYesGamma CurvePanasonic V-Gamut, V-LogRecording LimitNoneBroadcast OutputNTSC/PALIP Streaming (RTP, RTSP)3840 × 2160 to 1280 × 720 at 25p, 29.97p, 50p, 59.94p (4.0 to 25.00 Mb/s)Built-In Microphone TypeStereoAudio RecordingMOV: 2-Channel 24-Bit 48 kHz LPCM AudioMP4: 2-Channel 16-Bit 48 kHz AAC Audio", "Viewfinder": "TypeBuilt-In Electronic (OLED)Resolution3,680,000 DotEye Point21mmCoverage100%MagnificationApprox. 0.78xDiopter Adjustment-4 to +2", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

	Panasonic Lumix S5 IIX
	Panasonic Type-A 5V/1.8A 1-Port USB Charger
	Panasonic DMW-BLK22 Battery
	USB 3.1 Gen 2 Type-A to Type-C w / Ferrite Bead Cable 3’', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1284, 1, 44, 'Panasonic Lumix S9 (Black)', 'panasonic-lumix-s9-black', 'The Panasonic Lumix S9 is a sleek, ultra-compact camera that offers advanced video and still feature sets designed with content creators’ social-media workflows in mind. Key features include:

Designed for content creators
Fast camera-to-phone workflow
Real Time LUTs for videos and photos
6K30p 4:2:0 10-bit video capture

Optimized for Content Creators. The Panasonic Lumix S9 is optimized for content creators’ social-media workflows. Its improved connection speed and stability help get your videos and images directly from the camera to your socials quickly, eliminating the need for a computer or third-party software. Its Real Time Look Up Table (LUT) system lets you use a dedicated button to instantly apply signature color and tone presets to your videos and photos to give you the look you want right out of the camera, without the use of color-editing software.

Social-Media Friendly Video Options. The S9 offers full-frame, open-gate 6K30p video capture with 4:2:0 10-bit color for up to half an hour, and unlimited video capture in DCI and UHD 4K60p 4:2:2 10-bit mode. You also get MP4Lite video, a new file format optimized for quick uploads, and 120p capture for high-res slow-motion video. The 6K30p option uses the entire sensor to produce a 3:2 aspect ratio file that you can re-crop to any other aspect ratio you need, including 1:1, 2:1, 4:3. 16:9, and 65:24. It features clean HDMI output to an external recorder, a built-in stereo mic for quick audio capture, and a 3.5mm mic jack for your advanced audio-recording needs. Please note that for 6K and 4K capture, you must use an SD memory card that’s UHS-I Class 3 or faster.

Real Time LUT System. The S9’s expanded Real Time LUT system lets you apply pre-loaded custom looks to videos and stills so that you can post content directly to your socials without the need for outside-the-camera color editing. You can use LUTs with any of the S9’s Photo Style color modes—not just the V-Log style—and you can create and store custom looks that combine two different LUTs and apply them on top of a base Photo Style. This camera can store up to 39 LUTs in its internal memory, which you can instantly access via a dedicated LUT button.

Full-Frame Sensor, High-Efficiency Processing Engine. This camera’s 24.2MP full-frame BSI CMOS sensor features on-sensor phase detection. It works in tandem with the processing engine, developed in partnership with Leica, to enable full-resolution shooting at up to 30 fps with the electronic shutter. You also get great low-light performance, a 100-51,200 ISO range that’s expandable to 50-204,800, and enhanced color reproduction and suppressed noise levels throughout the camera’s sensitivity range. This camera can record stills in 3:2 format, 65:24 and 2:1 panoramic formats, 1:1 square format, and 16:9 format.

Phase Hybrid Autofocus System. As mentioned above, the S9 incorporates an on-sensor Phase Hybrid autofocus system, which uses 779 phase-detection points to facilitate fast and highly accurate performance, even in backlit or low-light shooting situations. Six subject-based tracking modes can follow certain subject types—humans, animals, cars, motorcycles, trains, and airplanes—and even prioritize certain parts of those designated subjects to help to ensure maximum precision.

Versatile, Vlogger-Ready Image Stabilization. The in-body five-axis sensor-shift image stabilization system compensates for roughly five stops of camera shake, giving your hand-held videos and stills utmost sharpness. The Boost I.S. mode approximates footage shot from a tripod, giving you increased steadiness with less mobility, while the Dual I.S. mode syncs the camera’s in-body stabilization with compatible lenses’ optical image stabilization for up to 6.5 stops of correction. Finally, the Active I.S. mode improves stabilization when you’re shooting video while you walk, making it great for going live when you’re out and around.

Intuitive Controls. On the top of the S9’s body, you’ll find the mode dial, the shutter button, which is surrounded by a programmable command dial, and a programmable red button that acts as a Recording Start key if its function isn’t defined otherwise. The camera’s only display is a 1.84m-dot 3.0-inch flip-out rear touchscreen LCD, which you can use for menu navigation; focus-point selection; and image composition, review, and playback. The LCD’s free-tilting design lets you work from low and high angles, even when you’re shooting in vertical orientation. There’s a four-way controller that you can also use to make menu selections and choose focus points. There are dedicated, programmable LUT and AF On buttons situated in an easy-to-reach spot above the touchscreen, while the highly sensitive control dial and other buttons are to the right of the touchscreen.

L-Mount Alliance. This camera’s wide-diameter lens mount is a joint collaboration between Leica, Panasonic, and Sigma that’s focused on a line of premium cameras & lenses in a mirrorless format. At 51.6mm mount diameter and just 20mm flange distance, the L-mount is well-suited for fast-aperture full-frame optics with compact dimensions.

Connectivity, Media, and Power. Wi-Fi and Bluetooth connectivity provide wireless control and viewing options via the free Lumix Lab App for Android and iOS, and the Lumix Sync app for Android and iOS. This camera has a single UHS-II compatible SDHC/XC slot and uses the rechargeable DMW-BLK22 battery, which is rated for approximately 470 shots per charge.', 2300000.0, '{"Brand": "Panasonic", "Camera Mount": "L", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Exposure Control": "Shutter TypeElectronic Rolling ShutterShutter Speed – Electronic Shutter1/8000 to 60 Seconds in Manual Mode1/16000 to 1/25 Second in Movie ModeBulb/Time ModeBulb ModeISO Sensitivity Range – Photo/Video100 to 51,200Extended: 50 to 204,800Metering MethodsCenter-Weighted Average, Highlight Weighted, Multiple, SpotExposure ModesAperture Priority, Auto, Manual, Program, Shutter PriorityExposure Compensation-5 to +5 EV (1/3 EV Steps)Metering Range0 to 18 EVWhite Balance2500 to 10,000KWhite-Balance PresetsAWB, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Daylight, Incandescent, Shade, White Set 1, White Set 2, White Set 3, White Set 4Continuous ShootingUp to 30 fps at Maximum ResolutionInterval RecordingYesSelf-Timer2/10-Second Delay", "Flash": "Built-In Flash/LightNoExternal Flash ConnectionNo", "Focus": "Focus TypeAuto and Manual FocusFocus ModesContinuous-Servo AF, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AFAutofocus PointsContrast Detection, Phase Detection: 779Autofocus Sensitivity6 to +18 EV", "General": "Battery1x DMW-BLK22 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 7.2 VDC, 2200 mAh (Included)Shoe Mount1x Cold ShoeTripod Mounting Thread1x 1/4\\"-20 Female (Bottom)Operating Conditions32 to 104°F / 0 to 40°C at 10 to 80% HumidityDimensions (W x H x D)4.96 × 2.91 × 1.84″ / 12.6 × 7.39 × 4.67 cmWeight0.9 lb. / 403 g (Body Only)1.1 lb. / 486 g (With Battery, Recording Media)", "Imaging": "Sensor ResolutionActual: 25.3 MegapixelEffective: 24.2 Megapixel (6000 × 4000)Image Sensor35.6 × 23.8mm (Full-Frame) CMOSSensor Crop (35mm Equivalent)Crop Factor: 1xAdditional Crop Occurs in Select Video ModesImage StabilizationSensor-Shift, 5-AxisBuilt-In ND FilterNoCapture TypeStills & Video", "Interface": "Media/Memory Card SlotSingle Slot: SD/SDHC/SDXC (UHS-II) [V90 or Faster Recommended]Video I/O1x Micro-HDMI OutputAudio I/O1x 1/8\\" / 3.5mm TRS Stereo Microphone InputPower I/O1x USB-C InputOther I/O1x USB-C Data Output (Shared with Power Input)WirelessWi-Fi 5 (802.11ac), Bluetooth 5.0Mobile App CompatibleYes: Android & iOSApp Name: Lumix Lab / Lumix SyncFunctionality: Access Stored Files, Adjust Settings, Firmware Update, Remote Control, View Live FeedGlobal Positioning (GPS, GLONASS, etc.)GPS, via Connected Smartphone", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Video Resolution": "6K", "Mfr. Model Number": "DC-S9BODYK", "Monitor": "Display Size3\\"Resolution1,840,000 DotDisplay TypeFree-Angle Tilting Touchscreen LCD", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Still Image Capture": "Aspect Ratio1:1, 2:1, 3:2, 4:3, 16:9, 65:24Image File FormatsJPEG, RAW", "Video Capture": "Internal Recording Modes – H.264 Long GOP/H.265 Long GOP/MOV 4:2:2/4:2:0DCI 4K (4096 × 2160) at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [150 Mb/s]3840 × 2160 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [150 Mb/s]1920 × 1080 at 23.98/24.00/29.97/47.95/48.00/50/59.94/100/120 fps [100 to 150 Mb/s]Internal Recording Modes – H.265 Long GOP/MOV 4:2:0 10-Bit5952 × 3968 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [200 Mb/s]5888 × 3312 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [200 Mb/s]5952 × 3136 at 23.98/24.00/25/29.97 fps [200 Mb/s]Internal Recording Modes – H.265 Long GOP/MP4/MP4 Lite 4:2:0 8/10-Bit3840 × 2560 at 25 fps [50 Mb/s]3840 × 2160 at 23.98/25/29.97 fps [72 to 100 Mb/s]1920 × 1080 at 23.98/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps [20 to 28 Mb/s]External Recording Modes – 4:2:2 8/10-Bit via HDMI4096 × 21603840 × 21601920 × 1080p1920 × 1080iFast-/Slow-Motion SupportYesGamma CurveHDR-HLG, Panasonic V-LogRecording Limit15-Minute Maximum in 4KIP StreamingNoBuilt-In MicrophoneStereoAudio RecordingMOV: 2-Channel 24-Bit 48 kHz LPCM AudioMP4: 2-Channel 16-Bit 48 kHz AAC Audio", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

