INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1335, 1, 48, 'Ricoh G900', 'ricoh-g900', 'The Ricoh G900 is an ultra-rugged, compact digital camera with advanced security and information management support for worksite efficiency. We now have the updated G900 II available! Key features include:

Water-, shock-, crush-, freeze- and dustproof build
High-res stills and UHD 4K30 video capture
Integrated 5x zoom lens with LED ring light
Camera memo, barcode scanner, and password features

Tough Physical Design. The Ricoh G900’s main selling point is its extremely durable build. It’s waterproof down to 65.6 feet, shockproof to falls from up to 6.6 feet, crushproof to up to 220 lbf. of pressure, freezeproof down to 14°F, and dustproof. It’s also chemical-resistant to ethanol disinfection, bleach disinfection, and liquid chlorine dioxide, making it ideal for use in business, industrial, civil engineering, construction, and disaster-relief settings. Need a remote camera trigger? We recommend the O-RC1 Waterproof Infrared Remote Control

20MP BSI CMOS Sensor. The 20MP BSI CMOS sensor enables the G900 to capture high-res stills and UHD 4K30 video. Its back-illuminated design provides excellent clarity, minimal noise, and a 1,250-25,600 ISO range that lets you work in an array of lighting conditions. There are shake-reduction options for diminishing

Built-In 5x Zoom Lens with LED Ring Light. The integrated 5-25mm f/3.5 to f/5.5 lens provides a 35mm focal-length range equivalent to 28mm-140mm and a 0.4-inch minimum focusing distance, making it a strong choice for a wide range of applications. Its nine-group/eleven-element design maximizes image quality while reducing optical aberrations and ensuring corner-to-corner sharpness. The lens is surrounded by a six-LED ring light with configurable lighting patterns, ten brightness settings, and compatibility with the camera’s barcode scanning mode.

Shake Reduction. The G900’s Movie SR+ setting acts as an “electronic gimbal” to minimize the appearance of camera shake when you’re shooting handheld video. There’s also a standard Movie SR mode that clips the frame to promote steadier video and produce a more neutral, less distorted appearance.

Memo Function. A memo function lets you attach up to one hundred 128-character text items or one 30-second audio file to your images. This feature also lets you browse your stored memos for relevant information. You can use the G900’s barcode scanning mode to attach scanned barcode information to an image as embedded memo data.

Password Protection. You can use a password to partially or completely restrict access to the G900’s camera functionality, menus, internal memory, and USB connection. This camera will store two separate passwords—one for an admin and the other for a standard user—and the password protection extends to encrypting SD cards to protect your images if your card is lost or stolen.

Controls and Display. This camera’s interface is designed for easy operation in harsh conditions, even when you’re wearing gloves. A customizable ADJ button gives you easy access to your most frequently used features, a top dial lets you quickly switch between shooting modes, and an ergonomic four-way controller lets you select your desired camera functions. The 3.0-inch 1.04m-dot LCD’s brightness and AR coating make it easy to read in most any lighting conditions.

GPS, Power, and Memory. The G900’s built-in GPS module is fast and accurate, and lets you record location information to images via its memory function. It also gives you access to an electronic compass that covers 360° in 16 directions. This camera includes a rechargeable DB-110 battery, and it records images to a SDHC/XC memory card via its single slot. It also has 6.5GB of internal memory for image storage.', 1200000.0, '{"Aspect Ratio": "1:1, 3:2, 4:3", "Audio Recording": "Built-In Microphone", "Battery": "1x DB-110 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 3.6 VDC, 1350 mAh", "Brand": "Ricoh", "Built-in Flash": "Yes", "Camera Type": "Compact", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Connectivity": "HDMI D (Micro), USB Type-C (USB 3.0)", "Crushproof": "220 lbf / 100 kgf", "Depth": "1.3\\"", "Exposure Compensation": "-2 to +2 EV (1/3 EV Steps)", "Exposure Modes": "Program", "Flash Modes": "Flash On, Off, Red-Eye Reduction", "Flash Range": "ISO Auto\\n0.66 to 18.04’ / 0.2 to 5.5 m (Wide)\\n0.66 to 11.48’ / 0.2 to 3.5 m (Telephoto)", "Focal Length": "5 to 25mm (35mm Equivalent Focal Length: 28 to 140mm)", "Focus Range": "Normal\\n1.64’ to Infinity\\n\\nMacro\\n0.39\\" to 1.97’", "GPS": "Yes", "Groups/Elements": "9/11", "Height": "2.6\\"", "Image File Formats": "JPEG", "Internal Storage": "6.5GB", "Interval Recording": "Yes", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Aperture": "f/3.5 to 5.5", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Memory Card Slot": "Single Slot: SD/SDHC/SDXC", "Mfr. Model Number": "162102", "Monitor Resolution": "1,040,000 Dot", "Monitor Size": "3\\"", "Monitor Type": "Fixed LCD", "Operating Temperature": "14 to 104°F", "Screen Type": "Fixed", "Sensor Resolution": "Effective: 20 Megapixel", "Sensor Size": "1-Inch", "Sensor Type": "CMOS", "Shockproof": "6.6’ / 2 m", "Shutter Speed": "Electronic Front Curtain Shutter\\n1/4000 to 4 Seconds", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Video Encoding": "NTSC", "Video Recording Limit": "Up to 25 Minutes", "Video Recording Modes": "H.264\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 29.97p\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 29.97p\\nHD (1280 × 720) at 29.97p", "Waterproof Depth Rating": "65.6’ / 20 m", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "White Balance": "Auto, Cloudy, Daylight, Fluorescent (Day White), Fluorescent (Daylight), Fluorescent (White), Manual, Ring Light, Shade, Tungsten", "Width": "4.7\\"", "Zoom": "5x"}', 'Includes

	Ricoh G900
	DB-110 battery
	BJ-11 charger
