Creative Uses. You can take advantage of this ultra-wide angle lens’s extreme angle of view to capture unorthodox images. This type of lens is commonly used for landscape and architectural photography, but It’s able to shoot some rather interesting portraits as well. Its 9.84-inch minimum focusing distance makes it simple to exaggerate perspective.', 850000.0, '{"Angle of View": "100.1°", "Aperture Blades": "7", "Brand": "Rokinon", "Dimensions": "2.5 × 2.38″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "58.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "18-18", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "8/9", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "2.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.09x", "Mfr. Model Number": "IO18AF-E", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "9.84\\"", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "0.32 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Includes

