Optimized for Astrophotography. In addition to its large maximum aperture, the 14mm f/1.4 has a range of features that make it a fantastic choice for astrophotography. Its optical design and in-camera corrections keep distortion reined in, producing extremely well-controlled sagittal flare that yields pin-point stars from edge to edge while limiting ghosting. A new Manual Focus Lock switch disables the focus ring so that your focus never changes even if you’re shooting under the night sky for hours. This lens’s rear filter holder accepts sheet-type filters that are often used by astrophotographers to produce various artistic effects.

Inner Focus Autofocus System. The 14mm’s autofocus system uses a stepping motor to provide fast, smooth, and nearly silent focusing for stills and video alike. You can also just rotate the focus ring at any point for manual-focus override. A built-in Autofocus-Lock button can be assigned additional functions, giving you more options and capabilities, while the above-mentioned Manual Focus Lock feature disables the focus ring entirely. This lens is compatible with select Sony E-mount cameras’ AF Assist function.

Advanced Optical Design. This lens’s fifteen-group/nineteen-element optical design includes three aspherical elements, one Special Low-Dispersion element, and three “F” Low-Dispersion elements to minimize chromatic aberrations, distortion, and vignetting while providing maximum sharpness, color accuracy, and clarity. The elements have a Super Multilayer Coating that helps prevent flare and produce contrasty, color-neutral images, even when you’re shooting in backlit conditions.

High-Quality Build. The Sigma 14mm’s Thermally Stable Composite build is dust- and splash-resistant, so that you can use it in adverse conditions. It also boasts a brass bayonet mount for maximum durability. An included petal-type hood helps to prevent flare and protect the lens’s front element.', 2425000.0, '{"Angle of View": "114.2º", "Aperture Blades": "11, rounded", "Brand": "Sigma", "Dimensions": "4 × 5.9″ (ø x L)", "Filter Type": "Rear Mount", "Focal Length": "14-14", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "15/19", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "1.4", "Maximum Magnification": "0.1x", "Mfr. Model Number": "451965", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "11.8\\"", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "2.58 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Sigma 14mm f/1.4 DG DN Art for Sony E
	Front & rear caps
	Hood
	Sigma TS-141 tripod ring/foot
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1508, 2, 51, 'Sigma 14mm f/1.8 DG HSM Art for Canon EF', 'sigma-14mm-f-1-8-dg-hsm-art-for-canon-ef', 'The Sigma 14mm f/1.8 DG HSM Art for Canon is a fast-aperture wide-angle prime that’s part of Sigma’s Global Vision line. This version is for Canon EF-mount cameras. Key features include:

Great for low-light outdoor shooting and astrophotography
Excellent image quality, clarity, contrast, and sharpness
Fast, smooth, and quiet autofocus with manual override
Sigma USB dock compatible

Fast f/1.8 Aperture Wide Angle. The Sigma 14mm f/1.8 DG HSM Art’s bright f/1.8 maximum aperture, wide-angle perspective, and fast, flexible performance make it excellent for low-light outdoor shooting and astrophotography. You can also use this lens on APS-C mount cameras, on which it’ll provide a 22.4mm equivalent focal length.

High-Quality Optics. As a part of Sigma’s Art lens line, the 14mm f/1.8 goes through rigorous testing to ensure high image quality. Four aspherical elements help to eliminate distortion and spherical aberrations. Three “F” Low-Dispersion elements and four Super Low-Dispersion glass elements correct for chromatic aberrations and color fringing while ensuring high image sharpness, clarity, and contrast. The Super Multi-Layer Coating minimizes lens flare and ghosting, helping to provide high contrast in strong lighting.

Hyper Sonic Motor Autofocus System. The autofocus system provides fast, smooth, and quiet operation in a broad range of shooting situations. You can also manually override the autofocus motor at any time by rotating the focusing ring, giving you quick fine-tuning ability. The 14mm f/1.8 offers a 10.6-inch minimum focusing distance.

Sigma Dock Compatibility. This lens is compatible with the Sigma USB Dock for Canon EF Lenses (separate rental item), allowing you to adjust certain parameters through the Sigma Optimization Pro software.', 2100000.0, '{"Brand": "Sigma", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Canon EF", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle"}', 'Includes

	Sigma 14mm f/1.8 Art
	Push-on cap
	Rear cap
	Lens case', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
