Made with Marco in Mind. Making this a truly all-in-one lens, the Sigma 16-300mm f/3.5-6.7 DC OS Contemporary is equipped with a max magnification ratio of 1:2 at 70mm, 1:3 at the wide end, and 1:4 at the tele end. So not only is this a great choice for landscapes, events, and travel but also for closeup portraits and fine details.

Try it with These L-Mount Cameras. The Sigma 16-300mm f/3.5-6.7 DC OS Contemporary is a crop-view lens, meaning it is designed to be paired with cameras using APS-C or Super 35 sensors. To use this with existing full-frame L-mount cameras, make sure it is in “crop mode” to compensate for the 1.5x crop factor. The Sigma BF offers a crop mode to accommodate this lens, as does the Panasonic S5 II.', 1400000.0, '{"Angle of View": "83.2-5.4°", "Brand": "Sigma", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "L", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Standard, Telephoto, and Supertelephoto"}', 'Includes

	Sigma 16-300mm f/3.5-6.7 DC OS Contemporary for L-Mount
	Front & rear caps
	Sigma LH706-03 hood
	67mm Hoya EVO antistatic filter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1527, 2, 51, 'Sigma 16-300mm f/3.5-6.7 DC OS Contemporary for Sony E', 'sigma-16-300mm-f-3-5-6-7-dc-os-contemporary-for-sony-e', 'The Sigma 16-300mm f/3.5-6.7 DC OS Contemporary for Sony E is an APC-C format zoom lens that is compatible with crop sensor Sony E mount cameras. Key features include:

1:2 (half life size) macro ratio at 70mm
Fast AF with High-Response Linear Actuator
Powerful 6-stop stabilization with OS2 algorithm
18.8x zoom ratio, 24-450mm equivalent in 35mm terms

Powerful and Portable. This extremely versatile zoom offers a massive 18.8x zoom ratio, which is among the world’s largest for a mirrorless-compatible APS-C lens. In 35mm terms, this is equivalent to a 24-450mm lens, making it a perfect all-in-one that is suitable for nearly any subject.

AI-Enhanced Features. Sigma has engineered an Intelligent OS2 algorithm that features a drive unit with a specially-designed actuator and high-precision sensor to meet the shooting demands of action subjects. It is equipped with an exceptional 6-stop optical stabilization system (4.5 at the tele end), helping photographers capture blur-free images at longer focal lengths in lower light.

Made with Marco in Mind. Making this a truly all-in-one lens, the Sigma 16-300mm f/3.5-6.7 DC OS Contemporary is equipped with a max magnification ratio of 1:2 at 70mm, 1:3 at the wide end, and 1:4 at the tele end. So not only is this a great choice for landscapes, events, and travel but also for closeup portraits and fine details.

Try it with These Sony Cameras. The Sigma 16-300mm f/3.5-6.7 DC OS Contemporary is compatible with any crop sensor E-mount mirrorless camera. Its portable design is especially well suited for the feature-rich, vlog-friendly Sony a6700 or the exceptionally portable ZV-E10 II.', 1400000.0, '{"Angle of View": "83.2-5.4°", "Aperture Blades": "9, rounded", "Brand": "Sigma", "Dimensions": "2.9 × 4.9\\" (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "67.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "16-300", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "14/20", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "APS-C", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Standard, Telephoto, Supertelephoto, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "3.5", "Maximum Magnification": "0.5x", "Mfr. Model Number": "887965", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "6.7-41.3\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "1.35 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

