Strong, Yet Svelte. The Sigma 24-70mm Mark II is dust- and moisture-sealed, so that you can use it in adverse conditions without worry. Its internal structure includes metal parts for zoom extension, and there’s a brass bayonet mount for maximum durability. At 4.8 inches long and 1.6 lb., it’s noticeably smaller and lighter than its predecessor while still including the same number of lens elements.', 1850000.0, '{"Angle of View": "84.1-34.3°", "Aperture Blades": "11, rounded", "Brand": "Sigma", "Dimensions": "3.5 × 4.8″  (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "82.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "24-70", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "15/19", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Standard, Telephoto, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "2.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.37x", "Mfr. Model Number": "57A965", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "6.7\\"", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "1.6 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

