Fast f/1.4 Aperture Normal Range Prime. The Sigma 50mm f/1.4 DG HSM Art’s combination of normal focal range and fast aperture makes this lens ideal for portraiture where subject-background isolation is needed. This also makes it a perfect choice for shooting in low light. Being a standard 50mm focal length, the Sigma 50mm f/1.4 DG HSM Art is useful for just about any type of photography. Using a APS-C sensor camera? You’ll have a focal length equivalent to 75mm.

High-Quality Optics. As a part of Sigma’s Art lens line, this lens goes through Sigma’s rigorous A1 testing to ensure high image quality. It features a molded glass aspherical element to eliminate sagittal coma flare, vignetting, and color blur throughout the aperture range. Three Super Low-Dispersion glass elements correct for axial chromatic aberration while the Super Multi-Layer Coating minimizes ghosting and lens flare. All this is incorporated into a floating optical design that provides high-detail rendering and a 1.3-foot minimum focusing distance.

Hyper Sonic Motor Autofocus System. Provides fast, smooth, and quiet operation in a wide variety of shooting situations. You can also manually override the autofocus motor at any time by rotating the focusing ring, giving you quick fine-tuning ability.', 1050000.0, '{"Angle of View": "46.8°", "Aperture Blades": "9, rounded", "Brand": "Sigma", "Dimensions": "3.36 × 3.9″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "77.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "50-50", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "8/13", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Standard and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "1.4", "Maximum Magnification": "0.18x", "Mfr. Model Number": "311965", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "1.31’", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "1.79 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Includes

