INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1842, 1, 54, 'Sony Cyber-Shot RX1R II', 'sony-cyber-shot-rx1r-ii', 'The Sony RX1R II is a compact point-and-shoot camera that features a 35mm full-frame sensor. It has been upgraded by the long-awaited RX1R III. Key features of this older version include:

42.4MP CMOS sensor
Improved autofocus system
Variable optical low-pass filter
Sharp, high-contrast images with excellent color rendition

What’s New. Say you were to take the 42.4MP full-frame sensor and advanced autofocus system from the Sony Alpha a7R II and put it in the Sony Cyber-Shot RX1R with a large retractable EVF and variable optical low pass filter. That’s what’s new. The RX1R was good, but the Sony Cyber-shot RX1R II is just plain better.

42.4MP CMOS Sensor. The DSC-RX1R II uses a full-frame 42.4-megapixel Exmor R CMOS sensor in conjunction with the BIONZ X image processor to offer high-resolution stills and video while minimizing noise and improving speed.

Variable Optical Low-Pass Filter. In order to maximize detail from the 42.4-megapixel sensor, Sony has implemented the world’s first variable optical low-pass filter. This filter allows users to control the amount of antialiasing needed for each specific image as they work via a variable density liquid crystal filter layer. Users will have access to three settings: Off, Standard, and Hi. This first-of-its-kind feature set allows the RX1R II to work in a variety of circumstances that normally would require separate cameras.

Zeiss 35mm f/2 Lens. The RX1R II produces sharp images with great contrast and color rendition thanks to its fixed Zeiss Sonnar 35mm f/2 lens. The f/2 aperture enables decent speed for low-light shooting, and great background blur for controlling depth of field. The seven-group/eight-element optical construction uses three aspherical elements—including one advanced aspherical element—that minimize aberrations and distortion. This lens also offers a dedicated macro mode that shortens the minimum focus distance from 11.8 inches to just 7.9 inches.

Other Notable Features. While the physical layout and manual controls are largely the same as its predecessor’s, the RX1R II adds a retractable 2.4M-dot XGA OLED electronic viewfinder for rangefinder-esque shooting. You can use the built-in Wi-Fi feature for wireless image transfer and remote camera triggering, and you can capture Full HD 1080p video in XAVC S format. The camera records JPEG and RAW images (14-bit compressed/uncompressed) to SDHC/XC memory cards, while the same underwhelming NP-BX1 battery offers a paltry 220 shots per charge. If you can’t tell, we’re not big fans of this battery.', 5500000.0, '{"Angle of View": "62 degrees", "Aperture": "f/2-22", "Brand": "Sony", "Camera Type": "Compact", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Filter Size": "49mm", "Filter Style": "Unknown", "Focusing System": "Internal focusing, nonrotating, manual w/focus peaking", "Groups/Elements": "7/8", "Item Type": "Camera", "Low Dispersion Elements": "0", "Maximum Magnification": "Unknown", "Maximum Video Resolution": "1080p", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "11.81\\" (7.87\\" in macro mode)", "Screen Type": "Tilt", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "Weather Resistant": "No", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi"}', 'Includes

	Sony Cyber-Shot RX1R II
	Front cap & strap
	49mm protection filter
	NP-BX1 battery
	BC-TRX charger', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1843, 1, 54, 'Sony Cyber-shot RX1R III', 'sony-cyber-shot-rx1r-iii', 'The Sony RX1R III is the long-awaited followup to the esteemed Sony RX1R II. Its exceptional 61MP full frame sensor in a point-and-shoot body makes it an instant favorite for travel. Key features include:

Top-quality 35mm f/2 Zeiss lens
Updated AF tracking with advanced AI
12 creative look presets and 3 film styles
4K30p video in 4:2:2 10-bit with S-Cinetone

Fixed-Lens Fun, Premium Performance. The Sony RX1R II was a crowd favorite for street photography and this new iteration keeps all the best features of its predecessor while taking advantage of the latest tech. You still get a high-megapixel, portrait-worthy sensor and Zeiss 35mm lens but you also now have access to AI processing for an improved autofocus experience, including a new Human Pose Estimator that predicts movements with stunning accuracy.

Character and Operability. Sony made a few refinements to the overall build of the RX1R III. The top panel’s dials and hot shoe are perfectly flush for easier pocketing and a newly-developed, no-slip texture has been strategically added to the grip. The whole thing has a cool black matte coating and the EVF no longer pops up but is fixed, which is a bit more traditional. The LCD is also fixed to improve overall pocketability but now has touch operation. Both EVF and LCD adapt automatically to vertical shooting. The EVF is the same one found on the a7CR.

Imaging Improvements. This camera is equipped with the exact same lens as the prior model. This was a well-loved lens originally and Sony must have figured it was best to not mess with perfection. Top among its benefits is its leaf shutter design. Built into the lens itself, the shutter for this camera is not only super quiet but also super fast – fast enough to accommodate flash sync up to 1/4,000th of a second (1/2,000th when shooting at f/2). For comparison, most cameras max out sync at 1/250th of a second. This is especially beneficial for strobe shooters looking for studio-level results even in bright ambient conditions. Feel constricted by a prime lens? You have the option of using digital zoom to simulate 50mm or 70mm fields of view.

Creativity to Carry Everywhere. With smartphones, we’ve grown accustomed to adding filters as we go and the RX1R III is set up for a similar workflow. This compact is packed with fast presets for both photo and video, including three cinematic-style looks that soften results for a nostalgic vibe. While not particularly robust in the video specs, you can still expect UHD 4K recording for, seemingly, an unlimited amount of time (though it is recommended to stay under 50 minutes to prevent any overheating). The Multi-Function shoe is handy for shotgun mics and there is a decent set of ports for a camera of this form factor: 3.5mm mic jack, USB-C (with PD support), and micro-HDMI. With vintage flair, the shutter button on this camera is equipped with a threaded socket for shutter release cables. Overall, the RX1R III is a really great option for not only everyday shooting but also for beautiful portraits and photojournalism-style captures.', 6900000.0, '{"Brand": "Sony", "Camera Type": "Compact", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Fixed", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Stabilization": "No", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

	Sony Cyber-shot RX1R III
	Sony metal 49mm front cap
	Sony RX1R III eyecup
	Sony RX1R III strap
	49mm Hoya EVO antistatic filter
	Sony NP-FW50 battery
	Sony BC-TRW charger', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1844, 2, 54, 'Sony E 10-18mm f/4 OSS', 'sony-e-10-18mm-f-4-oss', 'The Sony E 10-18mm f/4 OSS is an excellent ultra-wide angle zoom lens made for Sony E-mount cameras and camcorders. Key features include:

Great for expansive landscape photography
Four-stop Optical SteadyShot image stabilization
9.84-inch minimum focusing distance
Seven-blade circular aperture

Wide-Angle Zoom. The Sony E 10-18mm f/4 OSS’s 35mm-equivalent focal length of 15-27mm makes it great for expansive landscape photography.

Excellent in Low Light. The constant f/4 aperture and built-in Optical SteadyShot image stabilization (up to four stops) make it useful for low-light shooting without fluctuating ISO and shutter speed settings, and the internal focusing design allows the lens to remain the same size when adjusting focus.

Advanced Optical Design. Optically, the lens includes three aspherical elements that help to provide high-contrast images with very little spherical aberration and distortion. A super extra-low dispersion glass element also helps to keep chromatic aberrations at bay.

Close Focusing. This lens offers a minimum focus distance of 9.84 inches for exaggerating perspective, and its 7-blade circular aperture creates very pleasing out-of-focus highlights. A petal-type lens hood is included to help prevent lens flare.', 1275000.0, '{"Angle of View": "109-76°", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Brand": "Sony", "Dimensions": "2.8 × 2.5″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "67.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "10-18", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "10/13", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "APS-C", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "4.0", "Maximum Magnification": "0.25x", "Mfr. Model Number": "SEL1018", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "4.6\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "0.56 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Sony E 10-18mm f/4 OSS
	Front & rear caps
	Hood
	62mm protective filter
	Lens pouch', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1845, 2, 54, 'Sony E 10-20mm f/4 PZ G', 'sony-e-10-20mm-f-4-pz-g', 'The Sony E 10-20mm f/4 PZ G is a lightweight, versatile, ultra-wide APS-C Power Zoom that’s optimized for content creators and vloggers. Key features include:

Optimized for content creators and vloggers
Advanced G-Series optical design
Power Zoom mechanism with intuitive control
Fast, silent autofocus performance

Versatile Ultra-Wide Zoom. The Sony E 10-20mm f/4 PZ G’s versatile, 15-30mm equivalent focal-length range is wide enough for handheld selfie-style vlogging and content creation but narrow enough to make a great everyday lens. The constant f/4 aperture isn’t quite fast enough for low-light shooting, but it’s better than a variable-aperture zoom and helps to keep this lens compact and lightweight.

G-Series Optical Design. The 10-20mm’s eight-group/eleven-element design includes three aspherical elements, two Extra-Low Dispersion elements, and one Extra-Low Dispersion aspherical element, which combine to produce clear, high-contrast images while minimizing chromatic aberrations and distortion throughout the zoom range. The lens’s rounded seven-blade diaphragm gives images smooth out-of-focus areas when you desire a shallow depth of field.

Power Zoom. This lens boasts an integrated Power Zoom lever on its barrel and a dedicated zoom ring that lets you make simple focal-length adjustments. When paired with select Sony cameras, you can also use Power Zoom via on-camera controls. With select Alpha cameras, you can adjust the zoom ring’s rotation direction. You can also remotely control the zoom from a linked smartphone or by using the Sony GP-VPT2BT Wireless Shooting Grip, which is available as a separate rental item.

Focusing Performance. A Linear Motor autofocus system uses two separate motors for fast, precise, and nearly silent focus and tracking performance, making it ideal for video and stills alike. You can use the AF/MF switch on the barrel to quickly switch between focus modes, while the internal focusing design keeps the lens length consistent while upping responsiveness. If you’re using manual focus, the minimum focusing distance is 5.1 inches at the 10mm position and 6.7 inches with a 0.18x maximum magnification at the 20mm position. If you’re using autofocus, minimum focusing distance is 7.9 inches with a 0.14x maximum magnification. No matter what, you’ll be able to get pretty close to your subject.

Compact, High-Quality Build. The 10-20mm boasts a lightweight, compact build that’s weather-sealed so that you can use it in inclement conditions without worry.', 1525000.0, '{"Angle of View": "109-70°", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Brand": "Sony", "Dimensions": "2.7 × 2.2″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "62.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "10-20", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Front Lens Diameter": "62mm", "Groups/Elements": "8/11", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "APS-C", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "4.0", "Maximum Magnification": "0.18x", "Mfr. Model Number": "SELP1020G", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "5.1\\"", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "0.39 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Sony 10-20mm f/4
	Front & rear caps
	ALC-SH169 hood
	62mm protective filter', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1846, 2, 54, 'Sony E 11mm f/1.8', 'sony-e-11mm-f-1-8', 'The Sony E 11mm f/1.8 is a lightweight, versatile, ultra-wide APS-C prime for Sony E-mount cameras. Key features include:

Versatile ultra-wide prime
Advanced optical design
Fast, silent autofocus performance
Compact, lightweight, weather-sealed build

Versatile Ultra-Wide Prime. The Sony E 11mm f/1.8’s versatile, 16.5mm equivalent focal length makes it great for handheld selfie-style vlogging, content creation, architecture photography, and landscape photography. The fast f/1.8 aperture is great for low-light shooting and subject-background isolation.

Advanced Optical Design. The 11mm’s eleven-group/twelve-element design includes three aspherical elements and three Extra-Low Dispersion elements, which combine to produce clear, high-contrast images while minimizing chromatic aberrations and distortion. The lens’s rounded seven-blade diaphragm gives images smooth out-of-focus areas when you desire a shallow depth of field.

Focusing Performance. A Linear Motor autofocus system uses two separate motors for fast, precise, and nearly silent focus and tracking performance, making it ideal for video and stills alike. You can use the AF/MF switch on the barrel to quickly switch between focus modes, while the internal focusing design keeps the lens length consistent while upping responsiveness. If you’re using manual focus, the minimum focusing distance is 4.7 inches with a 0.2x maximum magnification. If you’re using autofocus, minimum focusing distance is 5.9 inches with a 0.13x maximum magnification. No matter what, you’ll be able to get pretty close to your subject.

Compact, High-Quality Build. The 11mm boasts a lightweight, compact build that’s weather-sealed so that you can use it in inclement conditions without worry.', 1175000.0, '{"Angle of View": "104°", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Brand": "Sony", "Dimensions": "2.6 × 2.3″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "55.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "11-11", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Format": "APS-C", "Groups/Elements": "11/12", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "APS-C", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "1.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.2x", "Mfr. Model Number": "SEL11F18", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "4.7\\"", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "0.4 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Sony E 11mm f/1.8
	Front & rear caps
	Hood
	55mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1847, 2, 54, 'Sony E 15mm f/1.4 G', 'sony-e-15mm-f-1-4-g', 'The Sony E 15mm f/1.4 G is a fast, versatile, wide-angle APS-C prime for Sony E-mount cameras. Key features include:

Versatile wide-angle prime
Advanced optical design
Fast, silent autofocus performance
Compact, lightweight, weather-sealed build

Versatile Wide-Angle Prime. The Sony E 15mm f/1.4 G’s versatile, 22.5mm equivalent focal length makes it great for handheld selfie-style vlogging; content creation; and street, landscape, and travel photography. The ultra-fast f/1.4 aperture is great for low-light shooting and subject-background isolation.

Advanced Optical Design. The 15mm’s twelve-group/thirteen-element design includes three aspherical elements, two Extra-Low Dispersion elements, and one Super Extra-Low Dispersion element, which combine to produce clear, high-contrast images while minimizing chromatic aberrations and distortion. The lens’s rounded seven-blade diaphragm gives images smooth out-of-focus areas when you desire a shallow depth of field.

Focusing Performance. A Linear Motor autofocus system uses two separate motors for fast, precise, and nearly silent focus and tracking performance, making it ideal for video and stills alike. You can use the AF/MF switch on the barrel to quickly switch between focus modes, while the internal focusing design keeps the lens length consistent while upping responsiveness. If you’re using manual focus, the minimum focusing distance is 6.7 inches with a 0.15x maximum magnification. If you’re using autofocus, minimum focusing distance is 7.9 inches with a 0.12x maximum magnification. No matter what, you’ll be able to get pretty close to your subject. Smooth Motion Optics suppress focus breathing to maintain accuracy, and this lens is compatible with select Alpha cameras’ Breathing Compensation functions.

Compact, High-Quality Build. The 15mm boasts a lightweight, compact build that’s weather-sealed so that you can use it in inclement conditions without worry.', 1500000.0, '{"Angle of View": "87°", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Brand": "Sony", "Dimensions": "2.6 × 2.7″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "55.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "15-15", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "12/13", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "APS-C", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "1.4", "Maximum Magnification": "0.15x", "Mfr. Model Number": "SEL15F14G", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "6.7\\"", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "0.48 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Sony E 15mm f/1.4 G
	Front & rear caps
	Hood
	55mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1848, 2, 54, 'Sony E 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 OSS II PZ (Black)', 'sony-e-16-50mm-f-3-5-5-6-oss-ii-pz-black', 'The Sony E 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 OSS II PZ (Black) is a versatile standard-length power zoom that’s great for day-to-day use. Key features include:

Versatile standard-length power zoom
Optical SteadyShot image stabilization
Fast, silent autofocus, even while zooming
Compact, lightweight, travel-friendly build

Standard-Length Zoom Range. The Sony E 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 OSS II PZ (Black) gives users a single-lens option that covers a 24mm to 75mm full-frame equivalent focal length. Its combination of versatile zoom range and variable aperture makes it ideal for most everyday still and video use cases.

Optical SteadyShot Image Stabilization. The in-lens stabilizer corrects for camera shake to minimize blur and maximize stability in your shots. This image-stabilization system works in tandem with compatible cameras’ in-body stabilization systems, and the lens transmits gyro information to the camera for even greater coordination.

Power Zoom. The integrated power-zoom is quiet and responsive, so it’s particularly well-suited to movie shooting. You can control it with the zoom lever or the zoom and focus ring, depending on which option best suits your needs. Either way, you’ll get smooth, in-focus zooms at consistent speeds.

Updated Autofocus System. The 16-50mm’s revised autofocus system is based around an advanced linear motor that provides smooth, precise, and silent performance. It can accurately track subjects even when you’re shooting continuous stills at 120 fps or capturing high frame-rate video. You also get direct manual focusing via the zoom and focus ring, and a 9.8-inch minimum focusing distance that lets you get clear close-ups.

Optical Design. This lens’ eight-group/nine-element optical formula includes four aspherical elements and one Extra-Low Dispersion element to keep clarity and resolution high while minimizing distortion, color bleeding, and chromatic aberrations.

Lightweight, Compact Build. The 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 weighs just 3.8 oz. and retracts to just 1.25 inches when you power off the camera, but it’s plenty compact even when you’re actively using it.', 650000.0, '{"Angle of View": "83-32°", "Aperture Blades": "7", "Brand": "Sony", "Dimensions": "2.6 × 1.2″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "40.5mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "16-50", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "8/9", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "APS-C", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Standard, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "3.5", "Maximum Magnification": "0.22x", "Mfr. Model Number": "SELP16502", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "0.82’", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "0.23 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Sony E 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 OSS II PZ (Black)
	Front & rear caps
	40.5mm Hoya EVO antistatic filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1849, 2, 54, 'Sony E 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 PZ OSS', 'sony-e-16-50mm-f-3-5-5-6-pz-oss', 'The Sony E 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 PZ OSS is a compact standard zoom lens made for Sony E-mount cameras and camcorders. We also carry the next-gen Sony E 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 OSS II PZ. Key features include:

Four-stop Optical SteadyShot image stabilization
Electronically activated power zoom
Manual focus ring
Compact build

The Sony E 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 PZ OSS is a compact standard zoom lens made for Sony E-mount cameras and camcorders. It features a retractable power zoom that’s electronically activated when the camera is powered on. This allows the lens to come in at a mere 1.18" when not in use. The 35mm-equivalent focal length of 24-75mm makes it a great everyday walk-around lens, and Sony’s built-in Optical SteadyShot image stabilization unit provides up to four stops of correction for camera shake.

The 16-50mm PZ uses one ED element and four aspherical elements to minimize optical aberrations and provide high-contrast images with little field curvature. You can adjust the power zoom function via a zoom rocker switch on the side of the lens, but you can also use the dual-function control ring for both zooming and manual focus. When set to autofocus, the control ring functions as a power zoom ring, allowing a more hands-on approach than the rocker switch. When set to manual focus, the control ring provides accurate manual focus adjustment. This method works in both still and video shooting, making the 16-50mm PZ a great choice for any and all users.', 575000.0, '{"Angle of View": "83-32º", "Aperture Blades": "7, rounded", "Brand": "Sony", "Dimensions": "2.55 × 1.18″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "40.5mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "16-50", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "8/9", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "APS-C", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle, Standard, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "3.5", "Maximum Magnification": "0.21x", "Mfr. Model Number": "SELP1650", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "9.84\\"", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "0.25 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

	Sony E 16-50mm f/3.5-5.6 PZ OSS
	Front & rear caps
	40.5mm protective filter
	Lens bag', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1850, 2, 54, 'Sony E 16-55mm f/2.8 G', 'sony-e-16-55mm-f-2-8-g', 'The Sony E 16-55mm f/2.8 G is a professional-grade wide-to-portrait length zoom for crop-frame Sony E-mount cameras. Key features include:

Professional-grade wide-to-portrait length zoom
Fast, nearly silent autofocus; full-time manual focusing
Advanced optical design for high-quality images
Crop-frame Sony E-mount lens

Crop-Frame E-Mount. The Sony E 16-55mm f/2.8 G is designed for crop-frame Sony E-mount cameras, on which it provides a 24-82.5mm equivalent focal length.

Pro-Grade Wide-to-Portrait Zoom. The E 16-55mm f/2.8 G is a telephoto zoom that’s great for portraiture, wedding/event photography, and all-around general use. Its bright f/2.8 constant aperture lets you shoot in a range of lighting conditions while giving you excellent depth-of-field control. The rounded nine-blade diaphragm helps create smooth bokeh when you’re using selective-focus techniques.

XD Linear Motor Autofocus System. This system provides fast, nearly silent, and highly accurate autofocus performance that’s great for still and video use. A dedicated focus hold button and AF/MF switch help to tailor focusing to your shooting needs.

Advanced Optics. The E 16-55mm f/2.8 G’s twelve-group/seventeen-element design includes four aspherical elements and three extra-low dispersion elements to minimize chromatic aberrations, and to produce clear, high-contrast images. Nikon has applied Nano Crystal and Super Integrated coatings to the elements to combat ghosting and lens flare, even when you’re working in bright or backlit conditions.', 2475000.0, '{"Angle of View": "83-29º", "Aperture Blades": "9, rounded", "Brand": "Sony", "Dimensions": "2.87 × 3.94″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "67.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "16-55", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "12/17", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "APS-C", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Ultra Wide Angle, Wide Angle, Standard, and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "2.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.2x", "Mfr. Model Number": "SEL1655G", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "1.08’", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Weight": "1.09 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Variable Focal Length"}', 'Includes

