Five-Axis In-Body Image Stabilization. The FX30’s built-in image-stabilization feature helps keep things smooth even when you’re shooting hand-held or in low light. Its Active Mode smooths out your footage even more by combining optical systems and digital optimization. This camera can record gyro movement when optical image stabilization is turned off so that you can stabilize your footage in post.

Dual CFexpress Type A Support. The Sony FX30 uses CFexpress Type A media for the highest bitrate recording and offers a variety of recording options for file spanning and redundancy. The CFexpress slots double as UHS-II SDXC slots for less demanding frame rates and bitrates.

Monitor and Control. As of November 2023, you can use Sony’s Monitor & Control app for Android and iOS to turn your smartphone into a wireless video monitor. It lets you use your phone to remotely control the camera, display and control clips from the camera, start and stop recording, adjust white balance, change ISO, adjust color settings, and swap between LUTs.

Additional Features. Whether controlling the camera via a smartphone or tablet or wirelessly transferring files to editorial, the FX30 is prepared to handle all of your wireless needs with built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth. This camera is powered by the NP-FZ100 battery, which will give you up to 115 minutes of actual video recording, approximately 175 minutes of continuous video recording, and roughly 570 still shots on a single charge. You can also power the camera via USB provided that there’s a battery installed.', 4150000.0, '{"Brand": "Sony", "Camera Mount": "Sony E", "Camera Type": "Cinema", "Compatible Media": "CFexpress Type A and SD", "Environmental": "Operating Temperature32 to 104°F / 0 to 40°CStorage Temperature-4 to 140°F / -20 to 60°C", "Exposure Control": "Shutter TypeElectronic Rolling ShutterShutter Speed1/8000 to 30 Seconds in Photo Mode1/8000 to 1/4 Second in Video ModeISO Sensitivity100 to 32,000 (Extended: 50 to 102,400)Advertised Dynamic Range14 StopsWhite Balance2500 to 9900KWhite-Balance PresetsAuto, Cloudy, Color Temperature, Daylight, Fluorescent, Incandescent, Shade, Underwater", "Focusing": "Focus TypeAuto and Manual FocusFocus ModeAutomatic, Continuous-Servo AF, Direct Manual Focus, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AF, Touch AF & ShutterAutofocus Points (Video)Phase Detection: 495Autofocus Sensitivity-3 to +20 EV", "General": "Battery TypeSony Z-SeriesTripod Mounting Thread1x 1/4\\"-20 Female (Bottom)Accessory Mount1x Intelligent Hot Shoe on Camera Body5x 1/4\\"-20 Female on Camera Body3 × 1/4\\"-20 Female on Included HandleMaterialMagnesium AlloyDimensions (W x H x D)5.1 × 3.1 × 3.3″ / 129.7 × 77.8 × 84.5mmWeight1.2 lbs. / 562 g (Body Only)", "Imaging": "Lens CommunicationYes, with Autofocus SupportSensor ResolutionActual: 27 MegapixelEffective: 26 Megapixel (6192 × 4128)Sensor Type23.3 × 15.5 mm (APS-C) CMOSImage StabilizationSensor-Shift, 5-AxisBuilt-In ND FilterNoneInternal Filter HolderNoCapture TypeStills & Video", "Interface": "Media/Memory