INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1967, 1, 54, 'Sony ZV-E1 Mirrorless Camera', 'sony-zv-e1-mirrorless-camera', 'The Sony ZV-E1 Mirrorless Camera is an advanced, ultra-compact photo and cinema camera with features optimized for content creators, vloggers, and influencers. Key features include:

Designed for content creators, vloggers, and influencers
UHD 4K 120p / Full HD 240p 10-bit 4:2:2 video capture
CineVlog video mode for instantly cinematic footage
Fast hybrid autofocus system; 5-axis image stabilization

Designed for Content Creators and Vloggers. The Sony ZV-E1 Mirrorless Camera includes a range of features aimed squarely at content creators and influencers. Its Cinematic Vlog setting, rear LCD with side flip-out design, built-in front-facing three-capsule mic, external-mic and headphone jacks, Face Priority Auto-Exposure, Soft Skin effect, Background Defocus feature, Product Showcase setting, Active SteadyShot image-stabilization system, large REC button, and compact, lightweight design all make it a particularly vlogger-friendly camera.

12.1MP Full-Frame Exmor Sensor and BIONZ XR Image Processor. The redesigned 12.1MP full-frame Exmor RS BSI CMOS sensor features a back-illuminated Exmor R design for greater clarity and improved noise reduction. It gives you an impressive 80-102400 ISO range for stills and movies that can be extended to ISO 40-409600 for stills and ISO 80-409600 for movies. When this sensor is coupled with the revised BIONZ XR image processor, you get up to 8x faster processing, faster overall camera speed, and markedly reduced rolling shutter. On top of that, this sensor-processor combination gives you up to fifteen-plus stops of dynamic range for stills and video, and 10 fps continuous shooting for up to 1000 uncompressed RAW stills.

UHD 4K 120p Video. This camera captures UHD 4K video at up to 120 fps and Full HD at up to 240 fps using full pixel readout with no line skipping or pixel binning, and all recording modes offer internal 10-bit 4:2:2 sampling. The ZV-E1’s lack of recording-time limits on video clips and its heat-dissipating construction make it the perfect choice for long-form recording, and it supports the All-Intra and XAVC S-I intraframe codecs that give you consistent performance and quality at bit rates up to 600 Mb/s.

CineVlog Video Mode. CineVlog mode, which you can activate with a single press of an onscreen button, instantly gives you a more cinematic look by putting the camera into the low-contrast S-Cinetone color profile, shooting at 23.98p, and giving you a 2.35:1 cinematic widescreen crop, although the footage is still output at 16:9 UHD. CineVlog mode also gives you the option to apply Moods—which adjust color response, and Looks—which adjust tonal response and contrast, in any combination to give your videos the exact vibe you want.

Additional Vlogging-Specific Video Features. The ZV-E1 includes a few automated video modes meant to simplify the creation of high-quality, production-ready video for people creating content on their own. The My Image Style feature gives you onscreen camera-settings buttons labeled in non-technical, layperson’s terms, making it easy to get your image just right. The Product Showcase mode overrides face-detection autofocus and gives temporary focus priority to items held in front of the camera. The ZV-E1 supports instant time-lapse settings with fully customizable frame rates, recording, light, and interval parameters. You get exceptional image quality when using Slow & Quick Motion mode to directly replay movies while using the XAVC S-I format at 60p. When you’re using the XAVC S format, you can replay movies at up to 10x slow motion in Full HD resolution at 240 fps.

Connectivity and Streaming. You can use the Sony Creators’ App, which replaces the Imaging Edge App, to connect to the Creators’ Cloud platform which lets you share and store media, edit, and collaborate, all in the cloud. The ZV-E1 can use USB output using UVC/UAC control via a computer for streaming and broadcasts, with the USB output supporting up to 4K30 video. The camera itself is also capable of livestreaming by using its webcam function in tandem with a computer. The ZV-E1 can output up to 4K30 video to a computer via USB-C, and it supports UVC/UAC control-protocol standards.

Fast Hybrid Autofocus System. This camera’s Fast Hybrid autofocus system uses 759 phase-detection points for photo and 627 phase-detection points for video to give you fast, accurate focusing in a broad range of lighting conditions with sensitivity down to 6 EV. You can use autofocus in all recording modes, and it greatly benefits video and still-shooting applications. It locks onto subjects quickly and has an AI-based Real-Time Tracking feature for moving subjects, but you can also use touch tracking instead. The Real-Time Eye AF feature is designed for maximum sharpness when shooting portraits, and it works on humans and animals alike. You have control over how quickly and smoothly focus shifts from subject to subject for even greater fine tuning.

Autofocus Tracking Features. The ZV-E1’s autofocus system features a range of AI-based tracking features, many of which are new. Its Real-Time Recognition AF feature works with seven selectable subject types. Its Human mode tracks people by their body and head positions for maximum sharpness when shooting portraits, and the Real-Time Eye AF feature’s performance has been improved by 60%. Its Animal, Bird, and Animal/Bird modes are 40% more accurate for recognizing a variety of animal types—including insects—and pinpointing and tracking their heads and eyes. This system also has dedicated Car/Train and Airplane modes, which can detect and track those subjects with utmost accuracy, even at high speeds.

Five-Axis In-Body Image Stabilization. The built-in image-stabilization system helps keep things smooth even when you’re shooting hand-held or in low light. Its Optical Active mode increases stabilization when you’re shooting while walking, and the Dynamic Active mode adds electronic stabilization that’s ideal for quick camera moves and longer focal lengths. The Framing Stabilization option adjusts the sensor crop in Dynamic Active mode to keep the subject centered in the frame while stabilizing your footage.

Side Flip-Out LCD and Audio Options. A rear 3.0-inch, 1.07m-dot touchscreen LCD features a side flip-out design that’s great for filming yourself and taking selfies with ease. The camera’s top plate incorporates a directional three-capsule mic built for forward-directional audio recording, and there’s a 3.5mm mic port, a headphone jack, and a Multi-Interface Shoe to accommodate external mics and accessories.

Versatile Control Options. This camera offers control options optimized for content creators. There’s a giant Record button for ease of use when vlogging, and a dedicated function button that can be programmed to offer quick adjustments of several different functions, allowing users to forego menu diving. If you prefer touchscreen controls, the ZV-E1 has you covered. Swiping the left or right edge of the touchscreen lets you access shooting mode, Cinematic Vlog mode, and more, while swiping up on the touchscreen pulls up the function menu.

Power and Memory. The ZV-E1 is powered by the NP-FZ100 rechargeable lithium-ion battery, which is rated for roughly 570 stills or 120 minutes of video recording per charge. It records images and video to a single UHS-II SDHC/XC memory card. Please note that 4K video capture in S-Log3 requires a UHS-I Class 3 or faster memory card.', 3625000.0, '{"Brand": "Sony", "Camera Mount": "Sony E", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Environmental": "Operating Temperature32 to 104°F / 0 to 40°C", "Exposure Control": "Shutter TypeElectronic Shutter, Mechanical Focal Plane ShutterShutter Speed1/8000 to 30 Second1/8000 to 1 Second in Movie ModeISO Sensitivity – Photo80 to 102,400 (Extended: 80 to 409,600)Metering MethodCenter-Weighted Average, Highlight Weighted, Multiple, SpotMetering Range3 to 20 EV", "Flash": "Built-In FlashNoneExternal Flash ConnectionIntelligent Hot Shoe", "Focusing": "Focus TypeAuto and Manual FocusFocus ModesAutomatic, Direct Manual Focus, Manual FocusAutofocus Points – PhotoPhase Detection: 759Autofocus Points – VideoPhase Detection: 627Autofocus Sensitivity6 to +20 EV", "General": "Battery Type1x NP-FZ100 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion (Approx. 570 Shots)Power Consumption≤7 WTripod Mounting Thread1x 1/4\\"-20 FemaleAccessory Mount1x Intelligent Hot ShoeDimensions (W x H x D) – camera only4.8 × 2.8 × 2.1″ / 121 × 71.9 × 54.3mmWeight – camera body only0.9 lb. / 399 gWeight – with battery and recording media1.1 lb. / 483 g", "Imaging": "Sensor ResolutionEffective: 12.9 Megapixel (4240 × 2832)Image Sensor35.6 × 23.8mm (Full-Frame) CMOSImage StabilizationDigital, 5-AxisBuilt-In ND FilterNoneCapture TypeStills & Video", "Interface": "Media/Memory Card SlotSingle Slot: SD/SDHC/SDXC (UHS-II)Video I/ONoneAudio I/O1x 1/8\\" / 3.5mm TRS Stereo Microphone Input1x 1/8\\" / 3.5mm TRS Stereo Headphone OutputPower I/O1x USB-C InputOther I/O1x USB-C (USB 3.2 / 3.1 Gen 1) Data Input/Output (Shared with Power Input)1x Sony Multi/Micro-USB ControlWirelessWi-Fi, BluetoothMobile App CompatibleYes\\n\\n*As of March, 2023: Check with manufacturer for the most up-to-date compatibilityGlobal Positioning (GPS, GLONASS, etc.)None", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Mfr. Model Number": "ILCZV-E1/B", "Monitor": "Size3.0\\"Resolution1,036,800 DotDisplay TypeArticulating Touchscreen LCD", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Sensor Size": "Full-Frame", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Still Image Capture": "Image Sizes\\n3:212 MP (4240 × 2832)5.1 MP (2768 × 1848)3 MP (2128 × 1416)Image File FormatsHEIF, JPEG, RAWBit Depth10-Bit", "Video Capture": "Internal Recording Modes – RawXAVC HS 4:2:0 10-BitUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 50/59.94 fps [45 to 150 Mb/s]UHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.98 fps [30 to 100 Mb/s] Internal Recording Modes – RawXAVC HS 4:2:2 10-Bit3840 × 2160 at 50/59.94 fps [100 to 200 Mb/s]840 × 2160 at 23.98 fps [50 to 100 Mb/s] Internal Recording Modes – RawXAVC S 4:2:2 8-BitUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 50/59.94 fps [100 to 200 Mb/s]UHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 25/29.97 fps [140 Mb/s]UHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 23.98 fps [100 Mb/s]Internal Recording Modes – RawXAVC S 8-Bit1920 × 1080p at 100/120 fps [60 to 100 Mb/s]1920 × 1080p at 50/59.94 fps [25 to 50 Mb/s]1920 × 1080p at 25/29.97 fps [16 to 50 Mb/s]1920 × 1080p at 23.98 fps [50 Mb/s]Internal Recording Modes – RawXAVC S 10-Bit1920 × 1080p at 23.98/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps [50 Mb/s]Internal Recording Modes – RawXAVC S-I 10-Bit3840 × 2160 at 59.94 fps [600 Mb/s]3840 × 2160 at 50 fps [500 Mb/s]3840 × 2160 at 29.97 fps [300 Mb/s]3840 × 2160 at 25 fps [250 Mb/s]3840 × 2160 at 23.98 fps [50 Mb/s]1920 × 1080p at 59.94 fps [222 Mb/s]1920 × 1080p at 50 fps [185 Mb/s]1920 × 1080p at 29.97 fps [111 Mb/s]1920 × 1080p at 25 fps [93 Mb/s]1920 × 1080p at 23.98 fps [89 Mb/s]External Recording ModesNoneFast-/Slow-Motion SupportYesRecording LimitNoneBroadcast OutputNTSC/PALIP StreamingNoneBuilt-In Microphone TypeStereo", "Weather Sealing": "Yes", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

	Sony ZV-E1
	Sony NP-FZ100 battery
	Sony 1-Port USB Type-A charger
	USB 2.0 A Male to Type-C cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1968, 1, 54, 'Sony ZV-E10 II Mirrorless Camera (Black)', 'sony-zv-e10-ii-mirrorless-camera-black', 'The Sony ZV-E10 II Mirrorless Camera (Black) is a compact, video-focused mirrorless camera with an expanded feature set optimized for content creators, vloggers, and influencers. It’s an update to the original Sony ZV-E10. Key features include:

Designed for content creators, vloggers, and influencers
Internal 4K 60p video with S-Cinetone, S-Log3, and more
759-point autofocus system with updated algorithm
Right-hand grip and 3.0-inch side flip-out touchscreen LCD

What’s Changed? The Sony ZV-E10 II Mirrorless Camera (Black) is a serious update to the previous-gen ZV-E10. It uses the markedly faster 26MP BSI CMOS sensor from the a6700 and FX-30 to capture 4K60p 10-bit video and to otherwise improve its performance. There are updated autofocus algorithms, a focus-breathing compensation feature, and the Cinematic Vlog mode first seen in the ZV-1 II. This camera uses the higher-capacity NP-FZ100 battery, which affords you much longer shooting times.

Designed for Content Creators and Influencers. Like its predecessor, the ZV-E10 II was designed for content creators. Its rear LCD with side flip-out design, built-in front-facing three-capsule mic, Face Priority Auto-Exposure, Soft Skin effect, Background Defocus feature, Product Showcase setting, Active Mode electronic image-stabilization system, oversized REC button, comfortable right-hand grip, 3.5mm mic and headphone ports, and compact, lightweight design all make it a particularly vlogger-friendly camera.

Side Flip-Out LCD and Audio Options. A rear 3.0-inch, 1.04m-dot touchscreen LCD features a side flip-out design that’s great for filming yourself and taking selfies with ease. A built-in tally lamp puts a red border around the LCD while you’re filming, and the LCD will change its orientation from landscape to portrait if you’re filming vertically. The camera’s top plate incorporates a directional three-capsule mic built for forward-directional audio recording, and there’s a Multi-Interface Shoe to accommodate external mics and accessories. A 3.5mm mic input and a 3.5mm headphone port give you everything you need to record and monitor audio on the fly.

26MP APS-C CMOS Sensor and BIONZ XR Processor. The ZV-E10 II revolves around a 26MP APS-C Exmor CMOS image sensor and a BIONZ XR image processor working in tandem to create images with reduced noise at high sensitivities. The ISO range covers a base level from 100-32,000, but it’s expandable to ISO 102,400 for even better performance in low light. This sensor and processor combination lets you shoot bursts at up to 11 fps until you fill up the 1000 JPEG/59 RAW compressed buffer.

UHD 4K 60p Capture. The ZV-E10 Mark II borrows its video functionality from higher-end Sony cameras, and can internally record 10-bit UHD 4K 60p, 30p, and 24p video. All of the 4K footage is taken from oversampled capture—6K for frame rates up to 30p, and 5.6K with a 1.1x crop for 50p and 60p frame rates—all of which uses full pixel readout without any binning. When not shooting 4K, you can record Full HD video anywhere between 1-120 frames per second for expressive slow and fast motion. Both 4K and Full HD resolutions use 600 Mb/s XAVC HS and XAVC S-I formats with 4:2:2 sampling. You also get S-Cinetone and S-Log3 gammas, which give you an effective 14-stop dynamic range with increased grading control in the image’s shadow to mid-tone regions. For more demanding shoots, ZV-10 II has a Micro-HDMI output for uncompressed 4K 4:2:2 video to an external recorder, and a 5 Gbps USB Type-C data output port lets you use the Mark II as a 4K 30p webcam, livestream to social-media platforms, and transfer data to supported devices via the Sony Creators app.

Cinematic Vlog Mode. Cinematic Vlog mode, which you can activate with a single press of an onscreen button, instantly gives you a more cinematic look by giving you a 2.35:1 cinematic widescreen crop and 24 fps frame rate, although the footage is still output at 16:9 UHD. Cinematic Vlog mode also gives you the option to apply Moods—which adjust color response, and Looks—which adjust tonal response and contrast, in any combination to give your videos the exact vibe you want.

Improved Phase-Detection Autofocus. This autofocus system’s fast, hybrid 759-point phase-detection and subject-recognition algorithms have been updated for improved performance. The ZV-E10 II boasts Real-Time Eye AF technology, which uses AI-based object recognition to detect and process eye data in real time so that focus on the subject’s eye will be as sharp as possible. When you’re working with recognized Sony lenses, a focus-breathing compensation function will crop into the narrowest effective field of view and make adjustments to the crop and scaling to keep framing consistent even as the focusing distance changes.

Advanced Controls. This camera offers control options optimized for content creators. There’s a giant Record button for ease of use when vlogging, and a dedicated function button that can be programmed to offer quick adjustments of several different functions, allowing users to forego menu diving. You also get dedicated Movie Record, Background Defocus, Product Showcase, and S&Q buttons that give you immediate access to popular vlogging features. The large, comfortable right-hand grip was designed with one-handed use in mind, a built-in zoom lever surrounds the shutter button and works with select Power Zoom lenses.

Built-In Bluetooth and Wi-Fi. Integrated Bluetooth and Wi-Fi let you instantly transfer images to your mobile device so that you can easily share them on social media, in email, and to the cloud. Once you’ve connected the camera to Bluetooth or Wi-Fi, it can display a live-view image on its screen. You can use the Sony Creators app to connect to a smartphone using a QR code. The Creators app app lets you create time-lapse movies, edit your footage, and more.

User Flexibility. The ZV-E10 II records images/video to SDHC/XC memory cards (not included) and is powered by the popular NP-FZ100 rechargeable lithium-ion battery, which is rated for roughly 610 shots per charge. Please note that 4K video capture in S-Log2 and S-Log3 requires a UHS-1 Class 3 or faster memory card.', 1900000.0, '{"Brand": "Sony", "Camera Mount": "Sony E", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Exposure Control": "Shutter TypeElectronic Rolling ShutterShutter Speed – Electronic Shutter1/8000 to 30 Seconds1/8000 to 1 Second in Movie ModeISO Sensitivity Range – Photo100 to 32,000 in Manual Mode (Extended: 50 to 102,400)100 to 6400 in Auto ModeISO Sensitivity Range – Video100 to 32,000 in Manual Mode100 to 6400 in Auto ModeMetering MethodsAverage, Center-Weighted Average, Highlight Weighted, Multi, SpotExposure ModesAperture Priority, Auto, Manual, Program, Shutter PriorityExposure Compensation-5 to +5 EV (1/3, 1/2 EV Steps)Metering Range-3 to 20 EVWhite Balance2500 to 9900KWhite-Balance PresetsATW, AWB, Auto, Color Temperature, Color Temperature Filter, Custom, Daylight, Flash, Fluorescent (Cool White), Fluorescent (Day White), Fluorescent (Daylight), Fluorescent (Warm White), Incandescent, Shade, UnderwaterContinuous ShootingUp to 11 fps for up to 59 Frames (RAW) / 1000 Frames (JPEG)Interval RecordingYesSelf-Timer2/5/10-Second Delay", "Flash": "Built-In Flash/LightNoFlash ModesAuto, Fill Flash, Off, Rear Sync, Slow SyncMaximum Sync Speed1/30 SecondFlash Compensation-3 to +3 EV (1/3, 1/2 EV Steps)Dedicated Flash SystemTTLExternal Flash ConnectionShoe Mount", "Focus": "Focus TypeAuto and Manual FocusFocus ModesAutomatic, Continuous-Servo AF, Direct Manual Focus, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AFAutofocus Points – PhotoPhase Detection: 759Autofocus Points – VideoPhase Detection: 495Autofocus Sensitivity-3 to +20 EV", "General": "Battery Type1x NP-FZ100 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion (Approx. 610 Shots)Shoe Mount1x Intelligent Hot ShoeTripod Mounting Thread1x 1/4\\"-20 Female (Bottom)Operating Conditions32 to 104°F / 0 to 40°C Dimensions (W x H x D)4.5 × 2.7 × 2.1″ / 114.8 × 67.5 × 54.2mmWeight10.3 oz / 292 g (Body Only)13.3 oz / 377 g (With Battery, Recording Media)", "Imaging": "Sensor ResolutionActual: 27 MegapixelEffective: 26 MegapixelImage Sensor23.3 × 15.5mm (APS-C) CMOSSensor Crop (35mm Equivalent)Crop Factor: 1.5x\\n*Additional Crop Occurs in Select Video ModesImage StabilizationDigital (Video Only)Built-In ND FilterNoCapture TypeStills & Video", "Interface": "Media/Memory Card SlotSingle Slot: SD (Unspecified Type) (UHS-II)Video I/O1x Micro-HDMI (Unspecified Signal) OutputAudio I/O1x 1/8\\" / 3.5mm TRS Stereo Headphone Output on Camera Body1x 1/8\\" / 3.5mm TRS Stereo Microphone InputPower I/O1x USB-C InputOther I/O1x USB-C (USB 3.2 / 3.1 Gen 1) Data Output (Shared with Power Input)Wireless2.4 / 5 GHz Wi-Fi 5 (802.11ac), Bluetooth 4.2Mobile App CompatibleYes: Android & iOSApp Name: Creators’ AppFunctionality: Access Stored Files, Adjust Settings, Remote Control", "Item Type": "Camera", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Mfr. Model Number": "ZVE10M2B", "Monitor": "Display Size3.0\\"Resolution1,036,800 DotDisplay TypeArticulating Touchscreen LCD", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Sensor Size": "APS-C", "Stabilization": "Yes", "Still Image Capture": "Image Sizes – 3:226 MP (6192 × 4128)13 MP (4384 × 2920)6.4 MP (3104 × 2064)Aspect Ratio3:2Image File FormatHEIF, JPEG, RAWBit Depth14-Bit", "Video Capture": "Internal Recording Modes – H.265/XAVC HS 4:2:2/4:2:0 10-Bit3840 × 2160 at 23.98/50/59.94 fps [50 to 200 Mb/s]Internal Recording Modes – H.264/MPEG-4 AVC/XAVC S 4:2:2/4:2:0 8/10-Bit3840 × 2160 at 23.98/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps [100 to 200 Mb/s]1920 × 1080 at 23.98/25/29.97/50/59.94/100/120 fps [50 to 100 Mb/s]Internal Recording Modes – Internal Recording Modes – XAVC S-I 4:2:2 10-Bit3840 × 2160 at 23.98/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps [240 to 600 Mb/s]1920 × 1080 at 23.98/25/29.97/50/59.94 fps [89 to 222 Mb/s]External Recording Modes – HDMI3840 × 2160p1920 × 1080pFast-/Slow-Motion SupportYesGamma CurveS Cinetone, Sony S-Log3Recording LimitNoIP Streaming – RTMP, RTMPS, SRT3840 × 2160 at 25p, 30pBuilt-In MicrophoneStereo (Microphone Location: Top)Audio Recording2-Channel 16-Bit 48 kHz LPCM Audio2-Channel 24-Bit 48 kHz LPCM Audio", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

	Sony ZV-E10 II Mirrorless Camera (Black)
	Sony NP-FZ100 battery
	Sony ALC-B1EM body cap
	Shoulder strap
	Thunderbolt 4 USB 3-foot cable', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (1969, 1, 54, 'Sony ZV-E10 Mirrorless Camera', 'sony-zv-e10-mirrorless-camera', 'The Sony ZV-E10 Mirrorless Camera is compact, video-focused, and optimized for content creators, vloggers, and influencers. It’s the predecessor to the more feature-rich Sony ZV-E10 II. Key features include:

Designed for content creators, vloggers, and influencers
Internal 4K video capture with HLG and S-Log3 gammas
24.2MP APS-C CMOS sensor; 425-point hybrid autofocus
Right-hand grip and 3.0-inch side flip-out touchscreen LCD

Designed for Content Creators and Influencers. The Sony ZV-E10 Mirrorless Camera is an update to the ZV-1, which itself was designed for content creators. Its rear LCD with side flip-out design, built-in front-facing three-capsule mic, Face Priority Auto-Exposure, Soft Skin effect, Background Defocus feature, Product Showcase setting, Active SteadyShot image-stabilization system, oversized REC button, comfortable right-hand grip, and compact, lightweight design all make it a particularly vlogger-friendly camera.

24.2MP APS-C CMOS Sensor. The ZV-E10 revolves around a 24.2MP APS-C Exmor CMOS image sensor and a BIONZ X image processor working in tandem to create images with reduced noise at high sensitivities. The ISO range covers a base level from 100-32,000, but is expandable to ISO 51,200 for shooting in low-light scenarios. Snap at a rate up to 11 fps burst before you fill up the 77 JPEG/33 RAW compressed buffer.

Side Flip-Out LCD and Audio Options. A rear 3.0-inch, 921.6k-dot touchscreen LCD features a side flip-out design that’s great for filming yourself and taking selfies with ease. The camera’s top plate incorporates a directional three-capsule mic built for forward-directional audio recording, and there’s a 3.5mm mic port and a Multi-Interface Shoe to accommodate external mics and accessories.

UHD 4K Capture. The ZV-E10 borrows its video functionality from the higher-end a6100. This camera records 4K internally to an SD card at 100 Mbps using the XAVC-S codec. To create the 4K image, the sensor provides a full pixel readout, without any pixel binning, resulting in a near-6K image that’s oversampled to create the final image. And if you don’t want to record internally, you can always output an uncompressed HDMI signal at 4K with 4:2:2 sampling. When not shooting 4K, you can record Full HD video anywhere between 1-120 frames per second to go slow motion or fast paced.

Fast Hybrid Autofocus. This autofocus system’s 425 hybrid phase- and contrast-detection autofocus points densely cover 84% of the sensor area for ridiculously precise focusing at a speed of 0.02 seconds. The ZV-E10 boasts Real-Time Eye AF technology, which uses AI-based object recognition to detect and process eye data in real time so that focus on the subject’s eye will be as sharp as possible. You also get High-Density Tracking AF, which tracks moving subjects with ease in a variety of lighting conditions; Lock-On AF, which holds focus on movie subjects via a configurable frame over the subject; and Expand Flexible Spot, which uses neighboring focus points to maintain focus on even if the selected point loses focus.

Advanced Controls. This camera offers control options optimized for content creators. There’s a giant Record button for ease of use when vlogging, and a dedicated function button that can be programmed to offer quick adjustments of several different functions, allowing users to forego menu diving. You also get dedicated Movie Record, Background Defocus, Product Showcase, and S&Q buttons that give you immediate access to popular vlogging features. The large, comfortable right-hand grip was designed with one-handed use in mind, a built-in zoom lever surrounds the shutter button and works with select Power Zoom lenses.

Built-In Bluetooth and Wi-Fi. Integrated Bluetooth and Wi-Fi let you instantly transfer images to your mobile device so that you can easily share them on social media, in email, and to the cloud. Once you’ve connected the camera to Bluetooth or Wi-Fi, it can display a live-view image on its screen. You can use Sony’s Imaging Edge mobile app to connect to a smartphone using a QR code. The Imaging Edge app lets you create time-lapse movies, edit your footage, and more.

User Flexibility. The ZV-E10 records images/video to SDHC/XC memory cards (not included) and is powered by the popular NP-FW50 rechargeable lithium battery, which is rated for roughly 440 shots per charge. Please note that 4K video capture in S-Log2 and S-Log3 requires a UHS-1 Class 3 or faster memory card.

Newer Version Available. Please note that we offer this camera’s more feature-rich successor, the Sony ZV-E10 II Mirrorless Camera.', 1700000.0, '{"Aspect Ratio": "1:1, 3:2, 4:3, 16:9", "Audio File Formats": "Linear PCM (Stereo)", "Audio Recording": "Built-In Microphone (Stereo)\\nExternal Microphone Input (Stereo)", "Autofocus Points": "Phase Detection: 425\\nContrast Detection: 425", "Autofocus Sensitivity": "-3 to +20 EV", "Battery": "1x NP-FW50 Rechargeable Lithium-Ion, 7.2 VDC, 1080 mAh (Approx. 440 Shots)", "Brand": "Sony", "Built-in Flash": "No", "Camera Mount": "Sony E", "Camera Type": "Mirrorless", "Compatible Media": "SD", "Continuous Shooting": "Up to 11 fps at 24.2 MP for up to 116 Frames (JPEG) / 46 Frames (RAW)", "Crop Factor": "1.5x", "Dedicated Flash System": "TTL", "Depth": "1.8\\"", "Exposure Compensation": "-5 to +5 EV (1/3, 1/2 EV Steps)", "Exposure Modes": "Aperture Priority, Auto, Manual, Program, Shutter Priority", "External Flash Connection": "Hot Shoe", "External Video-Recording Modes": "4:2:2 8-Bit\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) up to 29.97p", "Flash Compensation": "-3 to +3 EV (1/3 EV Steps)", "Flash Modes": "Auto, Fill Flash, Off, Rear Sync, Slow Sync", "Focus Modes": "Automatic, Continuous-Servo AF, Direct Manual Focus, Manual Focus, Single-Servo AF", "Focus Type": "Auto and Manual Focus", "GPS": "No", "Height": "2.5\\"", "Image File Formats": "JPEG, RAW", "Inputs/Outputs": "3.5mm Microphone\\n3.5mm Headphone\\nUSB Type-C (USB 3.1)\\nHDMI D (Micro)", "Interval Recording": "Yes", "Item Type": "Camera", "Live Streaming": "Yes", "Maximum Sync Speed": "1/160 Second", "Maximum Video Resolution": "4K", "Memory Card Slot": "Single Slot: SD/SDHC/SDXC/Memory Stick Duo Hybrid (UHS-I)", "Metering Range": "-2 to 20 EV", "Mfr. Model Number": "ILCZV-E10/B", "Monitor Resolution": "921,600 Dot", "Monitor Size": "3.0\\"", "Monitor Type": "Articulating Touchscreen LCD", "Operating Temperature": "32 to 104°F", "Screen Type": "Touchscreen and Swivel", "Self Timer": "2/5/10-Second Delay", "Sensor Resolution": "Actual: 25 Megapixel\\nEffective: 24.2 Megapixel (6000 × 4000)", "Sensor Size": "APS-C", "Sensor Type": "23.5 × 15.6mm (APS-C) CMOS", "Shutter Speed": "Mechanical Shutter\\n1/4000 to 30 Second\\nBulb Mode\\n1/4000 to 1/4 Second in Movie Mode", "Stabilization": "Digital (Video Only)", "Video Encoding": "NTSC/PAL", "Video Recording Limit": "Unlimited for UHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 29.97p", "Video Recording Modes": "XAVC S 4:2:0 8-Bit\\nUHD 4K (3840 × 2160) at 24.00p/25p/29.97p [60 to 100 Mb/s]\\nFull HD (1920 × 1080) at 23.976p/25p/29.97p/50p/59.94p/100p/119.88p [16 to 100 Mb/s]", "Viewfinder Type": "Electronic", "Webcam Functionality": "Yes", "White Balance": "Auto, Cloudy, Color Temperature Filter, Custom, Daylight, Flash, Fluorescent (Cool White), Fluorescent (Day White), Fluorescent (Daylight), Fluorescent (Warm White), Incandescent, Shade, Underwater", "Width": "4.5\\"", "Wireless": "Wi-Fi\\nBluetooth", "Wireless Connectivity": "Wi-Fi and Bluetooth"}', 'Includes

