Electronic Interface. The Tokina 85mm’s lens mount includes an electronic interface that transfers all EXIF data to the camera. It also means you can use in-camera functions like image stabilization, manual-focus assist, and eye autofocus.', 675000.0, '{"Angle of View": "28.5º", "Aperture Blades": "9", "Brand": "Tokina", "Dimensions": "3.15 × 3.67″ (ø x L)", "Filter Size": "72.0mm", "Filter Type": "Screw-On", "Focal Length": "85-85", "Focus Type": "Autofocus", "Groups/Elements": "7/10", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Format": "Full-Frame", "Lens Mount": "Sony E", "Lens Type": "Telephoto and For Mirrorless", "Maximum Aperture": "1.8", "Maximum Magnification": "0.13x", "Mfr. Model Number": "ATX-M-AF85FE", "Minimum Focusing Distance": "2.62’", "Stabilization": "No", "Weather Sealing": "No", "Weight": "1.42 lb.", "Zoom Type": "Fixed Focal Length"}', 'Includes

