INSERT INTO products (id, category_id, brand_id, name, slug, description, base_price, specifications, accessories_included, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (2319, 1, 65, 'Z CAM E2-F6 Full-Frame 6K Cinema Camera (Leica M)', 'z-cam-e2-f6-full-frame-6k-cinema-camera-leica-m', 'The Z CAM E2-F6 Full-Frame 6K Cinema Camera (Leica M) is an ultra-compact full-frame camera capable of ZRAW & HEVC recording. It builds on the ergonomics and features of the previous Z CAM E2 Camera. Key features include:

37.09 × 24.75 mm, full-frame, CMOS sensor with 15-stop dynamic range
Records in 12-bit ZRAW at DCI 4K & 10-bit H.265 at up to 6244 × 4168p to CFast 2.0 media
Leica M mount for compatibility with most M-mount lenses
Powered by common Sony L-series (NP-F) batteries

12-bit ZRAW & 10-bit H.265 Recording. The Z CAM E2-F6 Full-Frame 6K Cinema Camera (Leica M) can capture up to 12-bit ZRAW at DCI 4K and 10-bit H.265 or 8-bit H.264 at up to 6244 × 4168/30p to CFast 2.0 media. The sensor is full-frame and capable of 15-stops of dynamic range. This Z Cam cannot record to external media via its USB Type C connector. Want a Super 35 version of this camera? Check out the Z CAM E2-F6 Super 35 6K Cinema Camera.

RAW Out Over HDMI. In addition to the codec-rich internal recording options, the Z Cam E2 F6 can also output 12-bit ProRes RAW over HDMI when paired with a compatible recorder like the Atomos Ninja V when running the latest ATOMOS firmware.

Metal Cube With A Sensor. Z Cam seems to have found their niche with entry-level cameras that are not much bigger than the lenses that will attach to them. This is still the case with the Z Cam E2-F6. The all metal housing makes sure the tightly packed electronics can still dissipate heat while shooting.

