1.8-foot minimum focusing distance
Ten-blade curved aperture

Excellent Image Quality. Despite its wide 90° angle of view, this lens offers very low distortion and excellent image quality across the frame. Its 1.8-ft. minimum focusing distance allows you to take exaggerated perspective shots, and its ten-blade curved aperture makes for smooth out-of-focus highlights. Its flare control and lack of geometric distortion provides useful accuracy for architectural, landscape, and product photography.

High-Quality Build. An all-metal lens housing gives the ZM 21mm f/2.8 Biogon a premium feel. Its manual focus ring offers precision focus adjustment and excellent speed.', 1400000.0, '{"Angle of View": "90 degrees", "Brand": "Zeiss", "Dimensions": "Length: 2.9\\"", "Groups/Elements": "7/9", "Hood Included": "No", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Leica M", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle", "Maximum Magnification": "0.047x", "Mfr. Model Number": "1365-651"}', 'Includes

