Ten-blade curved aperture

Solid Image Quality. This lens offers solid image quality and great color warmth across the frame. Its ten-blade curved aperture makes for smooth out-of-focus highlights. Its flare resistance and lack of geometric distortion provide useful accuracy for photojournalism and street photography. It produces a bit more distortion than some lenses, so it may not be quite as good for architectural work. This focal length isn’t particularly suited to that work, anyway.

High-Quality Build. An all-metal lens housing gives the ZM 35mm f/2 Biogon a premium feel. Its manual focus ring offers precision focus adjustment and excellent speed.', 1425000.0, '{"Angle of View": "63 degrees", "Brand": "Zeiss", "Dimensions": "Length: 2.65\\"", "Groups/Elements": "6/9", "Hood Included": "No", "Item Type": "Lens", "Lens Mount": "Leica M", "Lens Type": "Wide Angle", "Maximum Magnification": "0.055x", "Mfr. Model Number": "1365-659"}', 'Includes

